        "4052": {"comment":"Page 2 address"},
        "4056": {"synopsis":"Finishes EXOS 27: restores page 0 and the caller's alternate registers, clears BC+1 bytes\ndown from just above the new IX, and returns the new IX (the descriptor's base, 16 bytes\nbelow the pointer): it replaces the IX the kernel saved before the call (the second word on\nthe stack), so the kernel's exit loads it.","comment":"Caller's page 0"},
        "4059": {"comment":"Page 0 back"},
        "4063": {"comment":"Caller's alternate set back"},
        "4068": {"comment":"Return address into the kernel"},
        "4069": {"comment":"Drop the saved IX"},
