        "4079": {"comment":"Clear the rest"},
        "4081": {"comment":"Back into the kernel"},
        "4082": {"synopsis":"Steps IY down EXOS's segment list for an address that has gone below a segment's start.\nEntry: HL = address, DE = amount to subtract (0: step at once), IY = list position.\nExit: A = the high byte of the address within its segment; IY moved one place for each 16K\nadded.","comment":"Nothing to subtract?"},
        "4087": {"comment":"Subtract it"},
