        "4091": {"synopsis":"Steps one place down the list and adds 16K to the high byte until it carries.","comment":"One segment further down the list"},
        "4093": {"comment":"Add 16K"},
        "4095": {"comment":"Until back in range"},
        "4098": {"synopsis":"Before EXOS takes more RAM (EXOS 27 at $0D92, and $0A8B): when there is no shared segment\nand free segments remain, and the next free segment is a video segment ($FC-$FF) numbered\nabove one of EXOS's own segments, swaps them: the video segment takes that place in EXOS's\nsegment list (from $ABD0 down; $BF9A points at EXOS's lowest), the old segment's 16K is\ncopied into it and every link in the channel list that named the old segment is changed.\nRepeats, then sets $BF8A (FIND_VID_SEG). The swap was not run in the profile.","comment":"L = shared segment, H = free segments"},
        "4101": {"comment":"Shared segment in use?"},
        "4105": {"comment":"No free segments?"},
        "4108": {"synopsis":"Compares the next free segment with EXOS's segments, top down.","comment":"Next free segment's entry, below EXOS's"},
        "4112": {"comment":"Scan EXOS's list from the top"},
        "4115": {"synopsis":"Steps down EXOS's segment list while its entries are higher than the free one."},
        "4116": {"comment":"EXOS's segment"},
        "4117": {"comment":"Reached the free entry itself?"},
        "4120": {"comment":"EXOS's is higher: keep looking"},
        "4122": {"comment":"Keep EXOS's segment"},
        "4123": {"comment":"The free segment"},
        "4124": {"comment":"A video segment?"},
        "4126": {"comment":"No: nothing to swap"},
        "4128": {"comment":"It takes the place in EXOS's list"},
        "4129": {"comment":"Page 1 = the video segment"},
        "4131": {"comment":"A = the old segment"},
