        "4504": {"synopsis":"VIDEO, read block (entry +12): reads BC characters into the caller's buffer at DE with\nVIDEO's read character (VID_READ_CHAR) through BLOCK_READ. Its second instruction hides\nKEYBOARD's\nread block (entry +12) at $119C: LD HL,KBD_READ_CHAR (KEYBOARD's read character,\nKBD_READ_CHAR). On this\npath IY is loaded with KBD_READ_CHAR by that instruction's bytes.","comment":"VIDEO's read character"},
        "4507": {"comment":"Byte $119C is LD HL,KBD_READ_CHAR: KEYBOARD's read block"},
        "4511": {"synopsis":"Reads a block one character at a time: calls the read-character routine at HL BC times and\nstores each character (B) in the caller's buffer at DE, paging the buffer into page 1\n(MAP_CALLER_DE) and paging it again each time DE crosses into the next page. Shared by VIDEO\nand\nKEYBOARD (through VID_READ_BLOCK/$119C) and EDITOR ($32F8).\nEntry: HL = read-character routine, BC = count, DE = caller's buffer address, the channel's\nsegment in page 1.\nExit: A = status (the first error stops it), BC = bytes not read, DE = the buffer address\nafter the last byte.","comment":"Channel RAM's segment"},
        "4513": {"comment":"Keep it in A'"},
        "4514": {"comment":"Buffer address on the stack"},
        "4515": {"synopsis":"Pages the buffer (its caller address on the stack) into page 1.","comment":"Buffer address"},
        "4517": {"comment":"Page the buffer into page 1"},
        "4520": {"comment":"Anything to read?"},
        "4522": {"synopsis":"Reads one character with the channel RAM paged and stores it in the buffer.","comment":"Buffer's segment"},
        "4524": {"comment":"A = channel's segment"},
        "4525": {"comment":"Page 1 = channel RAM"},
        "4528": {"comment":"Keep the buffer's segment"},
        "4532": {"comment":"Keep the channel's segment"},
        "4538": {"comment":"Read a character"},
        "4545": {"comment":"Status to A'"},
        "4546": {"comment":"Channel's segment"},
        "4547": {"comment":"Page 1 = channel RAM"},
        "4549": {"comment":"Character (B) to the other set"},
        "4553": {"comment":"Buffer's segment"},
        "4554": {"comment":"A = status"},
        "4555": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "4556": {"comment":"Yes: stop"},
        "4558": {"comment":"Channel's segment"},
        "4561": {"comment":"Page 1 = buffer"},
        "4563": {"comment":"Character from the other set"},
        "4566": {"comment":"Into the buffer"},
        "4568": {"comment":"Advance the caller's buffer address"},
        "4571": {"comment":"One less to read"},
        "4572": {"comment":"Still inside page 1?"},
        "4574": {"comment":"No: page the next part of the buffer"},
        "4576": {"synopsis":"Loops while bytes are left.","comment":"Bytes left?"},
        "4578": {"comment":"Yes: next character"},
        "4580": {"synopsis":"Returns the advanced buffer address in DE.","comment":"DE = the caller's address after the last byte"},
        "4582": {"synopsis":"VIDEO, write block (entry +16): writes BC characters from the caller's buffer at DE with\nVIDEO's write character (VID_WRITE_CHAR) through BLOCK_WRITE. Its second instruction hides\nSOUND's\nwrite block (entry +16) at $11EA: LD HL,SND_WRITE_CHAR (SOUND's write character,\nSND_WRITE_CHAR). On this path\nIY is loaded with SND_WRITE_CHAR by that instruction's bytes.","comment":"VIDEO's write character"},
        "4585": {"comment":"Byte $11EA is LD HL,SND_WRITE_CHAR: SOUND's write block"},
        "4589": {"synopsis":"Writes a block one character at a time: reads each byte from the caller's buffer at DE into\nB and calls the write-character routine at HL, BC times, paging the buffer into page 1\n(MAP_CALLER_DE) and paging it again each time DE crosses into the next page. Shared by VIDEO\nand\nSOUND (through VID_WRITE_BLOCK/$11EA) and EDITOR ($32D2).\nEntry: HL = write-character routine, BC = count, DE = caller's buffer address, the channel's\nsegment in page 1.\nExit: A = status (the first error stops it), BC = bytes not written, DE = the buffer address\nafter the last byte written.","comment":"Buffer address on the stack"},
        "4590": {"synopsis":"Pages the buffer (its caller address on the stack) into page 1, keeping its segment in A'.","comment":"Channel RAM's segment"},
        "4592": {"comment":"Keep it in A'"},
        "4593": {"comment":"Buffer address"},
        "4595": {"comment":"Page the buffer into page 1"},
        "4598": {"comment":"Buffer's segment"},
        "4601": {"comment":"A = channel's segment"},
        "4602": {"comment":"Page 1 = channel RAM"},
        "4605": {"comment":"A' = buffer's segment"},
        "4606": {"comment":"Anything to write?"},
        "4608": {"synopsis":"Takes one byte from the buffer and writes it with the channel RAM paged."},
