        "4651": {"comment":"One less to write"},
        "4652": {"comment":"Advance the caller's buffer address"},
        "4655": {"comment":"Next byte"},
        "4656": {"comment":"Still inside page 1?"},
        "4658": {"comment":"No: page the next part of the buffer"},
        "4660": {"synopsis":"Loops while bytes are left.","comment":"Bytes left?"},
        "4662": {"comment":"Yes: next character"},
        "4664": {"synopsis":"Returns the advanced buffer address in DE.","comment":"DE = the caller's address after the last byte"},
        "4666": {"synopsis":"Makes a caller's address reachable through page 1: pages in the segment that was in the\naddress's page at the EXOS call (USR_P0-USR_P3, $BFFC-$BFFF, chosen by the top two bits of\nD) and turns DE into the same byte's page-1 address ($4000-$7FFF). Used wherever EXOS reads\nthe caller's strings and buffers.\nEntry: DE = caller's address.\nExit: DE = page-1 address, page 1 = that segment.\nChanges: A."},
        "4667": {"comment":"Top two bits of the address"},
        "4670": {"comment":"= its page number"},
        "4672": {"comment":"USR_P0 to USR_P3"},
        "4677": {"comment":"The caller's segment for that page"},
        "4678": {"comment":"Page it into page 1"},
        "4680": {"comment":"Address within page 1"},
        "4686": {"synopsis":"Adds BC to the word at HL+2 and leaves HL on it, so that repeated calls walk a list of\nwords; with Z set on entry the result is kept in page 1 (bit 15 cleared, bit 14 set). Used\nby the devices' buffer-moved entries to move their pointers (VIDEO $165C, SOUND $287E,\nEDITOR $30AF).\nEntry: HL = 2 bytes before the word, BC = distance, Z = a page-1 pointer.\nExit: HL = the word's address.\nChanges: DE."},
        "4688": {"comment":"Read the word"},
        "4692": {"comment":"Add the distance (flags of the entry kept)"},
        "4693": {"comment":"Not a page-1 pointer"},
        "4695": {"comment":"Keep it in page 1"},
        "4699": {"synopsis":"Stores the moved word.","comment":"Store it back"},
        "4704": {"synopsis":"VIDEO, initialise (entry +24; also called by the reset at $007B):\n1. Fills the status line, 40 bytes at $BEB8, with spaces.\n2. Sets LP_POINTER to $B900 and builds the line parameter table there: 28 copies of the\n   16-byte block at VID_LPB_BLANK, then 6 blocks whose first 4 bytes come from the table at\n   VID_LPB_TAIL\n   (the other 12 bytes are left as they are).\n3. Clears the 28 bytes at $BBA1.\n4. Gives NICK the table's address (ports 82h/83h, $90 and $xF: video address $F900, the\n   system segment's $B900).\n5. Stores $36 at $B909 (byte 9 of the first block) and sets ST_POINTER to $BEB8.\n6. If the table's first byte was zero before step 2, falls into VID_FONT_RESET; otherwise\n   returns.","comment":"Status line text"},
        "4707": {"comment":"40 characters"},
        "4709": {"synopsis":"Fills the status line with spaces.","comment":"Space"},
        "4714": {"comment":"Line parameter table"},
        "4717": {"comment":"LP_POINTER"},
        "4721": {"comment":"Template block"},
        "4724": {"comment":"Table's first byte before"},
        "4726": {"comment":"28 blocks"},
        "4728": {"synopsis":"Copies the 16-byte template block once per pass."},
        "4729": {"comment":"16 bytes each"},
        "4737": {"comment":"First 4 bytes of the last 6 blocks"},
        "4742": {"synopsis":"Copies 4 bytes into each of the last 6 blocks."},
        "4744": {"comment":"Copy 4 bytes"},
        "4746": {"comment":"Skip the other 12"},
        "4754": {"comment":"Clear the 28 bytes at $BBA1"},
        "4759": {"synopsis":"Clears the bytes at $BBA1.","comment":"A = 0 here"},
        "4763": {"comment":"Low byte of $F900 / 16"},
        "4765": {"comment":"LPT address low"},
        "4768": {"comment":"Was the first byte non-zero?"},
        "4770": {"comment":"High nibble $F"},
        "4772": {"comment":"Yes: only the final write"},
        "4774": {"comment":"LPT address high, bits 6 and 7 low"},
        "4776": {"comment":"Bit 6 high"},
        "4780": {"synopsis":"Sets the LPT address's control bits (port 83h bits 6 and 7) and finishes.","comment":"Bits 6 and 7 high"},
        "4784": {"comment":"Value for byte 9 of the first block"},
        "4789": {"comment":"Status line"},
        "4792": {"comment":"ST_POINTER"},
        "4796": {"comment":"Table was there: keep the font"},
        "4797": {"synopsis":"Rebuilds VIDEO's character set (also @@FONT through $1594): decodes 128 characters of 9 rows\nfrom the bit stream that starts at VID_FONT_BITS (HL+1; it ends at $2847) into the font at\n$B480\n(row n of character c at $B480 + c + n*$80). Each character starts with a 4-bit header in D:\nbit 2 = the two top rows are drawn (else blank), then five rows, then bit 1 = the two bottom\nrows are drawn; rows are coded as FONT_ROW says. Finally sets character $1F from the 9 bytes\nat\nVID_BLOCK_CHAR (VID_ESC_K with IX = $D312).","comment":"Bit stream, from the next byte"},
        "4800": {"comment":"Empty bit buffer"},
        "4803": {"comment":"First character, rows $80 apart"},
        "4808": {"synopsis":"Decodes one character.","comment":"Font address of the character"},
        "4813": {"comment":"Read the 4-bit header"},
        "4818": {"comment":"D = header"},
        "4819": {"comment":"Top rows drawn?"},
        "4821": {"comment":"Two top rows"},
        "4824": {"comment":"Five middle rows"},
        "4826": {"synopsis":"Decodes the five middle rows.","comment":"One row"},
        "4832": {"comment":"Bottom rows drawn?"},
        "4834": {"comment":"Two bottom rows"},
        "4838": {"comment":"Next character"},
        "4839": {"comment":"Until 128 are done"},
        "4841": {"comment":"IX-$20 = the block pattern at VID_BLOCK_CHAR"},
        "4845": {"comment":"Character $1F"},
        "4847": {"comment":"Copy the pattern into the font"},
        "4850": {"synopsis":"Character $1F's pattern: 9 rows of $FF, a solid block. Read through IX-$20 by VID_ESC_K_LOOP\n(VID_FONT_RESET passes IX = $D312)."},
        "4859": {"synopsis":"Reads 3 bits from the font stream into A.","comment":"Marker for 3 bits"},
        "4861": {"synopsis":"Reads bits from the font stream into A until the marker bit preset in A shifts out (A = $10\nreads 4 bits, $20 three, $04 six, $02 seven).\nEntry: A = marker, B = bits left in C (the current byte), HL = the stream's last byte read.\nExit: A = the bits, carry set.","comment":"Bits left in this byte?"},
        "4863": {"comment":"No: next byte"},
        "4866": {"comment":"Load it"},
        "4867": {"synopsis":"Shifts one bit from C into A.","comment":"Next bit"},
        "4869": {"comment":"Into A"},
        "4870": {"comment":"Until the marker shifts out"},
        "4873": {"synopsis":"Decodes two rows.","comment":"First row; falls into the second"},
        "4876": {"synopsis":"Decodes one row by the header in D and stores it: bit 3 set = 7 bits as they are; otherwise\nbit 0 clear = 6 bits moved one place left; otherwise 3 bits widened to a row symmetric about\nits middle (bits 6-1; checked by simulation, e.g. 101 gives 01011010).","comment":"Marker for 7 bits"},
        "4878": {"comment":"Rows of 7 bits?"},
        "4883": {"comment":"Yes: store it"},
        "4885": {"comment":"Marker for 6 bits"},
        "4886": {"comment":"Rows of 6 bits?"},
        "4891": {"comment":"Yes: shift and store"},
        "4893": {"comment":"3 bits for a symmetric row"},
        "4899": {"comment":"Mirror the bits"},
        "4904": {"synopsis":"Mirror step: shifts the bit into the row."},
        "4905": {"comment":"into the right half"},
        "4910": {"synopsis":"Second mirror step."},
        "4911": {"synopsis":"Moves the row one place left."},
        "4912": {"synopsis":"Stores the row in A at the font address (HL') and moves to the next row ($80 on).","comment":"Font pointer set"},
        "4913": {"comment":"Store the row"},
        "4914": {"comment":"Next row down"},
        "4917": {"synopsis":"With NZ decodes two rows; with Z stores two blank rows.","comment":"Drawn: decode two"},
        "4919": {"comment":"Blank row"},
        "4923": {"comment":"and a second"},
        "4925": {"synopsis":"VIDEO, interrupt (entry +0): sets the first line parameter block of the LPT at $B900 (the\nstatus line) from ST_FLAG ($BFDF). ST_FLAG 0: margins $0B/$73 and LD1 $FEB8, the status text\nat $BEB8 in the system segment. Any other value: left margin $3F, which hides the row.\nST_FLAG = $2A: margins $0E/$70 and LD1 $F230, which shows the 34 bytes at $B230 (the text\nfrom AUTHOR_TEXT that the boot copied there with the RAM pager).\nExit: A, DE, HL changed.","comment":"ST_FLAG"},
        "4928": {"comment":"The value that shows the copied credit text?"},
        "4932": {"comment":"LD1 = $B230 in the system segment"},
        "4935": {"comment":"Margins $0E (left) and $70 (right)"},
        "4940": {"synopsis":"ST_FLAG is not $2A: the status line's own text, shown or hidden.","comment":"LD1 = $BEB8, the status text"},
        "4943": {"comment":"Margins $0B and $73"},
        "4946": {"comment":"Status line on?"},
        "4949": {"comment":"No: left margin $3F hides it"},
        "4951": {"synopsis":"Writes the margins (L, H) and LD1 (DE) into the LPT's first block.","comment":"Margins of the LPT's first block"},
        "4954": {"comment":"Its LD1"},
        "4959": {"synopsis":"VIDEO open fails with the three size words still stacked: drops them and returns error $DE\n(.VSIZE).","comment":"Drop the three stacked sizes"},
        "4962": {"synopsis":"Returns error $DE (.VSIZE): the page size is invalid.","comment":"Error $DE (.VSIZE)"},
        "4965": {"synopsis":"VIDEO, open channel and create channel (entries +2 and +4): opens a video page from\nMODE_VID, COLR_VID, X_SIZ_VID and Y_SIZ_VID ($BFDB-$BFDE).\n1. MODE_VID must be 0, 1, 2, 5 or 15 (else error $DD, .VMODE); Y_SIZ_VID 1-255 and X_SIZ_VID\n   1-42 (else $DE, .VSIZE).\n2. Works out the RAM: X bytes per line (2X in modes 1 and 2), 9 lines a row. The video part\n   (BC of EXOS 27) is X*Y*9 bytes, X*Y in mode 0, X*Y*10 in mode 2 and X*Y*18 in mode 15;\n   the one-segment part (DE) is 2Y + 128 bytes. Calls EXOS 27 (allocate channel buffer).\n3. Stores the channel number (IX-1), the mode (IX-2), bytes per line (IX-$38), rows\n   (IX-$39), colour mode (IX-$37), the sizes (IX-$36, IX-$34) and the NICK addresses of the\n   main area (IX-$32) and the secondary area (IX-$30). The video data ends where the 2Y+128\n   bytes below IX begin.\n4. Fills the Y-word row table at IX-(2Y+128) (pointer at IX-$2E) with row n = n * bytes per\n   line, which is multiplied by 9 when used.\n5. Builds the channel's 16-byte line parameter block at IX-$13: 9 lines, the NICK mode byte\n   for the page (CH128, PIXEL, LPIXEL or ATTRIBUTE, with the colour mode in bits 6-5),\n   margins that centre the page in 62 columns, and LD1/LD2/palette from VID_LPB_BLANK+4\n   (text) or VID_LPB_GFX (graphics).\n6. Goes on to VID_GFX_OPEN for a graphics page (mode bit 0 set) or to VID_TX_OPEN for a text\n   page.\nEntry: A = channel number, IX = channel RAM.\nExit: A = status.","comment":"Keep the channel number in A'"},
        "4966": {"comment":"MODE_VID"},
        "4970": {"comment":"Attribute graphics?"},
        "4974": {"comment":"Low-resolution graphics?"},
        "4978": {"comment":"Mode 0-2?"},
        "4980": {"comment":"Error $DD (.VMODE)"},
        "4983": {"synopsis":"The mode is valid: checks Y_SIZ_VID (1-255) and X_SIZ_VID (1-42).","comment":"Y_SIZ_VID"},
        "4986": {"comment":"No rows?"},
        "4989": {"comment":"E = rows"},
        "4990": {"comment":"X_SIZ_VID"},
        "4993": {"comment":"No columns?"},
        "4996": {"comment":"More than 42?"},
        "5000": {"comment":"B = columns"},
        "5001": {"comment":"Mode again"},
        "5002": {"comment":"Modes 15, 5 and 0 use X bytes a line"},
        "5013": {"comment":"Modes 1 and 2: 2X bytes a line"},
        "5015": {"synopsis":"Works out rows * bytes per line and the one-segment size 2Y + 128.","comment":"HL = 0"},
        "5019": {"synopsis":"Adds the rows (DE) to HL once per byte of a line.","comment":"HL = rows * bytes per line"},
        "5022": {"comment":"DE = that product, HL = rows"},
        "5023": {"comment":"Two bytes a row for the row table"},
        "5024": {"comment":"BC = $0080 (B is 0 after the loop)"},
        "5026": {"comment":"Plus 128 bytes of variables"},
        "5027": {"comment":"DE = one-segment size, HL = product"},
        "5028": {"comment":"BC = X*Y"},
        "5030": {"comment":"Times 9 (lines a row), with overflow checks"},
        "5032": {"comment":"Too big?"},
        "5037": {"comment":"Plus once more: X*Y*9"},
        "5038": {"comment":"Too big?"},
        "5040": {"comment":"Attribute page?"},
        "5044": {"comment":"Yes: BC = X*Y*9, the attribute area"},
        "5046": {"synopsis":"Stacks the sizes and picks the video size for the mode.","comment":"Keep the one-segment size, the second area, the pixel area"},
        "5049": {"comment":"Mode 15: two areas of X*Y*9"},
        "5051": {"comment":"Mode 5: the bitmap only"},
        "5055": {"comment":"Mode 0: X*Y character codes only"},
        "5059": {"comment":"Mode 1: the bitmap only"},
        "5061": {"synopsis":"Modes 2 and 15: the video size is both areas together.","comment":"Modes 2 and 15: add the second area"},
        "5062": {"comment":"Too big?"},
        "5064": {"synopsis":"BC = the video size from HL.","comment":"BC = the video bytes"},
        "5066": {"synopsis":"Allocates the channel RAM and stores the page's variables.","comment":"EXOS 27 (allocate channel buffer): IX = new RAM"},
        "5068": {"comment":"HL = X*Y*9, BC = second area, DE = 2Y+128"},
        "5071": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "5072": {"comment":"Size of the main area"},
        "5078": {"comment":"Size of the second area"},
        "5084": {"comment":"The channel number"},
        "5085": {"comment":"Kept at IX-1"},
        "5088": {"comment":"MODE_VID"},
        "5091": {"comment":"Kept at IX-2"},
        "5094": {"comment":"Modes 15 and 0: X bytes a line"},
        "5101": {"comment":"Mode 5 too; modes 1 and 2 are NZ"},
        "5103": {"synopsis":"Bytes per line from X_SIZ_VID; doubled for modes 1 and 2 (NZ here).","comment":"X_SIZ_VID"},
        "5108": {"comment":"Doubled for modes 1 and 2"},
        "5109": {"synopsis":"Stores bytes per line, rows and colour mode, then the area addresses.","comment":"Bytes per line"},
        "5112": {"comment":"Y_SIZ_VID"},
        "5115": {"comment":"Rows"},
        "5118": {"comment":"COLR_VID"},
        "5121": {"comment":"Taken modulo 4"},
        "5123": {"comment":"Colour mode"},
        "5126": {"comment":"Keep the main area's size"},
        "5127": {"comment":"HL = IX"},
        "5130": {"comment":"Minus 2Y+128: the row table's address"},
        "5132": {"comment":"Row table pointer"},
        "5138": {"comment":"Page 1's segment"},
        "5140": {"comment":"Its two low bits into bits 7-6"},
        "5142": {"comment":"Make HL a NICK address (segment FCh-FFh = 0000h-FFFFh)"},
        "5147": {"comment":"The mode"},
        "5150": {"comment":"Attribute page?"},
        "5154": {"comment":"Graphics without a second area (modes 1, 5)?"},
        "5158": {"synopsis":"Modes 0, 2 and 15 have a second area below the end of the video data.","comment":"Below the end: the second area"},
        "5161": {"synopsis":"Stores the second area's NICK address, then the main area's below it.","comment":"Second area's NICK address"},
        "5167": {"comment":"The main area's size"},
        "5168": {"comment":"Mode 0: main and second areas coincide"},
        "5171": {"comment":"Below the second area: the main area"},
        "5173": {"synopsis":"Stores the main area's NICK address and fills the row table.","comment":"Main area's NICK address"},
        "5179": {"comment":"BC = bytes per line"},
        "5184": {"comment":"DE = 0, the first row's offset"},
        "5186": {"comment":"The row table"},
        "5192": {"comment":"A = rows"},
        "5195": {"synopsis":"One row table entry per row: 0, X, 2X, ... bytes.","comment":"Store this row's offset"},
        "5199": {"comment":"Next offset: one more line's bytes"},
        "5202": {"comment":"All rows?"},
        "5205": {"comment":"HL = IX"},
        "5208": {"comment":"Minus $13: the channel's LPB"},
        "5212": {"comment":"9 lines a block (256 - $F7)"},
        "5215": {"comment":"The mode"},
        "5219": {"comment":"Mode 0: CH128 with VRES clear"},
        "5223": {"comment":"LPIXEL"},
        "5225": {"comment":"Mode 5?"},
        "5229": {"comment":"PIXEL (modes 1 and 2)"},
        "5231": {"comment":"Mode 15?"},
        "5235": {"comment":"ATTRIBUTE"},
        "5237": {"synopsis":"D holds the NICK mode bits; adds the colour mode and the margins.","comment":"Colour mode into bits 6-5"},
        "5243": {"comment":"The LPB's mode byte"},
        "5246": {"comment":"X_SIZ_VID"},
        "5250": {"comment":"Left margin (62 - X) / 2: the page is centred"},
        "5256": {"comment":"Right margin: left + X"},
        "5259": {"comment":"DE = the LPB's LD1 field"},
        "5260": {"comment":"Text pages: LD1, LD2 and palette of VID_LPB_BLANK"},
        "5263": {"comment":"12 bytes"},
        "5266": {"comment":"Graphics page?"},
        "5272": {"comment":"Yes: VID_LPB_GFX"},
        "5273": {"synopsis":"Copies LD1, LD2 and the palette into the channel's LPB and goes on to the page set-up.","comment":"Copy the rest of the LPB"},
        "5275": {"comment":"Graphics page: set up the beam and clear it"},
        "5278": {"comment":"Text page: set up and clear it"},
        "5281": {"synopsis":"VIDEO, close channel and destroy channel (entries +6 and +8): removes the channel from every\nscreen row that shows it (the 27 row owners at $BBA2), then rebuilds the LPT with C = 0\n(VID_LPT_FREE), so those rows show the border.\nEntry: A = channel number.\nExit: A = 0.","comment":"Row owners: screen rows 1-27"},
        "5284": {"comment":"27 rows"},
        "5286": {"synopsis":"Clears each row owned by the closing channel.","comment":"Shows this channel?"},
        "5289": {"comment":"Yes: no owner"},
        "5291": {"synopsis":"Next screen row."},
        "5294": {"comment":"C = 0: rebuild the free rows"},
        "5298": {"synopsis":"VIDEO, read character (entry +10): returns the next byte of a reply that a control sequence\nleft (the count at IX-$2A/IX-$29, up to four bytes from IX-$28). Without one, reads from the\npage: VID_GR_READ on a graphics page, VID_READ_CELL on a text page.\nEntry: IX = channel RAM.\nExit: B = the byte, A = status.","comment":"IX-$2C: BC = handler, DE = reply size, remaining"},
        "5303": {"comment":"Reply bytes left?"},
        "5307": {"comment":"One fewer"},
        "5308": {"comment":"Offset of the next reply byte"},
        "5315": {"comment":"Point at it"},
        "5316": {"comment":"B = the reply byte"},
        "5318": {"synopsis":"No reply pending: reads from the page itself.","comment":"Graphics page?"},
        "5328": {"synopsis":"VIDEO, write character (entry +14): one byte to the page.\n1. After ESC (IX-$24 set), the byte is looked up in VID_CTRL_CODES; a control code below $20\n   is looked up too.\n2. A code is accepted when VID_CTRL_FLAGS allows it on this kind of page; its handler comes\n   from VID_CTRL_TABLE and its byte count (code included) from the flags' low nibble.\n   Parameter bytes are collected at IX-$21 on.\n3. With all bytes in, VID_CTRL_RUN calls the handler.\n4. Other bytes are printed with bit 7 cleared: VID_GR_CHAR on a graphics page, VID_PUT_CHAR\n   on a text\n   page.\nUnknown ESC sequences return error $E6 (.ESC); unknown control codes are ignored.\nEntry: B = the byte, IX = channel RAM.\nExit: A = status.","comment":"After ESC?"},
        "5334": {"comment":"A = the byte"},
        "5335": {"comment":"ESC is used up"},
        "5339": {"synopsis":"Looks up the code in A; C is left as the table index (30 - position).","comment":"The codes"},
        "5342": {"comment":"31 of them"},
        "5345": {"comment":"Known?"},
        "5349": {"comment":"Step back over the rest twice: the flag table is in reverse"},
        "5351": {"comment":"D = the code's flags"},
        "5352": {"comment":"Handlers for text pages and shared codes"},
        "5355": {"comment":"Graphics page?"},
        "5361": {"comment":"Allowed on a text page?"},
        "5367": {"synopsis":"Graphics page: the code needs flag bit 4; bit 6 picks the graphics handler table.","comment":"Allowed on a graphics page?"},
        "5371": {"comment":"Its own graphics handler?"},
        "5375": {"comment":"Yes: the graphics handlers"},
        "5378": {"synopsis":"Accepted: stores the byte count and the handler, then counts the code itself.","comment":"Bytes in the sequence, code included"},
        "5381": {"comment":"Kept as the total"},
        "5384": {"comment":"And as the bytes still to come"},
        "5387": {"comment":"Index"},
        "5388": {"comment":"DE = the handler"},
        "5391": {"comment":"Kept for VID_CTRL_RUN"},
        "5397": {"comment":"Count the code"},
        "5399": {"synopsis":"Unknown or not allowed here: error $E6 (.ESC) for a byte $20 or above (after ESC), else\nignored.","comment":"A printable byte after ESC?"},
        "5401": {"comment":"Error $E6 (.ESC)"},
        "5404": {"comment":"A control code: ignored"},
        "5406": {"synopsis":"No ESC pending: stores a parameter byte if a sequence is collecting them.","comment":"Parameters to come?"},
        "5412": {"comment":"E = still to come"},
        "5413": {"comment":"Total minus still to come"},
        "5417": {"comment":"= the byte's offset from IX-$22"},
        "5422": {"comment":"Point IX at the slot"},
        "5424": {"comment":"Store the parameter"},
        "5429": {"synopsis":"Counts one byte of the sequence; runs the handler when it is complete.","comment":"All bytes in?"},
        "5434": {"comment":"Not yet: OK"},
        "5436": {"synopsis":"An ordinary byte: a control code below $20 is looked up, anything else printed.","comment":"Control code?"},
        "5442": {"comment":"Printed with bit 7 clear"},
        "5444": {"comment":"Graphics page?"},
        "5451": {"comment":"Text page"},
        "5454": {"synopsis":"Calls the collected handler through $B225 (a JP (HL) in the RAM pager) with the parameters\nin C, B, E, D. A handler that returns H > 0 leaves H reply bytes (C, B, E, D) at IX-$28 for\nVID_READ_CHAR.","comment":"BC = parameters 1-2, DE = parameters 3-4"},
        "5459": {"comment":"The handler"},
        "5465": {"comment":"Call it (JP (HL) at $B225)"},
        "5468": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "5470": {"comment":"A reply?"},
        "5472": {"comment":"Reply size"},
        "5475": {"comment":"Reply bytes left"},
        "5478": {"comment":"Reply: C, B, E, D"},
        "5492": {"synopsis":"VIDEO control code $1B (ESC): marks an ESC pending (IX-$24 = $FF) and falls into\nVID_READ_STATUS to return OK.","comment":"ESC pending"},
        "5496": {"comment":"No reply"},
        "5498": {"synopsis":"VIDEO, read channel status (entry +18): returns C = 0 and A = 0 (status).","comment":"OK"},
        "5499": {"comment":"C = 0"},
        "5501": {"synopsis":"Special function code above 1: falls on into @@SIZE (2), which returns B = bytes per line, C\n= rows, D = the mode.","comment":"Not @@SIZE?"},
        "5503": {"comment":"IX-$39: C = rows, B = bytes per line"},
        "5508": {"comment":"D = the mode"},
        "5513": {"synopsis":"Code above 2: falls on into @@ADDR (3), which returns BC = the main area's and DE = the\nsecond area's NICK address.","comment":"Not @@ADDR?"},
        "5515": {"comment":"IX-$32: BC = main, DE = second area"},
        "5522": {"synopsis":"Code above 3: @@FONT (4) rebuilds the character set (VID_FONT_RESET, part of VIDEO\ninitialise);\nanything else is error $EA (.ISPEC).","comment":"Not @@FONT?"},
        "5524": {"comment":"Rebuild the character set"},
        "5527": {"synopsis":"VIDEO, special function (entry +22). B = 1 is @@DISP: shows rows C to C+D-1 of the page on\nscreen rows E to E+D-1 (1-27), recording the channel and page row of each screen row at\n$BBA2/$BBBD and rebuilding the LPT (VID_LPT_UPDATE). C = 0 blanks those screen rows instead.\nInvalid values return error $DC (.VDISP). B = 2, 3, 4 go to VID_SIZE, VID_ADDR, VID_FONT.\nEntry: A = channel number, IX = channel RAM.\nExit: A = status.","comment":"Keep the channel number in A'"},
        "5528": {"comment":"Not @@DISP?"},
        "5530": {"comment":"Screen row 0?"},
        "5534": {"comment":"No rows?"},
        "5538": {"comment":"More than 28 rows?"},
        "5543": {"comment":"Screen row above 28?"},
        "5546": {"comment":"Past screen row 27?"},
        "5552": {"comment":"Page row 0: blank the rows"},
        "5556": {"comment":"Last page row - 1"},
        "5559": {"comment":"Past the page?"},
        "5564": {"comment":"A = channel number"},
        "5565": {"comment":"Row owners (screen row 1 at $BBA2)"},
        "5569": {"comment":"B = rows"},
        "5572": {"comment":"IY = first screen row's owner"},
        "5574": {"synopsis":"Records owner and page row for each screen row, then rebuilds the LPT.","comment":"Owner"},
        "5577": {"comment":"Page row shown ($BBBD on)"},
        "5582": {"comment":"Next page row"},
        "5585": {"comment":"Rebuild the LPT"},
        "5587": {"synopsis":"Returns error $DC (.VDISP).","comment":"Error $DC (.VDISP)"},
        "5590": {"synopsis":"Returns error $EA (.ISPEC): no such special function.","comment":"Error $EA (.ISPEC)"},
        "5593": {"synopsis":"@@DISP with page row 0: frees the screen rows, which then show the border.","comment":"Row owners"},
        "5596": {"comment":"B = rows"},
        "5599": {"comment":"First screen row"},
        "5600": {"synopsis":"Clears the owner of each screen row."},
        "5604": {"synopsis":"Rebuilds the LPT blocks of free rows (owner 0, with C = 0 on entry) from VID_LPB_BLANK,\nwhose margins hide the row.","comment":"Source: the blank LPB"},
        "5610": {"synopsis":"Rebuilds the LPT blocks of the rows that show this channel. For each of screen rows 1-27\nowned by channel C, it works out the row's address on the page (through the row table, so\nscrolled rows land right), writes it into the channel's LPB at IX-$13 (LD1; LD1 and LD2 on\nan attribute page) and copies those 16 bytes into the row's block at $B910 + 16 * (row - 1).\nWaits for port B4h bit 4 first and works with interrupts off.\nExit: A = 0, H = 0.","comment":"C = this channel"},
        "5614": {"comment":"Source: the channel's LPB at IX-$13"},
        "5622": {"synopsis":"Walks the 27 row owners and page rows with HL' at the LPT block of screen row 1.","comment":"LPT block of screen row 1"},
        "5626": {"comment":"Row owners"},
        "5629": {"comment":"Page rows"},
        "5632": {"comment":"27 rows"},
        "5634": {"comment":"No interrupts while the LPT changes"},
        "5635": {"synopsis":"Waits until port B4h bit 4 is set.","comment":"Interrupt state"},
        "5639": {"comment":"Not yet?"},
        "5641": {"synopsis":"One screen row: rewrites its LPT block if channel C owns it.","comment":"Owned by channel C?"},
        "5643": {"comment":"A = its page row"},
        "5647": {"comment":"Keep the block and the source"},
        "5649": {"comment":"DE = main area address of the row, HL = second area's"},
        "5652": {"comment":"The mode"},
        "5655": {"comment":"Mode 0: LD1 = the character codes"},
        "5658": {"comment":"HL = main area address"},
        "5659": {"comment":"Attribute page?"},
        "5663": {"comment":"LD2 = the bitmap row"},
        "5669": {"comment":"Back to an offset in the main area"},
        "5677": {"comment":"Plus the second area: the attribute row"},
        "5684": {"synopsis":"Stores HL as LD1 of the channel's LPB and copies it into the LPT.","comment":"LD1 of the channel's LPB"},
        "5690": {"comment":"HL = source"},
        "5691": {"comment":"DE = the LPT block"},
        "5694": {"comment":"16 bytes"},
        "5697": {"comment":"Copy the block"},
        "5701": {"synopsis":"Next LPT block, owner and page row.","comment":"16 bytes a block"},
        "5706": {"comment":"Next owner"},
        "5707": {"comment":"Next page row"},
        "5710": {"comment":"Done"},
        "5714": {"synopsis":"VIDEO, buffer moved (entry +26): adds the displacement BC to the main and second area\naddresses (IX-$32, IX-$30) and the row table pointer (IX-$2E, kept a page-1 address),\nrecomputes the beam on a graphics page (VID_BEAM_ADDR) and rebuilds the LPT\n(VID_LPT_UPDATE).\nEntry: BC = how far the RAM moved, IX = channel RAM.","comment":"HL = IX"},
        "5717": {"comment":"Minus $34: before the three addresses"},
        "5721": {"comment":"Three words"},
        "5723": {"synopsis":"Adjusts one address; the last (A = 0) is folded into page 1 by ADD_BC_WORD."},
        "5724": {"comment":"Add BC to the next one"},
        "5727": {"comment":"All three?"},
        "5729": {"comment":"Graphics page?"},
        "5733": {"comment":"Yes: the beam's address too"},
        "5736": {"comment":"Rebuild the LPT"},
        "5739": {"synopsis":"Six 4-byte heads (line count, mode byte, left and right margin) that VIDEO initialise\n($1281) writes into the six LPT blocks after the 28 rows: 14 lines with VINT, then 3, 4 and\n1 lines in VSYNC mode, 4 and 34 lines, the last with RELOAD."},
        "5763": {"synopsis":"Line parameter block for a free row: 9 lines, CH128, margins $3F/$74 (left past right: only\nborder shows), LD1 $FEB8, LD2 $01E9 and eight palette colours. VIDEO initialise copies it\ninto all 28 row blocks ($1271), VID_LPT_FREE into freed rows, and VID_OPEN copies its last\n12 bytes into a text page's LPB."},
        "5779": {"synopsis":"LD1 ($0000), LD2 ($01E9) and the eight palette colours that VID_OPEN copies into a graphics\npage's LPB."},
        "5791": {"synopsis":"The 31 codes VID_WRITE_CHAR knows, as control codes or after ESC: $0A $0D $1A $1E M s S . P\nI ? a @ F E R A o O $19 $0B $09 $08 $16 D U = $1B c C K. The code at position n has index 30\n- n in the handler tables and its flags at VID_CTRL_FLAGS + 30 - n."},
        "5822": {"synopsis":"Flags of the 31 codes, in the order of their indexes (K first, $0A last): bits 3-0 the bytes\nin the sequence counting the code itself, bit 4 allowed on a graphics page, bit 5 allowed on\na text page, bit 6 a graphics page uses VID_CTRL_TABLE + 20."},
        "5853": {"synopsis":"Handler addresses: 31 words by index (text pages and shared codes, $16DD-$171A), and from\n$16F1 the same index for the graphics handlers of the codes with flag bit 6 (their indexes\n21-30 reach $171B-$172E)."},
        "5935": {"synopsis":"VIDEO ESC K (define a character, index 0): writes the nine row bytes (parameters 2-10) of\ncharacter C (bit 7 ignored) into the character set at $B480 + C, one row every 128 bytes.\nVIDEO initialise also jumps here ($12EF).\nEntry: C = code, the row bytes at IX-$20 on.\nExit: A = 0, H = 0, IX 9 higher.","comment":"BC = code"},
        "5937": {"comment":"Codes 0-127"},
        "5939": {"comment":"The code's first row in the set"},
        "5943": {"comment":"Nine rows"},
        "5945": {"comment":"128 codes a row"},
        "5948": {"synopsis":"Copies one row byte into the character set.","comment":"Next row byte"},
        "5953": {"comment":"Next parameter"},
        "5957": {"comment":"OK, no reply"},
        "5960": {"synopsis":"VIDEO ESC c (one palette colour): sets colour C (0-7) of the channel's LPB palette to B and\nrebuilds the LPT.","comment":"HL = IX"},
        "5963": {"comment":"Colour number 0-7"},
        "5966": {"comment":"Minus $0B: the LPB's palette"},
        "5974": {"comment":"Set it"},
        "5975": {"comment":"Show it"},
        "5978": {"synopsis":"VIDEO ESC C (all eight palette colours): copies the eight parameters (IX-$21 on) into the\nchannel's LPB palette and rebuilds the LPT.","comment":"HL = IX"},
        "5981": {"comment":"Minus $0B: the LPB's palette"},
        "5985": {"comment":"The destination"},
        "5987": {"comment":"Minus $16 more: the parameters"},
        "5991": {"comment":"8 colours"},
        "5996": {"comment":"Show them"},
        "5999": {"synopsis":"VIDEO's device pseudo-descriptor (ROM form): XX_NEXT $6B7B (SOUND's, page-1 address), XX_RAM\n-2, DD_TYPE 0, DD_IRQFLAG $20 (video interrupt), DD_FLAGS $01 (a video device), DD_TAB $5781\nsegment 0 (VID_ENTRIES), DD_UNIT_COUNT 0, name \"VIDEO\", XX_SIZE 13. The device chain word at\n$0008 points at XX_SIZE."},
        "6017": {"synopsis":"VIDEO's entry table (addresses as run in page 3): interrupt, open, create, close, destroy,\nread character, read block (VID_READ_BLOCK), write character, write block (VID_WRITE_BLOCK),\nread status, set\nstatus (ERR_NOFN, not supported), special function, initialise (VID_INIT), buffer moved."},
        "6045": {"synopsis":"Folds HL back into page 1 if it left it (VID_WRAP_PAGE1), then falls into VID_NICK_ADDR.","comment":"Bit 7 to carry, bit 6 to sign"},
        "6047": {"comment":"Outside page 1?"},
        "6050": {"synopsis":"Turns the page-1 address HL into a NICK address: bits 15-14 become the low two bits of page\n1's segment (FCh-FFh).\nChanges: A, H.","comment":"Page 1's segment"},
        "6052": {"comment":"Low two bits to bits 7-6"},
        "6054": {"comment":"Into H's top bits"},
        "6060": {"synopsis":"Compares X (BC) with the page's largest X (IX-$41).\nExit: carry if X is off the page; HL changed.","comment":"Largest X"},
        "6067": {"comment":"Carry: X is too big"},
        "6070": {"synopsis":"Compares Y (DE) with the page's largest Y (IX-$3F).\nExit: carry if Y is off the page; HL changed.","comment":"Largest Y"},
        "6077": {"comment":"Carry: Y is too big"},
        "6080": {"synopsis":"Shifts HL right by the colour mode + 1 (+1 more on modes 5 and 15): an X coordinate to a\npixel number.","comment":"Colour mode"},
        "6083": {"comment":"Plus 1"},
        "6084": {"synopsis":"Shifts HL right by B, plus 1 on modes 5 and 15 (mode bit 2).","comment":"Low-resolution or attribute page?"},
        "6091": {"synopsis":"Shifts HL right B times."},
        "6098": {"synopsis":"Called when HL has left page 1 (carry = HL bit 15): steps page 1 one segment back for an\naddress below $4000 or one forward for $8000-$BFFF, and makes HL a page-1 address again.\nChanges: A, H.","comment":"Page 1's segment"},
        "6100": {"comment":"One back (DEC leaves carry alone)"},
        "6101": {"comment":"Below page 1?"},
        "6103": {"comment":"No: one forward instead"},
        "6105": {"synopsis":"Pages the segment in and folds HL into $4000-$7FFF.","comment":"Page 1 = the next segment"},
        "6107": {"comment":"Back into $4000-$7FFF"},
        "6112": {"synopsis":"Multiplies HL by DE: the 32-bit product is HL (high) and IX (low).\nChanges: B, F.","comment":"Low word = 0"},
        "6116": {"comment":"16 bits"},
        "6118": {"synopsis":"One bit of the multiplier.","comment":"Shift the product left"},
        "6120": {"comment":"Top multiplier bit set?"},
        "6124": {"comment":"Add the multiplicand"},
        "6128": {"comment":"Carry into the high word"},
        "6129": {"synopsis":"Next bit."},
        "6132": {"synopsis":"Copies the graphics page's drawing state to work variables in the system segment, so\nplotting can run without IX: $BB4D pen colour byte (IX-$50), $BB90 and $BB8E the main and\nsecond area addresses, $BB48 the main area's size, $BB4B the mode, $BB47 the ESC a flags\n(IX-$55), $BB4A the attribute byte (IX-$51).\nExit: IY = the pixel writer (IX-$4A), E = bytes per line, D = 0, C = beam pixel mask, HL =\nbeam address in page 1, A = its segment.","comment":"The pixel writer for the line mode"},
        "6141": {"comment":"Pen colour byte"},
        "6144": {"synopsis":"Entry to VID_GFX_STATE with the pen colour byte already in A (used at $1DB0) and IY set by\nthe caller."},
        "6147": {"comment":"IX-$32: BC = main, DE = second area"},
        "6160": {"synopsis":"Entry to VID_GFX_STATE for the main area's size and what follows (used at $1B6C).","comment":"IX-$36: BC = main area's size"},
        "6165": {"comment":"Offset of the attribute area"},
        "6169": {"comment":"DE = bytes per line"},
        "6174": {"comment":"The mode"},
        "6180": {"comment":"ESC a flags"},
        "6186": {"comment":"Attribute (paper/ink) byte"},
        "6192": {"comment":"C = beam pixel mask"},
        "6195": {"comment":"HL = beam address"},
        "6201": {"comment":"A = beam's segment"},
        "6205": {"synopsis":"Graphics page set-up at open (from VID_OPEN): the largest X (bytes per line * 16 - 1, * 32\non modes 5 and 15) and Y (rows * 36 - 1), the line count (rows * 9), line style 1, line mode\n0, ink 1, paper 0; then falls into VID_GFX_CLEAR.","comment":"Bytes per line"},
        "6211": {"comment":"Times 16"},
        "6215": {"comment":"Low-resolution or attribute page?"},
        "6221": {"comment":"Times 32"},
        "6222": {"synopsis":"Stores the largest X and works out the largest Y.","comment":"Largest X"},
        "6229": {"comment":"Rows"},
        "6236": {"comment":"Times 9: pixel lines"},
        "6240": {"comment":"Kept at IX-$4D"},
        "6246": {"comment":"Times 4, minus 1: largest Y"},
        "6255": {"comment":"Colour mode"},
        "6258": {"comment":"Halved, plus 1"},
        "6263": {"comment":"Line style 1 (solid)"},
        "6268": {"comment":"Line mode 0 (put)"},
        "6273": {"comment":"Ink 1"},
        "6278": {"comment":"Paper 0"},
        "6283": {"synopsis":"VIDEO $1A on a graphics page (clear page): fills an attribute page's attribute area with the\nattribute byte (IX-$51) and its bitmap with 0, any other page's bitmap with the paper byte\n(IX-$51), turns the beam off and falls into VID_GFX_HOME.","comment":"Attribute byte"},
        "6286": {"comment":"Attribute page?"},
        "6292": {"comment":"Second area: the attributes"},
        "6298": {"comment":"Its size"},
        "6304": {"comment":"Fill it with D"},
        "6307": {"comment":"The bitmap gets 0: paper is in the attributes"},
        "6309": {"synopsis":"Fills the main area (the bitmap) with D.","comment":"Main area"},
        "6315": {"comment":"Its size"},
        "6321": {"comment":"Fill it"},
        "6324": {"synopsis":"VIDEO $1E on a graphics page (home): beam off (the XOR A inside $1AE1), the values at IX-$52\nand IX-$53 set to 1, the beam to X = 0, Y = 0; falls into VID_BEAM_SET.","comment":"Beam off; A = 0"},
        "6335": {"comment":"BC = X = 0, DE = Y = 0"},
        "6339": {"synopsis":"Moves the beam to X = BC, Y = DE without drawing, then falls into VID_BEAM_ADDR.","comment":"Beam Y"},
        "6345": {"synopsis":"Moves the beam to X = BC, keeping Y, then works out its address (used at $1C83, $1D30).","comment":"Beam X"},
        "6351": {"synopsis":"Works out the beam from its X (IX-$3D) and Y (IX-$3B): its pixel number (IX-$45), the pixel\nmask (IX-$48, from VID_PIX_MASKS rotated by the pixel's place in the byte), its line from\nthe top (IX-$43) and its byte address, kept as segment (IX-$4B) and page-1 address (IX-$47).\nY counts from the bottom, 4 per line.\nExit: A = 0, H = 0.","comment":"Beam X"},
        "6358": {"comment":"Byte column: X >> 4 (5 on modes 5, 15)"},
        "6363": {"comment":"Keep it; HL = X"},
        "6364": {"comment":"Pixel number"},
        "6373": {"comment":"Low bits: the pixel's place"},
        "6374": {"comment":"Mask for one pixel at the left"},
        "6381": {"comment":"Place 0-7"},
        "6383": {"comment":"Plus 1 for the DJNZ"},
        "6385": {"comment":"The mask"},
        "6386": {"comment":"LD E,$0F hides RRCA at $18F3, the loop's target"},
        "6388": {"comment":"Rotate right once per place"},
        "6390": {"comment":"Beam pixel mask"},
        "6393": {"comment":"Beam Y"},
        "6399": {"comment":"Largest Y"},
        "6406": {"comment":"Up from the bottom"},
        "6408": {"comment":"4 per line"},
        "6413": {"comment":"Beam line from the top"},
        "6419": {"comment":"Keep IX"},
        "6421": {"comment":"Bytes per line"},
        "6426": {"comment":"Line * bytes per line, low word in IX"},
        "6429": {"comment":"Product to the stack, IX back"},
        "6432": {"comment":"BC = byte column"},
        "6434": {"comment":"Plus the main area's start"},
        "6441": {"comment":"Segment FCh-FFh from bits 15-14"},
        "6446": {"comment":"Beam's segment"},
        "6449": {"comment":"As a page-1 address"},
        "6453": {"comment":"Beam address"},
        "6462": {"synopsis":"Masks for one pixel at a byte's left edge, by colour mode (read at $18E6): 2 colours $80, 4\ncolours $88, 16 colours $AA, 256 colours $FF."},
        "6466": {"synopsis":"Plots the beam's own pixel: loads the drawing state (VID_GFX_STATE), pages the beam's\nsegment into page 1 and falls into VID_PLOT. Page 1 is left changed.","comment":"State; A = beam's segment"},
        "6469": {"comment":"Page 1 = it"},
        "6471": {"synopsis":"Plots one pixel at HL (mask C) with the pen colour ($BB4D), through the pixel writer in IY.\nOn an attribute page (VID_PLOT_ATTR) it also writes the attribute. Folds HL back into page 1\nfirst if it left it.","comment":"Outside page 1?"},
        "6476": {"synopsis":"VID_PLOT for an HL already inside page 1 (called at $1E36, $1EF9 and $2235-$228F).","comment":"The mode"},
        "6479": {"comment":"Attribute page?"},
        "6483": {"synopsis":"Writes the pixel: pen colour in A, then the line mode's writer.","comment":"Pen colour byte"},
        "6486": {"comment":"Pixel writer (VID_PIX_WRITERS)"},
        "6488": {"synopsis":"Line mode 2 (AND): keeps the pixel's bits only where the pen colour has them too; continues\nthrough the put writer's XOR, AND C, XOR.","comment":"Pen AND screen"},
        "6489": {"synopsis":"Line mode 0 (put): the masked pixel takes the pen colour.","comment":"Pen XOR screen"},
        "6490": {"synopsis":"Line mode 3 (XOR): the masked pixel is XORed with the pen colour.","comment":"Only the pixel's bits"},
        "6491": {"comment":"Merge with the screen byte"},
        "6492": {"comment":"Store it"},
        "6494": {"synopsis":"Line mode 1 (OR): the masked pixel is ORed with the pen colour.","comment":"Only the pixel's bits"},
        "6495": {"comment":"OR the screen byte"},
        "6498": {"synopsis":"Attribute page: writes the attribute byte ($BB4A) of the pixel's character cell, its ink\nnibble unless ESC a flag bit 2 is set, its paper nibble unless bit 3 is set; then plots the\npixel too unless bit 1 is set.","comment":"Keep the address and the line step"},
        "6500": {"comment":"Keep page 1"},
        "6503": {"comment":"HL = NICK address"},
        "6506": {"comment":"Main area's size"},
        "6510": {"comment":"The same byte in the attribute area"},
        "6511": {"comment":"Page it in"},
        "6514": {"comment":"ESC a flags"},
        "6518": {"comment":"Mask: none yet"},
        "6519": {"comment":"Write the low (ink) nibble?"},
        "6523": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "6525": {"synopsis":"Adds the high (paper) nibble to the mask unless flag bit 3 is set.","comment":"Write the high (paper) nibble?"},
        "6529": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "6531": {"synopsis":"Replaces the masked nibbles of the attribute, restores page 1 and goes on to the pixel\nunless flag bit 1 is set.","comment":"D = the nibbles to write"},
        "6532": {"comment":"The attribute byte"},
        "6535": {"comment":"Replace the masked bits"},
        "6539": {"comment":"Page 1 back"},
        "6542": {"comment":"Pixel too?"},
        "6549": {"synopsis":"Line step up and left (HL = address, DE = bytes per line, C = pixel mask).","comment":"Up one line"},
        "6552": {"synopsis":"Line step left: the mask rotates left; past the byte's left pixel, the previous byte.","comment":"Next pixel to the left"},
        "6554": {"comment":"Still in this byte?"},
        "6555": {"comment":"The byte before"},
        "6557": {"synopsis":"Line step right and up.","comment":"Next pixel to the right"},
        "6559": {"comment":"Still in this byte?"},
        "6561": {"comment":"The next byte"},
        "6562": {"synopsis":"Line step up: one line less.","comment":"Up one line"},
        "6566": {"synopsis":"Line step left and down.","comment":"Next pixel to the left"},
        "6568": {"comment":"Still in this byte?"},
        "6570": {"comment":"The byte before"},
        "6571": {"synopsis":"Line step down: one line more.","comment":"Down one line"},
        "6573": {"synopsis":"Line step down and right.","comment":"Down one line"},
        "6574": {"synopsis":"Line step right: the mask rotates right; past the byte's right pixel, the next byte.","comment":"Next pixel to the right"},
        "6576": {"comment":"Still in this byte?"},
        "6577": {"comment":"The next byte"},
        "6579": {"synopsis":"Diagonal line steps by direction, read by VID_ESC_A ($1A0D): index (up * 2 + left):\ndown-right, left-down, right-up, up-left."},
        "6587": {"synopsis":"Straight line steps, read by VID_ESC_A ($1A2E): index (up * 4 + left * 2 + Y is the longer\naxis): right, down, left, down, right, up, left, up."},
        "6603": {"synopsis":"Returns HL = |HL - DE| and shifts into A a bit that is 1 when HL < DE.\nEntry: carry clear.","comment":"HL - DE"},
        "6605": {"comment":"Not negative?"},
        "6607": {"comment":"DE = the negative difference"},
        "6608": {"comment":"Carry is set: 1 - d - 1 = -d"},
        "6613": {"synopsis":"Shifts the sign (carry) into A.","comment":"A = A * 2 + (HL < DE)"},
        "6615": {"synopsis":"VIDEO ESC R (relative beam move): adds the beam's position to the offsets (BC = X, DE = Y,\nthrough VID_BEAM_ADD) and falls into VID_ESC_A.","comment":"BC, DE = the new position"},
        "6618": {"synopsis":"VIDEO ESC A (beam to X = BC, Y = DE): error $D8 (.VBEAM) off the page. With the beam off it\nonly moves (VID_BEAM_SET). With it on, it draws a line from the old position, one point per\nstep of the longer axis (Bresenham): VID_STEP_DIAG and VID_STEP_AXIS give the step routines\n(kept at $BB84 and $BB78), the line style byte ($BB4C, from IX-$4F) rotates once per point\nand a set bit plots it (VID_PLOT). IX is lost: the steps are jumped to through it.\nExit: A = 0 or error, H = 0.","comment":"Error $D8 (.VBEAM) if off the page"},
        "6620": {"comment":"X off the page?"},
        "6623": {"comment":"Y off the page?"},
        "6626": {"comment":"Yes: the error"},
        "6627": {"comment":"Beam on?"},
        "6631": {"comment":"No: only move the beam"},
        "6634": {"comment":"Keep the new X, Y in the other set"},
        "6635": {"comment":"IX-$45: BC = old pixel number, DE = old line"},
        "6640": {"comment":"Keep them"},
        "6642": {"comment":"Old beam: HL, C, E = bytes per line"},
        "6645": {"comment":"Its segment into A'"},
        "6646": {"comment":"New X, Y back"},
        "6647": {"comment":"Move the beam there"},
        "6650": {"comment":"BC = new pixel number, DE = new line"},
        "6655": {"comment":"A collects the direction bits"},
        "6656": {"comment":"HL = new line"},
        "6657": {"comment":"DE = old line"},
        "6658": {"comment":"HL = |dy|, up?"},
        "6661": {"comment":"DE = old pixel number"},
        "6662": {"comment":"Keep |dy|"},
        "6663": {"comment":"HL = new pixel number"},
        "6665": {"comment":"HL = |dx|, left?"},
        "6668": {"comment":"Keep |dx|"},
        "6669": {"comment":"Diagonal step for the direction"},
        "6675": {"comment":"Kept for the line loop"},
        "6679": {"comment":"HL = |dx|"},
        "6680": {"comment":"DE = |dy|"},
        "6682": {"comment":"Which axis is longer?"},
        "6685": {"comment":"Y longer: HL = |dx| already"},
        "6687": {"comment":"X longer: HL = |dy|, DE = |dx|"},
        "6688": {"synopsis":"HL = the shorter, DE = the longer distance: sets up the error term and the straight step,\nthen draws.","comment":"BC = shorter"},
        "6690": {"comment":"Keep the longer"},
        "6691": {"comment":"Plus 1 if Y is the longer axis"},
        "6693": {"comment":"Shorter - longer"},
        "6695": {"comment":"Kept as the diagonal step's error change"},
        "6696": {"comment":"Half the longer"},
        "6700": {"comment":"Starting error term"},
        "6702": {"comment":"Straight step for the direction"},
        "6708": {"comment":"Kept for the line loop"},
        "6712": {"comment":"HL = error term"},
        "6713": {"comment":"DE = shorter - longer"},
        "6714": {"comment":"Old beam's state back"},
        "6715": {"comment":"Line style"},
        "6721": {"comment":"HL = longer, the beam's address stacked"},
        "6722": {"comment":"A = the beam's segment"},
        "6723": {"comment":"Page it into page 1"},
        "6725": {"comment":"Point count (longer + 1) as A:B"},
        "6729": {"comment":"Outer count in A'"},
        "6730": {"comment":"HL = beam address"},
        "6731": {"comment":"Plot the first point"},
        "6733": {"synopsis":"Next round of 256 points: the outer count back from A'."},
        "6734": {"synopsis":"One step along the line.","comment":"Step to the next point"},
        "6737": {"synopsis":"Plots the point if the next line style bit is set, and counts the points.","comment":"Line style"},
        "6740": {"comment":"Next bit"},
        "6744": {"comment":"Set: plot it"},
        "6747": {"comment":"Inner count"},
        "6749": {"comment":"Outer count"},
        "6753": {"comment":"OK, no reply"},
        "6756": {"synopsis":"Bresenham step: with the error term (HL') negative, adds the shorter distance and takes the\nstraight step ($BB78); else adds shorter - longer and takes the diagonal step ($BB84).","comment":"Error term"},
        "6757": {"comment":"Negative?"},
        "6761": {"comment":"Error + shorter"},
        "6763": {"comment":"Straight step"},
        "6769": {"synopsis":"Error term not negative: diagonal step.","comment":"Error + shorter - longer"},
        "6771": {"comment":"Diagonal step"},
        "6777": {"synopsis":"Line style bit patterns for ESC . 1-16 (read by VID_ESC_DOT): one bit per point, a set bit\nplots."},
        "6793": {"synopsis":"VIDEO ESC . on a graphics page (line style): IX-$4F = pattern C (1-16) from VID_LINE_STYLES.","comment":"Style 1-16"},
        "6794": {"comment":"To 0-15"},
        "6798": {"comment":"The patterns"},
        "6804": {"comment":"The pattern"},
        "6805": {"comment":"Line style"},
        "6810": {"synopsis":"VIDEO ESC M on a graphics page (line mode): C bits 1-0 pick the pixel writer (0 put, 1 OR, 2\nAND, 3 XOR) from VID_PIX_WRITERS into IX-$4A. On an attribute page the pen's pixel value\nalso becomes 1 - (C >> 2), set through VID_SET_PEN.","comment":"Attribute page?"},
        "6817": {"comment":"C >> 2"},
        "6822": {"comment":"Inverted: the pen's pixel value"},
        "6825": {"comment":"Set the pen colour byte"},
        "6829": {"synopsis":"Stores the pixel writer for line mode C AND 3.","comment":"Mode 0-3"},
        "6832": {"comment":"The writers"},
        "6838": {"comment":"Pixel writer"},
        "6846": {"synopsis":"Pixel writers by line mode (read by VID_ESC_M): put VID_PIX_PUT, OR VID_PIX_OR, AND\nVID_PIX_AND, XOR VID_PIX_XOR."},
        "6854": {"synopsis":"VIDEO ESC a (attribute flags): only on an attribute page (else error $E6, .ESC). Stores C at\nIX-$55 (bit 1: no pixel, bit 2: keep ink, bit 3: keep paper, used by VID_PLOT_ATTR) and\nmakes the pen's pixel value 1 - bit 0 through VID_SET_PEN.","comment":"Error $E6 (.ESC) if not"},
        "6856": {"comment":"Attribute page?"},
        "6861": {"comment":"Attribute flags"},
        "6865": {"comment":"Pixel value: bit 0 inverted"},
        "6868": {"comment":"Set the pen colour byte"},
        "6870": {"synopsis":"VIDEO ESC S on a graphics page (beam on): plots the beam's point and sets IX-$4E to $FF. The\nLD H,$AF at $1AE1 hides ESC s (beam off), which enters at $1AE2 (XOR A) and stores 0.","comment":"Keep page 1"},
        "6873": {"comment":"Plot the beam's point"},
        "6877": {"comment":"Page 1 back"},
        "6879": {"comment":"Beam on"},
        "6881": {"comment":"Hides XOR A at $1AE2: ESC s, beam off"},
        "6883": {"comment":"Beam on/off"},
        "6886": {"synopsis":"Returns OK with no reply (A = 0, H = 0).","comment":"OK"},
        "6887": {"comment":"No reply"},
        "6889": {"synopsis":"VIDEO ESC I on a graphics page (ink): on an attribute page sets the low nibble of the\nattribute byte (IX-$51) to C; otherwise sets the pen colour through VID_SET_PEN.","comment":"Attribute page?"},
        "6895": {"comment":"The ink"},
        "6896": {"comment":"Low nibble"},
        "6898": {"synopsis":"Replaces the bits of IX-$51 selected by C with A's (ESC P on an attribute page enters here\nwith C = $F0).","comment":"Replace the masked bits"},
        "6905": {"comment":"Attribute byte"},
        "6910": {"synopsis":"Sets the pen colour byte IX-$50 from colour C: VID_COLOUR_BYTE expands C for the colour\nmode, and\nVID_GR_STORECOL stores it through IY = IX + 1. Returns OK through VID_GFX_OK.","comment":"A = colour C spread over a byte"},
        "6917": {"synopsis":"VIDEO, ESC P on a graphics page (paper colour), reached through the graphics escape table at\n$171D; also called with C = 0 when a graphics page is set up ($1888). On an attribute page\n(mode 15) the colour goes into the high nibble of the attribute byte (IX-$51); on a pixel\npage it is turned into a byte with every pixel in that colour and kept at IX-$51.\nEntry: C = the colour, IX = the channel RAM.\nExit: A = 0, H = 0.\nChanges: A, C, H, IY.","comment":"Attribute graphics (mode 15)?"},
        "6923": {"comment":"Colour to the high nibble"},
        "6928": {"comment":"Only the paper nibble changes"},
        "6930": {"comment":"Merge into the attribute byte at IX-$51"},
        "6932": {"synopsis":"Pixel page: the paper colour as a pixel byte, stored at IX-$51.","comment":"Byte filled with the colour; IY = IX"},
        "6935": {"synopsis":"Stores the colour byte A at IY-$51 and returns status 0. The paper path comes here with IY =\nIX (IX-$51); the ink path at VID_SET_PEN with IY = IX+1, so the byte lands at IX-$50.","comment":"IX-$51 (paper) or IX-$50 (ink)"},
        "6938": {"comment":"Status 0"},
        "6940": {"synopsis":"Turns a palette index into a byte whose every pixel has that colour, for the page's colour\nmode (IX-$37: 0 two, 1 four, 2 sixteen, 3 256 colours). Two colours: $00 or $FF from bit 0;\nfour colours: bit 0 fills the high nibble, bit 1 the low nibble; sixteen colours: two pixels\nof the colour; 256 colours: the index itself.\nEntry: C = the palette index, IX = the channel RAM.\nExit: A = the pixel byte, IY = IX.\nChanges: A, H, IY; C on the sixteen-colour path.","comment":"IY = IX"},
        "6944": {"synopsis":"Entry of VID_COLOUR_BYTE that leaves IY alone, used by the fill ($1D86) which keeps its plot\nroutine in IY.","comment":"Colour mode, shifted out bit by bit"},
        "6948": {"comment":"Bit 0: four or 256 colours?"},
        "6952": {"comment":"Bit 1: sixteen colours?"},
        "6956": {"comment":"Two colours: bit 0 of the index"},
        "6959": {"comment":"$00 or $FF"},
        "6961": {"synopsis":"Four or 256 colours: 256 colours return the index unchanged; four colours spread bit 0 over\nthe high nibble and bit 1 over the low nibble.","comment":"256 colours: the index is the byte"},
        "6964": {"comment":"Four colours: two colour bits"},
        "6966": {"comment":"Bit 0 kept in C, bit 1 to carry"},
        "6970": {"comment":"$FF when bit 1 is set"},
        "6971": {"comment":"Bit 0 back out of C"},
        "6973": {"comment":"Bit 0 to bit 7, bit 1 below it"},
        "6974": {"comment":"Spread each bit over its nibble"},
        "6980": {"comment":"Bit 0 in bits 7-4, bit 1 in bits 3-0"},
        "6981": {"synopsis":"Sixteen colours: spreads the four index bits over the byte so that both of its pixels have\nthe colour.","comment":"Sixteen colours: four index bits"},
        "6983": {"comment":"Interleave the bits through C"},
        "7004": {"comment":"The finished pattern"},
        "7005": {"comment":"Rotated into place"},
        "7008": {"synopsis":"VIDEO, ESC @ on a graphics page (read the beam position), reached through the escape table\nat $1701. Hands the beam's X and Y back to the escape dispatcher ($155C), which queues them\nas the next four bytes a read returns.\nExit: A = 0, H = 4 (bytes queued), BC = beam X, DE = beam Y.\nChanges: A, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"BC = beam X, DE = beam Y"},
        "7013": {"comment":"Four bytes for the next reads"},
        "7017": {"synopsis":"VIDEO, read character on a graphics page (from $14CA): the palette index of the pixel under\nthe beam. On an attribute page the pixel's bit chooses the ink (low) or paper (high) nibble\nof its attribute byte.\nEntry: IX = the channel RAM.\nExit: A = 0, B = C = the colour, H = 1.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IY ($BB47-$BB4D and $BB48 set by VID_GFX_STATE_B).","comment":"Keep page 1"},
        "7020": {"comment":"HL = beam address, C = its pixel mask"},
        "7023": {"comment":"Colour mode"},
        "7026": {"comment":"Page 1 = the beam's video segment"},
        "7028": {"comment":"The beam pixel's bits"},
        "7030": {"comment":"As a palette index"},
        "7035": {"comment":"Attribute graphics (mode 15)?"},
        "7042": {"comment":"Back to a 16-bit video address"},
        "7045": {"comment":"Past the pixel area: its attribute byte"},
        "7050": {"comment":"Page it into page 1"},
        "7053": {"comment":"Paper in the high nibble, ink in the low"},
        "7054": {"comment":"Pixel set: the ink nibble"},
        "7058": {"comment":"Pixel clear: the paper nibble"},
        "7062": {"synopsis":"Keeps the chosen attribute nibble as the colour.","comment":"Colour 0-15"},
        "7065": {"synopsis":"Restores page 1 and returns status 0 with the colour in B.","comment":"Page 1 back"},
        "7068": {"comment":"Status 0"},
        "7072": {"synopsis":"Turns the bits of one pixel (the byte masked to that pixel) into its palette index, the\ninverse of VID_COLOUR_BYTE.\nEntry: A = the masked pixel bits, B = the colour mode (0-3).\nExit: A = the palette index.\nChanges: A, B, C.","comment":"Bit 0: four or 256 colours?"},
        "7076": {"comment":"Bit 1: sixteen colours?"},
        "7080": {"comment":"Two colours: carry when the bit is set"},
        "7083": {"comment":"0 or 1"},
        "7086": {"synopsis":"Four or 256 colours: 256 colours return the byte; four colours take bit 0 from the high\nnibble and bit 1 from the low nibble.","comment":"256 colours: the byte is the index"},
        "7089": {"comment":"Carry: a bit in the high nibble"},
        "7093": {"comment":"Carry: a bit in the low nibble"},
        "7098": {"comment":"High-nibble bit back"},
        "7101": {"comment":"Index 0-3"},
        "7104": {"synopsis":"Sixteen colours: gathers the four interleaved colour bits of the pixel into an index 0-15.","comment":"Sixteen colours: collect four bits"},
        "7111": {"comment":"The pixel bits of one colour plane"},
        "7124": {"comment":"Index 0-15"},
        "7127": {"synopsis":"Adds the beam position to a pair of offsets, giving graphics coordinates relative to the\nbeam (ESC R at VID_ESC_R, the character and line-feed checks).\nEntry: BC = X offset, DE = Y offset, IX = the channel RAM.\nExit: BC = beam X + BC, DE = beam Y + DE.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Beam X"},
        "7133": {"comment":"X offset added"},
        "7136": {"comment":"Beam Y"},
        "7142": {"comment":"Y offset added"},
        "7145": {"synopsis":"VIDEO, write character on a graphics page (from $1548, codes 32 and up with bit 7 cleared).\nOn a pixel page it draws the character's 9 font rows (from $B480, $80 bytes apart) at the\nbeam, plotting each set bit with the current line mode and ink; in 16 and 256 colours every\nrow is drawn twice. The beam then moves right by the character's width; a character that\ndoes not fit on the line first gets a carriage return and line feed, and one that does not\nfit below the beam draws nothing. An attribute page goes to VID_AT_CHAR.\n1. Work out the character's right and bottom edges from the beam and check that the page\n   holds them.\n2. Draw the 8 x 9 bits with the alternate register set holding the plot position.\n3. Advance the beam, or start a new line when it has run off the right edge.\nEntry: B = the character, IX = the channel RAM.\nExit: A = 0, H = 0.\nChanges: all main and alternate registers, IY.","comment":"Attribute graphics (mode 15)?"},
        "7152": {"comment":"Character in C"},
        "7153": {"comment":"Second set: the sizes"},
        "7154": {"comment":"-16 per row repeat"},
        "7157": {"comment":"Row repeat: 1, or 2 in 16/256 colours"},
        "7160": {"synopsis":"Doubles the bottom-row offset once per row repeat.","comment":"-32 or -64: the bottom row"},
        "7163": {"comment":"DE = Y offset of the bottom row"},
        "7164": {"comment":"Colour mode"},
        "7167": {"comment":"Units per pixel: 2 to the mode+1"},
        "7170": {"comment":"Low resolution?"},
        "7177": {"synopsis":"Doubles the X units of one pixel once per colour-mode step.","comment":"Units per pixel"},
        "7180": {"comment":"Kept for the width at the end"},
        "7183": {"comment":"Seven pixels in X units"},
        "7189": {"comment":"Wider than the page?"},
        "7193": {"comment":"Status 0: nothing drawn"},
        "7195": {"comment":"The character's far corner"},
        "7198": {"comment":"Below the bottom of the page?"},
        "7201": {"comment":"Status 0: nothing drawn"},
        "7203": {"comment":"Past the right edge?"},
        "7208": {"comment":"Carriage return"},
        "7211": {"comment":"Line feed"},
        "7214": {"synopsis":"Draws the character: page 1 holds the beam's video segment, the alternate set the plot\nposition (HL, mask C, DE bytes per line), the main set the font pointer.","comment":"Keep page 1"},
        "7217": {"comment":"Row repeat count in A'"},
        "7221": {"comment":"Beam address, mask, plot routine"},
        "7224": {"comment":"Page 1 = the beam's video segment"},
        "7226": {"comment":"Main set: the font"},
        "7227": {"comment":"Font column of the character"},
        "7233": {"comment":"Next font row is $80 bytes on"},
        "7236": {"comment":"Nine rows"},
        "7238": {"comment":"Page the video segment"},
        "7242": {"synopsis":"Steps to the next font row.","comment":"Next font row"},
        "7243": {"synopsis":"Starts one font row: B = how many times it is drawn.","comment":"Rows left"},
        "7244": {"comment":"Row repeat count"},
        "7247": {"synopsis":"Draws one font row as one pixel line, eight pixels left to right.","comment":"Font row bits"},
        "7248": {"comment":"Plot set: eight pixels"},
        "7253": {"synopsis":"Moves the plot position one pixel right.","comment":"One pixel right"},
        "7256": {"synopsis":"Takes the next font bit and plots the pixel when it is set."},
        "7257": {"comment":"Next font bit"},
        "7260": {"comment":"Set: plot it"},
        "7263": {"comment":"Eight pixels"},
        "7265": {"comment":"One pixel line down"},
        "7268": {"comment":"Back seven pixels to the left edge"},
        "7270": {"synopsis":"Moves the plot position back to the character's left edge.","comment":"One pixel left"},
        "7275": {"comment":"Font set"},
        "7276": {"comment":"Same font row again?"},
        "7279": {"comment":"Next of the nine rows"},
        "7281": {"comment":"Page 1 back"},
        "7284": {"comment":"Character width: 8 pixels in units"},
        "7293": {"comment":"Beam X + width"},
        "7296": {"comment":"Still on the page?"},
        "7299": {"comment":"Yes: store the new beam X"},
        "7302": {"comment":"No: carriage return"},
        "7305": {"comment":"And line feed"},
        "7308": {"synopsis":"VIDEO, write character on an attribute graphics page (mode 15), from VID_GR_CHAR. The\ncharacter goes to the text cursor (row IX-$53, column IX-$52, from 1), not the beam: its 9\nattribute bytes get the ink and/or paper nibble of IX-$51 and its 9 pixel bytes the font\nrows, as the attribute flags (IX-$55) allow: bit 7 set leaves the paper nibble, bit 6 the\nink nibble, bit 5 the pixel bytes; bit 4 inverts the character. The cursor then moves one\ncolumn right, wrapping to the next row and from the last row back to the first.\nEntry: B = the character, IX = the channel RAM.\nExit: A = 0, H = 0.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IY.","comment":"Text row"},
        "7311": {"comment":"DE = the row's entry in the line table"},
        "7314": {"comment":"Nine pixel lines per text row"},
        "7320": {"comment":"Plus the column"},
        "7327": {"comment":"Cell's offset in the page"},
        "7328": {"comment":"Font base"},
        "7332": {"comment":"Font column of the character"},
        "7337": {"comment":"BC = pixel area, DE = attribute area"},
        "7345": {"comment":"The cell's first attribute byte"},
        "7346": {"comment":"Attribute: paper high, ink low"},
        "7349": {"comment":"Bytes per line"},
        "7354": {"comment":"Which nibbles to write"},
        "7355": {"comment":"Flag bit 6: leave the ink?"},
        "7361": {"comment":"No: write the low nibble"},
        "7363": {"synopsis":"Adds the paper nibble to the write mask unless flag bit 7 is set.","comment":"Flag bit 7: leave the paper?"},
        "7369": {"comment":"No: write the high nibble"},
        "7371": {"synopsis":"Writes the attribute nibbles of the cell's nine lines.","comment":"B = nibble mask"},
        "7372": {"comment":"Keep page 1"},
        "7375": {"comment":"Page the attribute byte"},
        "7378": {"comment":"Nine lines"},
        "7380": {"synopsis":"Merges the new nibbles into one attribute byte and steps to the next line."},
        "7381": {"comment":"New attribute under the mask"},
        "7386": {"comment":"Next line"},
        "7387": {"comment":"Left page 1?"},
        "7392": {"comment":"Lines left"},
        "7396": {"comment":"Page 1 back"},
        "7399": {"comment":"Pixel area and cell offset"},
        "7401": {"comment":"Flag bit 5: leave the pixels?"},
        "7408": {"comment":"The cell's first pixel byte"},
        "7409": {"comment":"Nine lines"},
        "7412": {"comment":"Flag bit 4: inverse?"},
        "7418": {"comment":"Yes: complement every row"},
        "7419": {"synopsis":"Writes the cell's nine pixel bytes from the font, complemented by C.","comment":"$00 or $FF"},
        "7420": {"comment":"Page the pixel byte"},
        "7423": {"synopsis":"Writes one font row as a pixel byte and steps to the next line."},
        "7424": {"comment":"Font row"},
        "7427": {"comment":"Inverse when asked"},
        "7429": {"comment":"Next font row"},
        "7434": {"comment":"Next line"},
        "7435": {"comment":"Left page 1?"},
        "7443": {"comment":"Page 1 back"},
        "7446": {"synopsis":"Moves the text cursor one column right, wrapping to column 1 of the next row at the end of\nthe line.","comment":"Column"},
        "7449": {"comment":"Last column?"},
        "7452": {"comment":"Yes: next row"},
        "7455": {"comment":"And column 1"},
        "7456": {"synopsis":"Stores the new column and returns status 0.","comment":"Next column"},
        "7460": {"comment":"Status 0"},
        "7463": {"synopsis":"VIDEO, carriage return ($0D) on a graphics page, reached through the graphics escape table\nat $172B; also used by VID_GR_CHAR. Moves the beam to X = 0, or on an attribute page the\ntext cursor to column 1.\nEntry: IX = the channel RAM.\nExit: A = 0, H = 0.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Attribute graphics (mode 15)?"},
        "7469": {"comment":"Beam X = 0"},
        "7475": {"synopsis":"Attribute page: the text cursor goes to column 1.","comment":"Column 1"},
        "7479": {"comment":"Status 0"},
        "7482": {"synopsis":"VIDEO, line feed ($0A) on a graphics page, reached through the graphics escape table at\n$172D; also used by VID_GR_CHAR. Moves the beam down one character line (36 Y units, 72 in\n16/256 colours) if a character still fits below the new position; otherwise nothing changes.\nOn an attribute page the text cursor goes to the next row.\nEntry: IX = the channel RAM.\nExit: A = 0, H = 0.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Attribute graphics (mode 15)?"},
        "7488": {"comment":"-34 per row repeat"},
        "7491": {"comment":"Row repeat: 1, or 2 in 16/256 colours"},
        "7494": {"synopsis":"Doubles the room needed once per row repeat: the next line plus a character below it.","comment":"Line height plus a character"},
        "7497": {"comment":"As a Y offset"},
        "7498": {"comment":"Y of the next line's character bottom"},
        "7502": {"comment":"Below the bottom of the page?"},
        "7505": {"comment":"Yes: status 0, beam unchanged"},
        "7507": {"comment":"-18 per row repeat"},
        "7513": {"synopsis":"Doubles the line step once per row repeat.","comment":"One character line, 36 units"},
        "7516": {"comment":"As a Y offset"},
        "7517": {"comment":"X unchanged"},
        "7520": {"comment":"Beam one line down"},
        "7523": {"comment":"Store it and its address"},
        "7526": {"synopsis":"Moves the attribute page's text cursor to the next row, from the last row back to row 1.\nEntry: IX = the channel RAM.\nExit: A = 0, H = 0.\nChanges: AF, H.","comment":"Text row"},
        "7529": {"comment":"Last row?"},
        "7534": {"comment":"Yes: back to row 1"},
        "7535": {"synopsis":"Stores the new row and returns status 0.","comment":"Next row"},
        "7539": {"comment":"Status 0"},
        "7542": {"synopsis":"VIDEO, ESC F on a graphics page (fill), reached through the escape table at $16FF. Paints\nwith the ink every pixel connected to the beam that has the beam pixel's colour, one\nhorizontal span at a time. Each span found is pushed on the stack as a three-word entry (its\nleft end's video address, its byte count and mask, and a word of pixel count with direction\nbits 7-6), below an end marker of 0; VID_FILL_ROOM makes room by dropping finished entries\nwhen the stack nears STACK_LIMIT.\n1. Read the beam pixel's colour as a pixel byte ($BB94); stop at once if it is the ink.\n2. Choose the plot: XOR with (region XOR ink) on a pixel page, so a region pixel becomes\n   ink; PUT with the ink on an attribute page, with graphics flag bit 1 cleared for the\n   fill.\n3. Fill the seed row, then take entries off the stack and scan the rows below and above each\n   span.\nEntry: IX = the channel RAM.\nExit: A = 0.\nChanges: all main and alternate registers, IY, $BB47, $BB4D, $BB92-$BB9F.","comment":"Stack position of the fill"},
        "7546": {"comment":"Page 1 at the start"},
        "7551": {"comment":"Plot routine: XOR"},
        "7555": {"comment":"C = colour under the beam"},
        "7558": {"comment":"As a pixel byte"},
        "7561": {"comment":"The region colour"},
        "7564": {"comment":"Already the ink colour?"},
        "7567": {"comment":"Then nothing to fill"},
        "7571": {"comment":"Attribute graphics (mode 15)?"},
        "7577": {"comment":"Plot routine: PUT"},
        "7581": {"comment":"With the ink byte"},
        "7584": {"synopsis":"Sets up the seed span at the beam: an end marker, the plot value, the beam's byte and mask,\nand the bytes left to the line's end.","comment":"Seed entry word: no direction"},
        "7587": {"comment":"End marker of the span stack"},
        "7588": {"comment":"Beam X"},
        "7594": {"comment":"HL = beam X / 16: its byte column"},
        "7599": {"comment":"Plot value to $BB4D, beam position"},
        "7603": {"comment":"Page 1 = the beam's video segment"},
        "7605": {"comment":"Graphics flag bit 1 off for the fill"},
        "7613": {"comment":"Bytes per line"},
        "7617": {"comment":"Bytes from the beam to the line end"},
        "7621": {"comment":"Beam as a 16-bit video address"},
        "7624": {"comment":"Current row address"},
        "7627": {"comment":"Byte count and pixel mask"},
        "7631": {"comment":"One pass: the seed row itself"},
        "7635": {"synopsis":"Takes the next span entry off the stack and starts on the row below it; the end marker ends\nthe fill.","comment":"Entry word: direction and pixel count"},
        "7636": {"comment":"End marker: the fill is done"},
        "7639": {"comment":"Byte count and mask"},
        "7647": {"comment":"Left end of the span"},
        "7648": {"comment":"The row below"},
        "7656": {"comment":"Two passes: below, then above"},
        "7658": {"comment":"Below the last row of the page?"},
        "7664": {"comment":"Yes: only the row above"},
        "7667": {"synopsis":"Scans one row against a span: the pass count goes to the other register set first.","comment":"Pass count to the other set"},
        "7668": {"synopsis":"Scans the row at $BB99 under the span $BB9D/$BB97, unless the span came from that row.","comment":"Room on the stack?"},
        "7671": {"comment":"No: drop this span"},
        "7674": {"comment":"Entry word"},
        "7677": {"comment":"Pixel count without the direction bits"},
        "7685": {"comment":"DE = pixels in the span"},
        "7686": {"comment":"Direction known?"},
        "7690": {"comment":"Bit 7 against the pass"},
        "7696": {"comment":"The row it came from: skip it"},
        "7699": {"synopsis":"Tests the first pixel of the span on the new row; a region pixel there starts a span that\nmay reach further left.","comment":"Row address"},
        "7702": {"comment":"Page it into page 1"},
        "7709": {"comment":"First pixel the region colour?"},
        "7714": {"comment":"No: look along the span"},
        "7716": {"comment":"Bytes back to the line start"},
        "7722": {"comment":"No pixels to the left yet"},
        "7727": {"synopsis":"Fills leftwards while the pixels have the region colour, counting them in DE.","comment":"Region colour?"},
        "7732": {"comment":"No: left end found"},
        "7734": {"comment":"Fill this pixel"},
        "7737": {"comment":"Pixels filled to the left"},
        "7738": {"synopsis":"Steps one pixel left, into the previous byte when the mask wraps.","comment":"One pixel left in the byte"},
        "7742": {"comment":"Previous byte"},
        "7743": {"comment":"Left page 1?"},
        "7748": {"comment":"Until the line start"},
        "7750": {"synopsis":"Left end found: back to the leftmost filled pixel and its byte count to the line end.","comment":"Bytes to the line end"},
        "7756": {"comment":"Back one pixel right"},
        "7762": {"synopsis":"Pushes the new span's left end, byte count and mask, then fills right from the start pixel\nand completes the entry word.","comment":"Left end as a video address"},
        "7765": {"comment":"Entry: left end"},
        "7766": {"comment":"Entry: byte count and mask"},
        "7767": {"comment":"Entry: pixels to the left"},
        "7768": {"comment":"Back to the start pixel"},
        "7778": {"comment":"Fill right, counting in DE"},
        "7781": {"comment":"HL = pixels to the left"},
        "7782": {"comment":"Did it reach left?"},
        "7786": {"comment":"Yes: direction bit 7"},
        "7788": {"synopsis":"Adds the right part to the left count: the span's pixel count.","comment":"Total pixels of the new span"},
        "7790": {"synopsis":"Compares the new span's end with the end of the span it came from and sets the entry word's\ndirection bits.","comment":"Right end"},
        "7791": {"comment":"Pixels left of the parent span"},
        "7797": {"comment":"DE = right end"},
        "7798": {"comment":"HL = entry word"},
        "7799": {"comment":"Keep the comparison"},
        "7800": {"comment":"Bit 7 already set?"},
        "7806": {"comment":"Past the parent span?"},
        "7808": {"comment":"Carry = which pass"},
        "7814": {"comment":"$40 or $C0"},
        "7815": {"synopsis":"Puts the direction bits into the entry word.","comment":"Direction bits into the word"},
        "7817": {"synopsis":"Stores the entry word and ends the pass when the parent span is used up."},
        "7818": {"comment":"Entry word in place on the stack"},
        "7819": {"comment":"Beyond the parent: pass done"},
        "7821": {"comment":"Parent used up: pass done"},
        "7823": {"comment":"HL = right end, DE = parent left"},
        "7824": {"synopsis":"Walks on along the parent span looking for the next region pixel, which seeds another span.","comment":"Room on the stack?"},
        "7827": {"comment":"No: drop this span"},
        "7830": {"comment":"Count with a low byte of 0?"},
        "7835": {"synopsis":"Tests one pixel under the parent span.","comment":"Region colour?"},
        "7840": {"comment":"Yes: a new span"},
        "7842": {"comment":"Parent pixels left"},
        "7845": {"synopsis":"Steps one pixel right, into the next byte when the mask wraps.","comment":"One pixel right in the byte"},
        "7849": {"comment":"Next byte"},
        "7851": {"comment":"Left page 1?"},
        "7856": {"comment":"Page the next video segment"},
        "7861": {"synopsis":"A region pixel under the parent: starts a span there that only reaches right.","comment":"Undo the count adjustment"},
        "7866": {"synopsis":"Keeps the parent count left and pushes the new span's entry.","comment":"Parent pixels left"},
        "7871": {"comment":"Entry: left end"},
        "7875": {"comment":"Entry: byte count and mask"},
        "7876": {"comment":"Fill right, counting in DE"},
        "7879": {"comment":"Entry: pixel count"},
        "7882": {"synopsis":"High byte of the parent count: goes on while it is not exhausted.","comment":"Count high byte"},
        "7886": {"synopsis":"Ends a pass: the pass count is in the other register set.","comment":"Pass count set"},
        "7887": {"synopsis":"After the row below, scans the row above the span; after both, takes the next entry.","comment":"Both passes done?"},
        "7892": {"comment":"From the row below to the row above"},
        "7907": {"comment":"Above the first row of the page?"},
        "7916": {"comment":"Scan the row above"},
        "7919": {"synopsis":"Fills rightwards from HL/C while the pixels have the region colour, up to B bytes.\nEntry: HL = the pixel's address in page 1, C = its mask, B = bytes to the line end.\nExit: DE = pixels filled; NZ when a different colour stopped it.\nChanges: AF, B, C, DE, HL.","comment":"No pixels yet"},
        "7922": {"synopsis":"Tests and fills one pixel, then steps right.","comment":"Region colour?"},
        "7927": {"comment":"No: right end found"},
        "7928": {"comment":"Pixels filled"},
        "7929": {"comment":"Fill this pixel"},
        "7932": {"comment":"One pixel right in the byte"},
        "7936": {"comment":"Next byte"},
        "7937": {"comment":"Left page 1?"},
        "7942": {"comment":"Until the line end"},
        "7945": {"synopsis":"Checks that the stack has room for more span entries above STACK_LIMIT ($BFFA). When it does\nnot, it collects the garbage: it walks the entries from the oldest (just under the end\nmarker, at the stack position kept in $BB92) to the newest, keeps an entry only while the\nrow below or above its span still has a region pixel (VID_FILL_LIVE), packs the kept ones\ntogether and moves its own saved registers and return address up after them.\nExit: carry set when there was no room and nothing could be dropped; the caller then gives\nup that span.\nChanges: F; HL, DE, BC and the alternate BC are preserved, SP may move up.","comment":"Keep HL, DE"},
        "7947": {"comment":"22 bytes below SP"},
        "7951": {"comment":"STACK_LIMIT"},
        "7955": {"comment":"Still above it?"},
        "7957": {"comment":"Yes: room enough"},
        "7960": {"comment":"Keep both BC and page 1"},
        "7966": {"comment":"Fill stack position"},
        "7969": {"comment":"Top of the oldest entry"},
        "7972": {"comment":"DE = write pointer"},
        "7974": {"synopsis":"Takes the next entry at the read pointer, or finishes when it has reached the saved\nregisters.","comment":"BC = read pointer"},
        "7976": {"comment":"Top of the saved registers"},
        "7983": {"comment":"HL = read pointer"},
        "7985": {"comment":"Not there yet: test this entry"},
        "7987": {"comment":"Saved registers and return address"},
        "7990": {"comment":"Move them up after the kept entries"},
        "7993": {"comment":"SP below them"},
        "7995": {"comment":"Page 1 back"},
        "7999": {"comment":"Did the write pointer move?"},
        "8002": {"comment":"Carry: nothing was dropped"},
        "8006": {"synopsis":"Restores DE and HL and returns.","comment":"HL, DE back"},
        "8009": {"synopsis":"Tests one entry: it is live when the row below or the row above its span, inside the page,\nstill has a region pixel.","comment":"Read the entry"},
        "8012": {"comment":"The row below"},
        "8013": {"comment":"Past the last row?"},
        "8021": {"comment":"No: back to the row below"},
        "8022": {"comment":"Region pixel there?"},
        "8025": {"comment":"Yes: keep the entry"},
        "8027": {"synopsis":"Tests the row above the entry's span, if it is inside the page.","comment":"Read the entry again"},
        "8031": {"comment":"The row above"},
        "8033": {"comment":"Before the first row?"},
        "8040": {"comment":"No: region pixel there?"},
        "8043": {"synopsis":"Copies a live entry down to the write pointer, or skips a finished one.","comment":"Pointer set"},
        "8044": {"comment":"Six bytes an entry"},
        "8047": {"comment":"Finished: drop it"},
        "8049": {"comment":"Live: copy it to the write pointer"},
        "8054": {"synopsis":"Skips a finished entry.","comment":"Read pointer past it"},
        "8060": {"synopsis":"VID_FILL_ENTRY entered with the main register set active: fetches the read pointer from the\nother set first.","comment":"Read pointer set"},
        "8061": {"synopsis":"Reads a span entry at the read pointer (the alternate HL).\nExit: HL = the span's left end, DE = its pixel count (direction bits removed), A = its pixel\nmask, BC = bytes per line ($BB95).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Read pointer"},
        "8064": {"comment":"Left end address"},
        "8067": {"comment":"Over the byte count"},
        "8069": {"comment":"Pixel mask"},
        "8071": {"comment":"Count without the direction bits"},
        "8077": {"comment":"A = mask"},
        "8078": {"comment":"Bytes per line"},
        "8084": {"synopsis":"Looks along a span for a pixel that still has the region colour ($BB94).\nEntry: HL = the left end (16-bit video address), A = its pixel mask, DE = the pixel count.\nExit: Z when one is found, NZ when none.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL; page 1.","comment":"Pixel mask"},
        "8085": {"comment":"Region colour byte"},
        "8089": {"comment":"Page the span start"},
        "8092": {"synopsis":"Tests one pixel.","comment":"Region colour?"},
        "8095": {"comment":"Yes: Z"},
        "8096": {"comment":"Pixels left"},
        "8099": {"synopsis":"Steps one pixel right, into the next byte and segment when needed.","comment":"One pixel right in the byte"},
        "8103": {"comment":"Next byte"},
        "8104": {"comment":"Still in page 1?"},
        "8109": {"comment":"Next video segment"},
        "8117": {"synopsis":"Counts down the high byte of the pixel count; NZ when the whole span was tested.","comment":"Count high byte"},
        "8122": {"synopsis":"VIDEO, ESC E on a graphics page (ellipse), reached through the escape table at $16FD. Draws\nan ellipse round the beam with the X radius BC and the Y radius DE (graphics units),\nplotting with the current line mode and ink, then puts the beam back at the centre. It\ntraces one quadrant with integer arithmetic and plots four mirrored points at each step,\nskipping points off the page.\n1. Convert the radii to pixels (a, b, at least 1) and form the 32-bit products b², a² and\n   -a·b² ($BB6E-$BB89).\n2. Note the room round the centre ($BB4E-$BB54) and set the four point positions to (±a, 0)\n   ($BB56-$BB61).\n3. Step in Y while the decision term is negative (VID_ELL_PART1), then in X (VID_ELL_PART2)\n   until x reaches 0.\nEntry: BC = X radius, DE = Y radius, IX = the channel RAM.\nExit: A = 0, H = 0.\nChanges: all main and alternate registers, IY, $BB4E-$BB89.","comment":"Second set"},
        "8123": {"comment":"BC = beam X, DE = beam Y"},
        "8128": {"comment":"Keep the centre"},
        "8131": {"comment":"Keep page 1"},
        "8134": {"comment":"Keep the channel RAM pointer"},
        "8136": {"comment":"X radius in pixels"},
        "8141": {"comment":"Zero?"},
        "8145": {"comment":"At least 1"},
        "8146": {"synopsis":"Keeps the X radius in pixels (a) and turns the Y radius into pixel rows (b).","comment":"a, the X radius"},
        "8150": {"comment":"Y radius"},
        "8152": {"comment":"In pixel rows: / 4"},
        "8157": {"comment":"Zero?"},
        "8161": {"comment":"At least 1"},
        "8162": {"synopsis":"Forms the 32-bit squares and the product a·b².","comment":"b"},
        "8164": {"comment":"b squared"},
        "8167": {"comment":"b², low word"},
        "8171": {"comment":"b², high word"},
        "8174": {"comment":"a"},
        "8178": {"comment":"a squared"},
        "8181": {"comment":"a², low word"},
        "8185": {"comment":"a², high word"},
        "8190": {"comment":"a times b² (low word)"},
        "8197": {"comment":"a·b², low word"},
        "8201": {"comment":"HL = a, keep the carry-over"},
        "8202": {"comment":"a times b² (high word)"},
        "8209": {"comment":"Add the carry-over"},
        "8212": {"comment":"a·b², high word"},
        "8216": {"comment":"Second term starts at 0"},
        "8225": {"comment":"Negate a·b²: low word"},
        "8232": {"comment":"Decision term, low word"},
        "8235": {"comment":"Kept negated"},
        "8238": {"comment":"High word with the borrow"},
        "8247": {"comment":"Decision term, high word"},
        "8253": {"comment":"Channel RAM pointer back"},
        "8257": {"comment":"BC = largest X, DE = largest Y"},
        "8262": {"comment":"Rightmost pixel column"},
        "8268": {"comment":"Lowest pixel row"},
        "8275": {"comment":"BC = beam column, DE = beam row"},
        "8280": {"comment":"Rows above the centre"},
        "8284": {"comment":"Rows below the centre"},
        "8291": {"comment":"Columns left of the centre"},
        "8295": {"comment":"Columns right of the centre"},
        "8302": {"comment":"Offsets: y = 0"},
        "8305": {"comment":"x = a"},
        "8309": {"comment":"Main set"},
        "8310": {"comment":"a as bytes and leftover pixels"},
        "8315": {"comment":"Pixels per byte: 2 to the 3-mode"},
        "8320": {"comment":"256 colours: one pixel a byte"},
        "8323": {"synopsis":"Divides a by the pixels per byte, the remainder shifted into C.","comment":"a / pixels per byte"},
        "8331": {"comment":"Remainder to the bottom of C"},
        "8332": {"synopsis":"Rotates the remainder bits back to the bottom of C.","comment":"Leftover pixels"},
        "8336": {"synopsis":"Puts the four points at (centre + a, 0) and (centre - a, 0) and sets the step routines.","comment":"Kept for the right and the left"},
        "8340": {"comment":"Beam address, mask, plot routine"},
        "8343": {"comment":"Bytes per line for the steps"},
        "8347": {"comment":"Page 1 = the beam's video segment"},
        "8349": {"comment":"Beam as a 16-bit video address"},
        "8352": {"comment":"a bytes to the right"},
        "8354": {"comment":"Leftover pixels"},
        "8356": {"comment":"Any?"},
        "8360": {"synopsis":"Steps the right point one pixel right.","comment":"One pixel right"},
        "8365": {"synopsis":"Counts the leftover pixels to the right.","comment":"Pixels left"},
        "8367": {"synopsis":"Stores the right point as P1 and P4.","comment":"Mask of the right point"},
        "8368": {"comment":"P1: address"},
        "8371": {"comment":"P1: mask"},
        "8374": {"comment":"P4: address"},
        "8377": {"comment":"P4: mask"},
        "8380": {"comment":"Back twice a bytes: the left side"},
        "8386": {"comment":"Leftover pixels"},
        "8388": {"comment":"Twice, to the left of the centre"},
        "8394": {"synopsis":"Steps the left point one pixel left.","comment":"One pixel left"},
        "8399": {"synopsis":"Counts the pixels to the left.","comment":"Pixels left"},
        "8401": {"synopsis":"Stores the left point as P2 and P3 and draws the ellipse.","comment":"Mask of the left point"},
        "8402": {"comment":"P2: address"},
        "8405": {"comment":"P2: mask"},
        "8408": {"comment":"P3: address"},
        "8411": {"comment":"P3: mask"},
        "8414": {"comment":"Main step: move in Y"},
        "8420": {"comment":"Side step: move in X"},
        "8426": {"comment":"Plot the two start points"},
        "8429": {"comment":"Trace the quadrant"},
        "8432": {"comment":"Plot the end points at x = 0"},
        "8435": {"comment":"Channel RAM pointer back"},
        "8437": {"comment":"Page 1 back"},
        "8440": {"comment":"The centre"},
        "8442": {"comment":"Beam back to the centre"},
        "8445": {"synopsis":"First part of the quadrant: while the sum of the terms at $BB80 and $BB74 is negative, takes\na main step, and a side step too when the decision term at $BB86 has turned non-negative.","comment":"Sum of the two terms, low words"},
        "8453": {"comment":"High words"},
        "8462": {"comment":"Not negative: the second part"},
        "8465": {"comment":"Main step"},
        "8468": {"comment":"Decision term negative: again"},
        "8470": {"comment":"Side step as well"},
        "8475": {"synopsis":"Second part: corrects the decision term, swaps the X and Y variable sets (and with them the\nstep routines) and steps until x reaches 0.","comment":"Decision term"},
        "8481": {"comment":"+ the second term"},
        "8484": {"comment":"- the first term"},
        "8490": {"comment":"Swap the roles of X and Y"},
        "8493": {"synopsis":"Steps the second part until the x offset is 0.","comment":"x offset 0?"},
        "8497": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "8498": {"comment":"Main step"},
        "8501": {"comment":"Decision term not negative: again"},
        "8503": {"comment":"Side step as well"},
        "8508": {"synopsis":"One main step: plots the four points, moves them with the routine at $BB78 and updates the\nterms: $BB74 += $BB7A, then the decision term $BB86 += 2 x $BB74 - $BB7A.\nExit: NZ when the decision term is negative.\nChanges: all main and alternate registers but IX.","comment":"Plot the four points"},
        "8511": {"comment":"Main step routine"},
        "8514": {"comment":"Run it"},
        "8517": {"comment":"Second term"},
        "8520": {"comment":"+= its step"},
        "8527": {"comment":"Decision term"},
        "8531": {"comment":"+= twice the second term"},
        "8534": {"comment":"-= the step"},
        "8538": {"comment":"Decision term negative?"},
        "8541": {"synopsis":"One side step: moves the points with the routine at $BB84, then $BB80 += $BB6E and the\ndecision term $BB86 += 2 x $BB80.\nChanges: all main and alternate registers but IX.","comment":"Side step routine"},
        "8544": {"comment":"Run it"},
        "8547": {"comment":"First term"},
        "8550": {"comment":"+= its step"},
        "8556": {"comment":"Decision term"},
        "8560": {"comment":"+= twice the first term"},
        "8563": {"synopsis":"Swaps the 12 bytes at $BB7A-$BB85 with those at $BB6E-$BB79: the squares, the two terms and\nthe two step routine pointers, so the second part steps with X and Y exchanged.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Twelve bytes"},
        "8571": {"synopsis":"Exchanges one byte pair.","comment":"Exchange one byte"},
        "8581": {"synopsis":"Adds the 32-bit number at HL twice to the one at DE.\nEntry: HL, DE = the two numbers (low byte first).\nExit: A = the top byte of the result.\nChanges: AF, B.","comment":"Once, then once more"},
        "8584": {"synopsis":"Adds the 32-bit number at HL to the one at DE.\nEntry: HL, DE = the two numbers (low byte first).\nExit: A = the top byte of the result; HL and DE unchanged.\nChanges: AF, B.","comment":"No carry in"},
        "8589": {"synopsis":"Adds one byte pair with the carry.","comment":"Byte with the carry"},
        "8599": {"synopsis":"Subtracts the 32-bit number at HL from the one at DE.\nEntry: HL, DE = the two numbers (low byte first).\nExit: A = the top byte of the result; HL and DE 4 bytes on.\nChanges: AF, B, DE, HL.","comment":"No borrow in"},
        "8602": {"synopsis":"Subtracts one byte pair with the borrow.","comment":"Byte with the borrow"},
        "8610": {"synopsis":"Ellipse step routine (from $BB78 or $BB84, run through $B225): the y offset grows by 1, P1\nand P2 move one pixel row up and P3 and P4 one row down.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL; the alternate DE.","comment":"y offset + 1"},
        "8613": {"comment":"Bytes per line"},
        "8617": {"comment":"P1 up"},
        "8626": {"comment":"P2 up"},
        "8635": {"comment":"P3 down"},
        "8644": {"comment":"P4 down"},
        "8654": {"synopsis":"Ellipse step routine (from $BB84 or $BB78, run through $B225): the x offset shrinks by 1, P1\nand P4 move one pixel left and P2 and P3 one pixel right.\nChanges: AF, C, DE, HL; the alternate BC.","comment":"x offset - 1"},
        "8657": {"comment":"Bytes per line"},
        "8661": {"comment":"P1 one pixel left"},
        "8678": {"comment":"P2 one pixel right"},
        "8695": {"comment":"P3 one pixel right"},
        "8712": {"comment":"P4 one pixel left"},
        "8730": {"synopsis":"Plots the four points P1 (right, up), P3 (left, down), P2 (left, up) and P4 (right, down),\neach only when its offsets (x in the alternate BC, y in the alternate DE) stay inside the\nroom round the centre.\nChanges: all main registers; page 1.","comment":"Offsets set"},
        "8731": {"comment":"Room to the right"},
        "8737": {"comment":"x beyond it: skip P1"},
        "8739": {"comment":"Room above"},
        "8744": {"comment":"y beyond it: skip P1"},
        "8747": {"comment":"P1"},
        "8750": {"comment":"Page it"},
        "8753": {"comment":"Its mask"},
        "8757": {"comment":"Plot it"},
        "8761": {"synopsis":"Plots P3 (left, down) when it is on the page.","comment":"Room to the left"},
        "8767": {"comment":"x beyond it: skip P3"},
        "8769": {"comment":"Room below"},
        "8774": {"comment":"y beyond it: skip P3"},
        "8777": {"comment":"P3"},
        "8780": {"comment":"Page it"},
        "8783": {"comment":"Its mask"},
        "8787": {"comment":"Plot it"},
        "8790": {"synopsis":"Plots only P2 and P4: used at the start and the end, where the other two points coincide\nwith them (an XOR line mode would undo a second plot).","comment":"Offsets set"},
        "8791": {"synopsis":"Plots P2 (left, up) when it is on the page.","comment":"Room to the left"},
        "8797": {"comment":"x beyond it: skip P2"},
        "8799": {"comment":"Room above"},
        "8804": {"comment":"y beyond it: skip P2"},
        "8807": {"comment":"P2"},
        "8810": {"comment":"Page it"},
        "8813": {"comment":"Its mask"},
        "8817": {"comment":"Plot it"},
        "8821": {"synopsis":"Plots P4 (right, down) when it is on the page.","comment":"Room to the right"},
        "8827": {"comment":"x beyond it: skip P4"},
        "8829": {"comment":"Room below"},
        "8834": {"comment":"y beyond it: skip P4"},
        "8837": {"comment":"P4"},
        "8840": {"comment":"Page it"},
        "8843": {"comment":"Its mask"},
        "8847": {"comment":"Plot it and return"},
        "8850": {"synopsis":"P4 is off the page: back to the main set.","comment":"Main set back"},
        "8852": {"synopsis":"VIDEO, the last part of opening a text page (from $149E, when the page is not graphics).\nSets the alternate-colour bits of the page's line parameter block (IX-$13: MSBALT and LSBALT\nin the left margin byte for software text, ALTIND1 in the right margin byte for hardware\ntext), clears the colour bits, the scroll and cursor flags, sets the cursor character to\n$0E, clears the page with the cursor at row 1, column 1 and sets cursor colour 2.\nEntry: IX = the channel RAM.\nExit: A = 0, H = 0.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IY.","comment":"Video mode"},
        "8855": {"comment":"Hardware text (mode 0)?"},
        "8858": {"comment":"Left margin byte: MSBALT"},
        "8862": {"comment":"And LSBALT"},
        "8868": {"synopsis":"Hardware text: ALTIND1 in the right margin byte of the line parameter block.","comment":"Right margin byte: ALTIND1"},
        "8872": {"synopsis":"Clears the text page's flags and colour bits and sets the cursor character."},
        "8873": {"comment":"Auto-scroll on"},
        "8876": {"comment":"Cursor shown"},
        "8879": {"comment":"Character colour bits 0"},
        "8885": {"comment":"Cursor character"},
        "8890": {"comment":"Clear the page, cursor home"},
        "8893": {"comment":"Cursor colour 2 (as ESC M 2)"},
        "8898": {"synopsis":"VIDEO, clear page ($1A) on a text page, reached through the text escape table at $1715; also\nthe end of VID_TX_OPEN. Clears every row (last first, through VID_CLEAR_ROW) and puts the\ncursor at\nrow 1, column 1.\nEntry: IX = the channel RAM.\nExit: A = 0, H = 0.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IY.","comment":"Rows of the page"},
        "8901": {"synopsis":"Clears one row, from the last up to the first.","comment":"Clear row B"},
        "8909": {"comment":"Row 1, column 1"},
        "8912": {"synopsis":"Moves the text cursor and shows it there.\nEntry: B = the column, C = the row (both from 1), IX = the channel RAM.\nExit: A = 0, H = 0.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IY.","comment":"Column"},
        "8915": {"comment":"Row"},
        "8918": {"synopsis":"Notes the character under the cursor and its colour bits (IX-$3C, IX-$3D, through\nVID_SAVE_CELL),\nthen shows the cursor.","comment":"Character under the cursor kept"},
        "8921": {"synopsis":"Draws the cursor character (IX-$3E, colour bits IX-$3F) at the cursor, unless the cursor is\noff (IX-$43 not 0).\nExit: A = 0, H = 0.","comment":"Cursor off?"},
        "8925": {"comment":"Yes: nothing to draw"},
        "8927": {"comment":"Cursor character"},
        "8930": {"comment":"Cursor colour bits"},
        "8935": {"synopsis":"Takes the cursor off: puts back the character kept from under it (IX-$3C, colour bits\nIX-$3D).\nExit: A = 0, H = 0.","comment":"Kept colour bits"},
        "8938": {"comment":"Kept character"},
        "8941": {"synopsis":"Writes a character into the cell at the cursor: its code into the page's character map and,\non a software text page, its 9 font rows into the pixel bytes, with bits 7 and 0 of each row\ntaken from C. Runs on past $22FF.\nEntry: B = the character, C = the colour bits (bits 7 and 0), IX = the channel RAM.\nExit: A = 0, H = 0.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IY."},
        "8942": {"comment":"DE = code byte, HL = pixel byte"},
        "8946": {"comment":"The code byte"},
        "8947": {"comment":"Page it"},
        "8950": {"comment":"Store the character"},
        "8951": {"comment":"Page 1 back"},
        "8953": {"comment":"HL = the cell's first pixel byte"},
        "8954": {"comment":"DE = the character"},
        "8957": {"comment":"Its font column"},
        "8961": {"comment":"IY = the character's column in the font"},
        "8963": {"comment":"Bytes per scan line of the page"},
        "8966": {"comment":"Hardware text page (mode 0)?"},
        "8969": {"comment":"Then only the character map holds it"},
        "8971": {"comment":"Page in the cell's video segment"},
        "8974": {"comment":"Old page-1 segment kept"},
        "8975": {"comment":"Nine scan lines per character"},
        "8977": {"synopsis":"Loop: one scan line of the character cell: the font row (bits 6-1) with the attribute bits\nin C (bits 7 and 0) goes into the bitmap, then on to the next scan line and the next font\nrow."},
        "8978": {"comment":"Past the end of the segment?"},
        "8980": {"comment":"Then step to the next one"},
        "8983": {"comment":"Font row of the character"},
        "8986": {"comment":"Keep bits 6-1, add the attribute bits"},
        "8989": {"comment":"Into the bitmap"},
        "8990": {"comment":"Next font row is $80 on"},
        "8995": {"comment":"Next scan line of the cell"},
        "8997": {"comment":"All nine lines?"},
        "8999": {"comment":"Old page-1 segment"},
        "9000": {"comment":"Page 1 restored"},
        "9002": {"synopsis":"Returns OK with H = 0 without drawing: the cursor drawing at $22DD comes here when the\ncursor is off (IX-$43 not 0).","comment":"A = 0, OK"},
        "9003": {"synopsis":"Returns with H = 0 (A is 0 on both ways in). The hardware text page's way out of the cell\ndrawing, which stores only the character map."},
        "9005": {"synopsis":"Pages the video RAM segment that holds a 16-bit video address into page 1. The top two bits\nof H select segment $FC-$FF; H is changed to the matching page-1 address ($4000-$7FFF).\nEntry: HL = video address (bits 15-14 the segment).\nExit: HL = the address in page 1; A = the old page-1 segment (for OUT ($B1),A afterwards);\nflags unchanged.","comment":"Current page-1 segment"},
        "9007": {"comment":"Kept for the caller"},
        "9008": {"comment":"Bits 7-6 of H"},
        "9009": {"comment":"to bits 1-0"},
        "9011": {"comment":"Video segments are $FC-$FF"},
        "9013": {"comment":"Into page 1"},
        "9015": {"comment":"HL now in $4000-$7FFF"},
        "9019": {"comment":"A = old segment, flags as on entry"},
        "9021": {"synopsis":"Reads two words of the channel's RAM below IX.\nEntry: IX = the channel RAM; E = the low byte of the negative offset (D is set to $FF here),\ne.g. E = $C5 for IX-$3B.\nExit: BC = the word at IX+DE, DE = the word after it; HL points at D's byte.","comment":"HL = IX"},
        "9024": {"comment":"DE = $FF00 + E, a negative offset"},
        "9027": {"comment":"First word into BC"},
        "9031": {"comment":"Second word into DE"},
        "9033": {"synopsis":"Reads row A's entry in the page's row table: the word list at the pointer IX-$2E/IX-$2D, one\nword per text row (1-based). The entries are the rows' offsets into the character map;\nscrolling rotates them (VID_SCROLL_UP).\nEntry: A = row (1-based).\nExit: DE = the entry; HL = the address of its high byte.","comment":"Rows count from 1"},
        "9034": {"comment":"HL = the row table"},
        "9040": {"synopsis":"Reads word A of a word table (also an entry point of its own: the VIDEO escape dispatch at\n$150C reads its handler table through it).\nEntry: HL = the table, A = the index (0-255).\nExit: DE = the word; HL = the address of its high byte.","comment":"Two bytes per entry"},
        "9044": {"comment":"Index carried into D"},
        "9046": {"comment":"Entry's address"},
        "9047": {"synopsis":"Reads the word at HL into DE, leaving HL on its high byte. VID_CHAN_WORDS joins here for its\nsecond word."},
        "9051": {"synopsis":"Works out the two video addresses of the start of text row C (VID_ROW_PTRS with the row in\nA)."},
        "9052": {"synopsis":"Works out the video addresses of the start of text row A, from its row-table entry (offset\nn):\n1. HL = the character map's base (word IX-$30) + n: one byte per character.\n2. DE = the bitmap's base (word IX-$32) + 9 x n: nine scan lines per text row.\nEntry: A = row (1-based).\nExit: HL = character map address, DE = bitmap address."},
        "9055": {"comment":"Row offset n kept"},
        "9056": {"comment":"BC = IX-$32 (bitmap base), DE = IX-$30 (map base)"},
        "9061": {"comment":"HL = n"},
        "9062": {"comment":"Map base kept"},
        "9063": {"comment":"DE = n"},
        "9065": {"comment":"8n"},
        "9068": {"comment":"9n"},
        "9069": {"comment":"9n + bitmap base"},
        "9070": {"comment":"BC = map base"},
        "9071": {"comment":"Join: HL = n + map base"},
        "9073": {"synopsis":"Works out the video addresses of the cursor's cell.\nExit: HL = its bitmap address, DE = its character map address; BC = column - 1.\nChanges: A.","comment":"Cursor row (1-based)"},
        "9079": {"comment":"BC = column - 1"},
        "9081": {"comment":"Cursor column"},
        "9085": {"comment":"Map address of the cell"},
        "9086": {"synopsis":"Adds BC to DE and swaps: HL = old DE + BC, DE = old HL. The common end of VID_ROW_PTRS and\nVID_CURSOR_ADDR.","comment":"Bitmap address in HL"},
        "9087": {"comment":"plus BC"},
        "9089": {"synopsis":"VIDEO, text page code $19 (clear to the end of the line; reached from the escape handler\ntable at $16F3): clears the cursor's row from the cursor to the last column, then redraws\nthe cursor (VID_TX_GETCUR).","comment":"HL, DE = cursor cell, C = column - 1"},
        "9092": {"comment":"Clear the rest of the row"},
        "9095": {"comment":"Cursor back on"},
        "9098": {"synopsis":"Clears the whole of text row C: spaces into the character map and, on a software page, the\npaper attribute into its nine scan lines.\nEntry: C = row (1-based).","comment":"Addresses of the row's start"},
        "9101": {"comment":"HL = bitmap, DE = map"},
        "9102": {"comment":"From column 1"},
        "9105": {"synopsis":"Clears a row from column C+1 to its end.\n1. The character map gets spaces ($20 with the colour bit from IX-$40).\n2. A page with a bitmap (IX-$02 not 0) gets the attribute byte from IX-$41 in all nine scan\n   lines of those cells.\nEntry: HL = bitmap address, DE = character map address of the first cell; C = columns\nalready skipped.","comment":"Columns in a row"},
        "9108": {"comment":"minus the ones skipped"},
        "9109": {"comment":"BC = cells to clear"},
        "9112": {"comment":"HL = character map"},
        "9113": {"comment":"Space"},
        "9115": {"comment":"with the colour bit"},
        "9119": {"comment":"Fill the map"},
        "9124": {"comment":"Bitmap page?"},
        "9128": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "9129": {"comment":"Attribute fill byte"},
        "9132": {"comment":"Nine scan lines"},
        "9134": {"synopsis":"Loop: fills one scan line of the span with D, nine times over."},
        "9137": {"comment":"Fill one scan line"},
        "9141": {"comment":"Next scan line is a row width on"},
        "9147": {"comment":"All nine?"},
        "9151": {"synopsis":"Fills BC bytes of video RAM from HL with D, paging the video segment in (VID_PAGE_IN) and\nstepping into the next segment when HL runs past the end of one (VID_WRAP_PAGE1).\nEntry: HL = video address, BC = count (not 0), D = the byte.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL.","comment":"Page the first byte in"},
        "9154": {"comment":"Old page-1 segment"},
        "9155": {"synopsis":"Loop: one byte of VID_FILL.","comment":"Past the end of the segment?"},
        "9157": {"comment":"Then step to the next one"},
        "9160": {"comment":"Store the byte"},
        "9161": {"comment":"HL+1, BC-1"},
        "9163": {"comment":"More to fill?"},
        "9167": {"comment":"Restore page 1"},
        "9170": {"synopsis":"Takes 32 from both B and C: an escape sequence's position bytes are sent offset by 32.\nExit: Z set when C was 32 (the result 0).","comment":"B - 32"},
        "9174": {"comment":"C - 32 (Z when 0)"},
        "9179": {"synopsis":"Checks the two row bytes of the scrolling escapes (VID_SCROLL_UP, VID_SCROLL_DOWN): C =\nfirst row + 32, B = last row + 32. Rows must be 1 or more, first <= last, and last <= the\npage's row count (IX-$39).\nExit: OK: the cursor is taken off (VID_TX_HIDECUR), C = first row, B = last row, A = last -\nfirst (Z\nwhen one row), L = C.\nOn an error the caller's return address is dropped, so the escape handler ends with error\n$DA (.VROW).","comment":"Take the 32 offsets off"},
        "9182": {"comment":"First row 0?"},
        "9184": {"comment":"Last row"},
        "9185": {"comment":"below the first?"},
        "9188": {"comment":"Last row - 1"},
        "9189": {"comment":"beyond the page?"},
        "9194": {"synopsis":"Takes the cursor off (VID_TX_HIDECUR) and returns A = B - C, L = C, for a scroll of rows C\nto B\n(VID_ROW_RANGE's last part; the auto-scroll at $25CC enters here)."},
        "9195": {"comment":"Cursor off while rows move"},
        "9199": {"comment":"Rows to move"},
        "9201": {"comment":"L = first row"},
        "9203": {"synopsis":"Error exit of VID_ROW_RANGE: drops the return address into the escape handler and returns\nerror $DA (.VROW) to the handler's caller.","comment":"Back to the handler's caller"},
        "9204": {"comment":"Error $DA (.VROW)"},
        "9207": {"synopsis":"Sets up the row-table move for a scroll.\nEntry: A = number of rows to move, L = a row (1-based); one word (the caller's) on the stack\nunder the return address.\nExit: BC = 2A (bytes to move); HL = DE = the address of row L's entry high byte; the stack\nholds row L's entry above the caller's word.","comment":"Two bytes per row"},
        "9209": {"comment":"Row L"},
        "9212": {"comment":"Carry of 2A into B"},
        "9214": {"comment":"DE = row L's entry"},
        "9217": {"comment":"HL = its value"},
        "9218": {"comment":"Under the return address"},
        "9220": {"comment":"HL = DE = entry's high byte"},
        "9223": {"synopsis":"VIDEO, text page ESC U (code from the escape table at VID_CTRL_CODES): scrolls rows C-32 to\nB-32 up\nby one. The rows' entries in the row table move up a slot and the top row's entry goes to\nthe bottom, where that row is cleared, so no screen data is moved; the display list is then\nrebuilt (VID_LPT_UPDATE).\nEntry: C = first row + 32, B = last row + 32.","comment":"Check the rows, cursor off"},
        "9226": {"synopsis":"VID_SCROLL_UP after the row check: the auto-scroll ($25CF) jumps here with C = 1, B = the\nlast row and the Z flag from VID_ROWS_PREP.","comment":"C = last row (to clear)"},
        "9227": {"comment":"One row: only clear it"},
        "9229": {"comment":"First/last rows kept"},
        "9230": {"comment":"Slots of the first row"},
        "9233": {"comment":"From the next row's entry"},
        "9234": {"comment":"to this one's"},
        "9235": {"comment":"Entries up one slot"},
        "9237": {"comment":"Top entry to the bottom"},
        "9239": {"synopsis":"VIDEO, text page ESC D: scrolls rows C-32 to B-32 down by one, the bottom row's entry going\nto the top, where that row is cleared (as VID_SCROLL_UP the other way round).\nEntry: C = first row + 32, B = last row + 32.","comment":"Check the rows, cursor off"},
        "9242": {"comment":"One row: only clear it"},
        "9244": {"comment":"C = first row (to clear)"},
        "9245": {"comment":"Last row"},
        "9246": {"comment":"Slots of the last row"},
        "9249": {"comment":"Back to the previous entry's high byte"},
        "9251": {"comment":"Entries down one slot"},
        "9253": {"comment":"DE on the freed entry's low byte"},
        "9254": {"synopsis":"Common end of the two scrolls: the saved row entry goes into the freed slot, row C is\ncleared, the cursor is redrawn and the display list rebuilt (VID_LPT_UPDATE).","comment":"HL = the freed slot"},
        "9255": {"comment":"Saved row entry"},
        "9259": {"comment":"C = row to clear"},
        "9260": {"synopsis":"Clears row C, puts the cursor back (VID_TX_GETCUR) and rebuilds the display\n(VID_LPT_UPDATE).","comment":"Blank the new row"},
        "9263": {"comment":"Cursor on again"},
        "9266": {"comment":"Display list from the row table"},
        "9269": {"synopsis":"VIDEO, text page ESC S (auto-scroll on): clears the scroll-off flag IX-$42. ESC s enters at\n$2437, inside the LD HL,$FF3E: its bytes 3E FF are LD A,$FF there, so ESC s sets the flag to\n$FF (auto-scroll off). The flag stops VID_LINE_FEED scrolling at the last row.","comment":"A = 0 for ESC S"},
        "9270": {"comment":"ESC s enters at $2437: LD A,$FF"},
        "9273": {"comment":"Scroll-off flag"},
        "9276": {"comment":"A = 0, H = 0: OK"},
        "9279": {"synopsis":"VIDEO, text page ESC O: clears the cursor-off flag IX-$43 and draws the cursor\n(VID_TX_SHOWCUR).","comment":"Cursor-off flag cleared"},
        "9283": {"comment":"Draw the cursor"},
        "9286": {"synopsis":"VIDEO, text page ESC o: sets the cursor-off flag IX-$43 and puts the character under the\ncursor back (VID_TX_HIDECUR).","comment":"Cursor-off flag set"},
        "9290": {"comment":"Redraw the cell without it"},
        "9293": {"synopsis":"VIDEO, code $1E (cursor home): moves the cursor to row 1, column 1.","comment":"Column 1, row 1"},
        "9298": {"synopsis":"VIDEO, code $0B (cursor up): adds $FFFF to the cursor (row - 1). Code $16 (cursor down)\nenters at $2456, inside the LD IY,$0001: its bytes 21 01 00 are LD HL,$0001 there (row + 1).\nBoth join VID_CURSOR_MOVE.","comment":"Row - 1 (as a 16-bit add)"},
        "9301": {"comment":"Code $16 enters at $2456: LD HL,$0001"},
        "9307": {"synopsis":"VIDEO, code $08 (cursor left): column - 1 (H = $FF, L = 0). Code $09 (cursor right) enters\nat $245E, inside the LD DE,$0126: its bytes 26 01 are LD H,$01 there (column + 1). Both go\non into VID_CURSOR_MOVE.","comment":"Column - 1"},
        "9309": {"comment":"Code $09 enters at $245E: LD H,$01"},
        "9312": {"comment":"Row unchanged"},
        "9314": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor by HL (H columns, L rows, added to the position as one 16-bit number) if\nthe new place is on the page; then VID_SET_CURSOR.\nExit: carry set (A = 0) when it would leave the page and nothing changed.","comment":"Offset kept"},
        "9315": {"comment":"BC = row/column, DE = rows/columns"},
        "9321": {"comment":"New position"},
        "9322": {"synopsis":"Checks a cursor position and moves there: H = column, L = row (1-based), against D = columns\nand E = rows.\nExit: carry set when off the page; otherwise as VID_SET_CURSOR.","comment":"New column"},
        "9323": {"comment":"0-based"},
        "9324": {"comment":"beyond the last column?"},
        "9327": {"comment":"New row"},
        "9329": {"comment":"beyond the last row?"},
        "9332": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor to H = column, L = row: redraws the old cell without the cursor\n(VID_TX_HIDECUR),\nstores the position and draws the cursor at the new one (VID_TX_SETCUR)."},
        "9333": {"comment":"Old cell without the cursor"},
        "9336": {"comment":"BC = new position"},
        "9337": {"comment":"Store it, cursor on"},
        "9340": {"synopsis":"Cursor move refused: A = 0, H = 0, carry set."},
        "9341": {"comment":"Carry: off the page"},
        "9344": {"synopsis":"VIDEO, code $0D (carriage return): column 1 of the current row (a 0 row byte keeps the row).","comment":"Column 1, row 0 = unchanged"},
        "9349": {"synopsis":"VIDEO, ESC = (position): C = row + 32, B = column + 32; a 0 after the offset keeps that\ncoordinate.\n1. A text page moves the cursor there (VID_CURSOR_CHECK); off the page gives error $D9\n   (.VCURS).\n2. On a graphics page (bit 0 of IX-$02) the position goes to VID_ATTR_POS (bit 3 set) or\n   VID_BEAM_POS.","comment":"Take the 32 offsets off"},
        "9352": {"comment":"Graphics page?"},
        "9358": {"synopsis":"Fills a 0 in the new position (C = row, B = column) from the cursor's current one and moves\nthere (VID_CURSOR_CHECK).","comment":"New position kept"},
        "9359": {"comment":"BC = current row/column"},
        "9364": {"comment":"H = column, L = row"},
        "9365": {"comment":"Column 0?"},
        "9369": {"comment":"Then the current one"},
        "9370": {"synopsis":"Keeps the current row when the new one is 0.","comment":"Row 0?"},
        "9374": {"comment":"Then the current one"},
        "9375": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor to HL; error $D9 (.VCURS) when off the page.","comment":"Check and move"},
        "9378": {"comment":"Moved: OK"},
        "9379": {"synopsis":"Returns error $D9 (.VCURS): the position is off the page.","comment":"Error $D9 (.VCURS)"},
        "9382": {"synopsis":"ESC = on an attribute graphics page (bit 3 of IX-$02, the page's MODE_VID, is set only in\nmode 15): checks the position (C = row, B = column, 0 = keep the current one) against the\nbytes at IX-$39/IX-$38 and stores it in IX-$53 (row) and IX-$52 (column).\nExit: error $D9 (.VCURS) when beyond them.","comment":"Attribute page (mode 15)?"},
        "9386": {"comment":"No: move the beam"},
        "9389": {"comment":"Limits from IX-$39/IX-$38"},
        "9394": {"comment":"New position"},
        "9395": {"comment":"Row 0?"},
        "9399": {"comment":"Then the stored row"},
        "9402": {"synopsis":"Keeps the stored column when the new one is 0.","comment":"Column 0?"},
        "9406": {"comment":"Then the stored column"},
        "9409": {"synopsis":"Checks the attribute position against its limits and stores it.","comment":"Row beyond the limit?"},
        "9413": {"comment":"Column beyond?"},
        "9417": {"comment":"Store the new position"},
        "9423": {"comment":"OK"},
        "9426": {"synopsis":"ESC = on a pixel graphics page: turns a text position (C = row, B = column, 1-based) into\nbeam coordinates and moves the beam there (VID_BEAM_SET).\n1. X = 8 x (column - 1), doubled IX-$37 + 1 times (once more when bit 2 of IX-$02, the\n   page's MODE_VID, is set: the low-resolution modes 5 and 15).\n2. Y = the word at IX-$3F less (row - 1) x 18 x 2^(IX-$54): character rows of 9 lines\n   counted down from the top.\n3. A 0 row or column keeps the beam's current Y (word IX-$3B) or X (word IX-$3D).\n4. VID_CHECK_X and VID_CHECK_Y check the result; error $D9 (.VCURS) when off the page."},
        "9427": {"comment":"8 dots per column"},
        "9433": {"comment":"Column 1 or 0?"},
        "9439": {"synopsis":"Loop: adds 8 for each column past the first.","comment":"X = 8 x (column - 1)"},
        "9442": {"synopsis":"Sets the doubling count for X from IX-$37 and the mode's bit 2.","comment":"Doubling count"},
        "9445": {"comment":"Bit 2 of the mode?"},
        "9451": {"comment":"One more doubling"},
        "9452": {"synopsis":"Adds the last doubling of the count.","comment":"Plus one"},
        "9453": {"synopsis":"Loop: doubles X.","comment":"Scale X"},
        "9456": {"comment":"X kept"},
        "9457": {"comment":"Doubling count for Y"},
        "9460": {"comment":"-18: one character row"},
        "9463": {"synopsis":"Loop: doubles the row step -18.","comment":"Scale the row step"},
        "9466": {"comment":"DE = row step"},
        "9467": {"comment":"Y of the top row"},
        "9473": {"comment":"Row"},
        "9474": {"comment":"Row 1 or 0?"},
        "9480": {"synopsis":"Loop: one character row down from the top.","comment":"Step down one row"},
        "9483": {"synopsis":"Gets the beam's current position for the coordinates given as 0.","comment":"DE = Y"},
        "9484": {"comment":"BC = X"},
        "9485": {"comment":"Current beam position into the second set"},
        "9491": {"comment":"Back to the first set"},
        "9492": {"comment":"Row and column given"},
        "9493": {"comment":"Row 0?"},
        "9497": {"comment":"Then the current Y"},
        "9501": {"synopsis":"Keeps the current X when the column is 0.","comment":"Column 0?"},
        "9505": {"comment":"Then the current X"},
        "9509": {"synopsis":"Checks the beam coordinates (DE, BC) and moves the beam (VID_BEAM_SET).","comment":"Error $D9 (.VCURS) if off"},
        "9511": {"comment":"Check one coordinate"},
        "9515": {"comment":"Check the other"},
        "9519": {"comment":"Move the beam"},
        "9522": {"synopsis":"VIDEO, ESC ? (read the position): returns the cursor's row and column, each + 32, as C and B\nwith H = 2 (two bytes to give back). On a graphics page only an attribute page (bit 3 of\nIX-$02) answers, with the position at IX-$53/IX-$52; otherwise H = 0, nothing.","comment":"IX-$3B: cursor row and column"},
        "9524": {"comment":"Graphics page?"},
        "9530": {"comment":"Nothing to return"},
        "9532": {"comment":"Attribute page?"},
        "9536": {"comment":"No: none"},
        "9537": {"comment":"IX-$53: attribute position"},
        "9539": {"synopsis":"Returns the position word at IX+E-256 as C, B, each + 32, with H = 2."},
        "9542": {"comment":"Row + 32"},
        "9546": {"comment":"Column + 32"},
        "9550": {"comment":"Two bytes back"},
        "9552": {"comment":"OK"},
        "9554": {"synopsis":"Reads the cell under the cursor: its character code from the character map into IX-$3C and\nthe attribute bits 7 and 0 of its first bitmap line into IX-$3D, so the cell can be redrawn\nwhen the cursor leaves it.","comment":"HL = bitmap, DE = map address"},
        "9557": {"comment":"Page the bitmap in"},
        "9560": {"comment":"First scan line of the cell"},
        "9561": {"comment":"Restore page 1"},
        "9563": {"comment":"Its attribute bits 7 and 0"},
        "9567": {"comment":"HL = map address"},
        "9568": {"comment":"Page it in"},
        "9571": {"comment":"Character code"},
        "9572": {"comment":"Restore page 1"},
        "9574": {"synopsis":"Stores B as the character under the cursor (IX-$3C) and C as its attribute (IX-$3D); returns\nOK.","comment":"Character code"},
        "9577": {"comment":"Attribute"},
        "9580": {"synopsis":"Returns A = 0 (OK) with H = 0 (no bytes back)."},
        "9583": {"synopsis":"VIDEO, text page ESC I and ESC P (both reach this one entry): turns colour C into the page's\ncurrent colour bits.\n- Software text page (IX-$02 not 0): bits 2-1 of C to bits 0 and 7 of IX-$41, the attribute\n  byte the cells are drawn with.\n- Hardware text page: bit 1 of C to bit 7 of IX-$40, which is XORed into the character\n  codes.","comment":"IY = IX"},
        "9587": {"synopsis":"Stores colour C as bits in the byte at IY-$41 (or IY-$40 on a hardware text page);\nVID_ESC_COLOUR and VID_ESC_CURCOL share it.","comment":"Hardware text page?"},
        "9591": {"comment":"Three colour bits"},
        "9593": {"comment":"No: software page"},
        "9595": {"comment":"Target moves to IX-$40"},
        "9597": {"comment":"Only two colour bits"},
        "9598": {"synopsis":"Converts and stores the colour bits.","comment":"Colour bits of C"},
        "9600": {"comment":"Bit 1 to bit 7 (and bit 2 to bit 0)"},
        "9601": {"comment":"IY-$41: the colour byte"},
        "9606": {"synopsis":"VIDEO, text page ESC M (cursor colour): converts colour C as VID_ESC_COLOUR does into the\ncursor's colour, IX-$3F on a software page or bit 7 of IX-$3E (the cursor's character code)\non a hardware one, keeping the cursor's character, and redraws the cursor (VID_TX_SHOWCUR).","comment":"Cursor character kept"},
        "9609": {"comment":"IY = IX + 2: cursor's colour bytes"},
        "9617": {"comment":"Colour bits in"},
        "9621": {"comment":"Old cursor character"},
        "9622": {"synopsis":"VIDEO, text page ESC . (cursor character): C (bits 6-0) becomes the cursor's character,\nkeeping its colour bit 7, and the cursor is redrawn (VID_TX_SHOWCUR).","comment":"ESC . enters here, C = the new character"},
        "9625": {"comment":"Keep its colour bit"},
        "9627": {"comment":"Code without bit 7"},
        "9630": {"comment":"New cursor character"},
        "9633": {"comment":"Draw the cursor"},
        "9636": {"synopsis":"Returns the character under the cursor in B (from IX-$3C) with H = 1; reached from the VIDEO\nread character code at $14CD. Bit 7 of C is cleared.","comment":"Character under the cursor"},
        "9641": {"comment":"One byte back"},
        "9645": {"synopsis":"VIDEO, writes a printable character B at the cursor on a text page (from $154B):\n1. The colour bit IX-$40 is XORed into the code, and the code with the attribute IX-$41\n   becomes the cell under the cursor.\n2. Moving the cursor right draws the cell; at the last column it is drawn by a move to\n   column 1 instead and the cursor goes on down a row (VID_LINE_FEED).","comment":"Character"},
        "9646": {"comment":"with the colour bit"},
        "9650": {"comment":"Attribute"},
        "9653": {"comment":"As the cell under the cursor"},
        "9656": {"comment":"Right one column (draws the cell)"},
        "9659": {"comment":"Done unless at the last column"},
        "9660": {"comment":"Column 1 (draws the cell)"},
        "9663": {"synopsis":"VIDEO, code $0A (line feed): the cursor down a row; at the last row the page scrolls up\n(rows 1 to the last, VID_SCROLL_UP_GO) unless auto-scroll is off (IX-$42).","comment":"Down a row"},
        "9666": {"comment":"Done unless at the last row"},
        "9667": {"comment":"B = last row"},
        "9668": {"comment":"Auto-scroll off?"},
        "9672": {"comment":"Then stay"},
        "9674": {"comment":"From row 1"},
        "9676": {"comment":"Cursor off, row count"},
        "9679": {"comment":"Scroll up"},
        "9682": {"synopsis":"The built-in character set, packed as a bit stream (offsets $25D2-$2847). VIDEO's initialise\ncode reads it from VID_FONT_BITS on (VID_FONT_RESET sets HL one below; FONT_BITS fetches the\nbits, MSB first) and\nunpacks 128 characters, each nine rows of 8 dots, into the system segment at $B480 (one\ncolumn per character, rows $80 apart). Each character starts with a 4-bit header: bit 2 says\nwhether the two top rows are stored (else 0), bit 1 the same for the two bottom rows, and\nbits 3 and 0 choose how each of the other rows is coded (7 bits raw; 6 bits; or 3 bits\nexpanded to a symmetric pattern). Simulating the decoder over these bytes uses them all, up\nto 4 bits of $2847, and gives recognisable letters ('A', '!')."},
        "10312": {"synopsis":"SOUND, open and create channel (entries +2 and +4): allows one channel only, else error $E9\n(.2NDCH). Asks EXOS for a channel buffer (EXOS 27) of $0400 + 10n + 1 bytes, n = BUF_SND (at\nleast 2): the envelope store (10n + 1 bytes) then four 256-byte sound queues. Its page-1\naddress goes to $B2F4 (envelopes) and $B2F6 (queues), and the segment that holds it to\n$B2F3, which also marks the device as open.\nExit: A = 0 or the error.","comment":"Buffer segment: is a channel open?"},
        "10316": {"comment":"H non-zero too"},
        "10317": {"comment":"Error $E9 (.2NDCH)"},
        "10320": {"comment":"BUF_SND: envelope phases"},
        "10323": {"comment":"At least 2"},
        "10329": {"synopsis":"Works out the buffer size from the phase count in L.","comment":"HL = 2n"},
        "10330": {"comment":"DE = 2n"},
        "10332": {"comment":"8n"},
        "10334": {"comment":"10n"},
        "10335": {"comment":"10n + 1: envelope store"},
        "10337": {"comment":"Four 256-byte queues"},
        "10341": {"comment":"Total kept"},
        "10342": {"comment":"DE = total"},
        "10343": {"comment":"Allocate channel buffer"},
        "10345": {"comment":"BC = total"},
        "10346": {"comment":"DE = envelope store's size"},
        "10347": {"comment":"No room: error"},
        "10348": {"comment":"HL = IX"},
        "10351": {"comment":"Buffer start: IX less the total"},
        "10353": {"comment":"Envelope store"},
        "10356": {"comment":"Queues after it"},
        "10360": {"comment":"Note the segment"},
        "10362": {"synopsis":"SOUND, buffer moved (entry +26): adds the distance moved (BC) to the envelope and queue\npointers at $B2F4 and $B2F6 (ADD_BC_WORD, which keeps them in page 1) and notes the buffer's\nnew\nsegment (page 1's) in $B2F3.","comment":"Pointers at $B2F4 and $B2F6"},
        "10365": {"comment":"Z: keep them in page 1"},
        "10366": {"comment":"Envelope store pointer"},
        "10370": {"comment":"Queue pointer"},
        "10373": {"synopsis":"Stores the segment now in page 1 (the channel buffer's) in $B2F3 and returns OK.","comment":"The buffer's segment"},
        "10378": {"comment":"OK"},
        "10380": {"synopsis":"SOUND, write character (entry +14; write block at $11EA calls it for each byte). The state\nbyte $B380 says what B is:\n1. 0: a code. ESC ($1B) starts a sequence ($B380 = $1B); any other goes to SND_CONTROL.\n2. $1B: the letter after ESC, looked up in SND_ESC_TABLE: its handler goes to $B37C and\n   minus its parameter count to $B380 (unknown letter: error $E6, .ESC).\n3. Negative: one parameter byte, stored from $B381 on (pointer $B37E). When the count\n   reaches 0, the handler runs with A = B = the last byte.","comment":"Escape state"},
        "10384": {"comment":"No sequence going?"},
        "10387": {"comment":"Positive ($1B): the letter"},
        "10390": {"comment":"One parameter fewer"},
        "10392": {"comment":"Where it goes"},
        "10397": {"synopsis":"SOUND: a byte with no sequence going: ESC starts one, anything else is a control code\n(SND_CONTROL).","comment":"The byte"},
        "10398": {"comment":"ESC?"},
        "10400": {"comment":"No: a control code"},
        "10402": {"synopsis":"Stores B as the new escape state and points the parameter pointer $B37E at $B381; returns\nOK.","comment":"Z clear (B not 0), A = 0"},
        "10404": {"synopsis":"Stores B at HL, the next parameter place, and runs the sequence's handler when the count has\nreached 0 (Z).","comment":"Store the byte (or the new state)"},
        "10406": {"comment":"Next parameter's place"},
        "10409": {"comment":"More to come?"},
        "10410": {"comment":"Sequence complete: its handler"},
        "10413": {"comment":"A = the last byte"},
        "10415": {"synopsis":"Looks up the letter after ESC in SND_ESC_TABLE.","comment":"State byte kept"},
        "10417": {"comment":"Look the letter up"},
        "10425": {"comment":"On the match (or the last entry)"},
        "10426": {"comment":"Error $E6 (.ESC) if none"},
        "10430": {"comment":"Handler's low byte"},
        "10432": {"comment":"High byte"},
        "10434": {"comment":"Handler for the sequence"},
        "10438": {"comment":"Minus the parameter count"},
        "10441": {"comment":"Unknown letter: error"},
        "10442": {"comment":"Count into the state byte"},
        "10444": {"synopsis":"SOUND, control codes:\n- $1A (CTRL Z): every channel is cleared (SND_EACH_CHAN runs SND_FLUSH_CHAN for channels 3\n  to 0).\n- $18 (CTRL X): the envelope store is emptied (a 0 at its start).\n- $07 (CTRL G): the ping (SND_PING).\n- Others are ignored (OK).","comment":"Routine for each channel: clear it"},
        "10448": {"comment":"CTRL Z?"},
        "10450": {"comment":"Clear all four channels"},
        "10453": {"comment":"CTRL X?"},
        "10457": {"comment":"Envelope store"},
        "10460": {"comment":"0: no envelopes"},
        "10462": {"synopsis":"SOUND: CTRL G pings (SND_PING), any other code is ignored.","comment":"CTRL G ($07 - $18)?"},
        "10464": {"comment":"Ping"},
        "10467": {"comment":"Others ignored"},
        "10469": {"synopsis":"The SOUND escape sequences, read by SND_ESC_LETTER: three letters, then the three handlers'\nlow bytes, their high bytes, and minus the parameter count of each:\n- ESC E (define envelope): SND_ESC_E, 3 bytes (more are read by the handler).\n- ESC S (sound): SND_ESC_S, 10 bytes.\n- ESC Z (clear a queue): SND_ESC_Z, 1 byte."},
        "10481": {"synopsis":"SOUND interrupt, run for each channel (IX for SND_EACH_CHAN at $EBE3): when the channel is\nnot\nplaying (bit 7 of its state, IY+7, clear) and a sound is queued, takes it from the queue.\n1. The queue (256 bytes at the pointer $B2F6 + 256 x channel) holds 10-byte entries; IY+0\n   counts its bytes.\n2. Bytes 0-8 of the first entry are copied to IY+1..IY+9 (envelope number + 1, pitch, left\n   and right volume, style, channel, duration); byte 9 holds the flags.\n3. A sync number (flags bits 1-0) loads the shared sync counter $B2F8 when it is 0, or else\n   counts it down, and the sound then waits (state $81) for the counter to reach 0;\n   otherwise the state is $80.\n4. IY+10 (the envelope's phase) is cleared and the rest of the queue moves down.\nEntry: IY = HL = the channel's block ($B2FB + 32 x channel); C = the channel number.","comment":"Still playing?"},
        "10486": {"comment":"Bytes queued"},
        "10487": {"comment":"A whole entry?"},
        "10490": {"comment":"One fewer"},
        "10491": {"comment":"DE = IY+1"},
        "10494": {"comment":"BC = 256 x channel"},
        "10496": {"comment":"Queue area"},
        "10499": {"comment":"This channel's queue"},
        "10500": {"comment":"Entry's flags byte"},
        "10505": {"comment":"Back to the entry"},
        "10507": {"comment":"Sync number?"},
        "10511": {"synopsis":"SOUND: a sound with a sync number: loads the shared counter $B2F8 or counts it down, and\nmarks the sound as waiting (bit 0 of its state).","comment":"Sync number kept"},
        "10512": {"comment":"Shared sync counter"},
        "10515": {"comment":"Count it down"},
        "10516": {"comment":"Was running: store it"},
        "10519": {"comment":"Was 0: load the sync number"},
        "10520": {"synopsis":"Stores the sync counter."},
        "10523": {"comment":"Wait for sync"},
        "10525": {"synopsis":"Copies the sound from the queue into the channel block with its new state.","comment":"Playing"},
        "10527": {"comment":"Entry start kept"},
        "10528": {"comment":"Nine bytes to the channel block"},
        "10530": {"comment":"Past the flags byte"},
        "10531": {"comment":"New state"},
        "10535": {"comment":"Phase 0: envelope not started"},
        "10537": {"comment":"Rest of the queue"},
        "10540": {"comment":"Empty?"},
        "10542": {"comment":"Move it down"},
        "10545": {"synopsis":"SOUND interrupt, run for each channel (IX for SND_EACH_CHAN at $EBEA), 50 times a second:\nplays the\nchannel's current sound.\n1. Nothing when neither bit 7 (playing) nor bit 5 (envelope running) of the state IY+7 is\n   set.\n2. A sound starting (IY+10 = 0) waits while bit 0 (sync) is set and $B2F8 is not 0. It then\n   starts its envelope (SND_PHASE) or, with envelope number 0 (255 as sent, the beep), sets\n   both amplitudes to $40.\n3. Unless the envelope is silent (bit 6), steps the pitch and the two amplitudes along the\n   current phase (SND_ENV_STEP) and writes the tone and volumes (SND_DAVE).\n4. Counts the duration down (SND_DURATION).\nEntry: IY = the channel block; $B2FA = the channel number.","comment":"Playing or envelope running?"},
        "10550": {"comment":"Neither: nothing"},
        "10551": {"comment":"Envelope phase"},
        "10555": {"comment":"Already started"},
        "10557": {"comment":"Waiting for sync?"},
        "10563": {"comment":"Sync counter"},
        "10567": {"comment":"Not yet"},
        "10568": {"comment":"Synced: start it"},
        "10572": {"synopsis":"Starts a sound: with envelope number 0 (the beep) both amplitudes become $40, else they\nstart at 0 and the envelope's first phase is loaded (SND_PHASE).","comment":"Envelope 0 (the beep)?"},
        "10577": {"comment":"Fixed amplitude $40"},
        "10579": {"synopsis":"Sets both current amplitudes to A and, for an envelope, loads its first phase.","comment":"Left amplitude"},
        "10582": {"comment":"Right amplitude"},
        "10585": {"comment":"Envelope: its first phase"},
        "10588": {"synopsis":"SOUND: a silent envelope (state bit 6) only counts the duration; the beep goes straight to\nSND_DAVE; an envelope steps first (SND_ENV_STEP).","comment":"Envelope silent?"},
        "10592": {"comment":"Then only the duration"},
        "10595": {"comment":"Envelope number"},
        "10599": {"comment":"The beep: no stepping"},
        "10602": {"synopsis":"Steps the envelope's current phase by one tick, spreading each change evenly over the\nphase's duration D (IY+$0D/$0E) with remainders:\n1. Pitch (IY+2/3): the accumulator IY+$1D/$1E gains |pitch change| / 16 (IY+$1B/$1C), and\n   for each D it holds the pitch moves 16 in the change's direction (IY+$1F).\n2. Each amplitude (IY+$11, $12): its accumulator (IY+$15/$17, $16/$18) gains |change|\n   (IY+$13, $14), and for each D it holds the amplitude moves 1 (IY+$19, $1A), kept in 0-63.\n3. The phase's tick count IY+$0F/$10 runs down; at 0 the next phase is loaded (SND_PHASE).","comment":"Pitch"},
        "10608": {"comment":"Pitch step: 16 up or down"},
        "10611": {"comment":"Sign into D"},
        "10615": {"comment":"Second set: the remainder"},
        "10616": {"comment":"Pitch accumulator"},
        "10622": {"comment":"|Pitch change|"},
        "10628": {"comment":"Divided by 16"},
        "10630": {"synopsis":"Loop: divides the pitch change by 16."},
        "10636": {"comment":"Accumulate"},
        "10637": {"comment":"Phase duration"},
        "10643": {"synopsis":"Loop: one pitch step for each phase duration the accumulator holds.","comment":"A whole step?"},
        "10645": {"comment":"No"},
        "10647": {"comment":"Pitch one step on"},
        "10650": {"comment":"Again"},
        "10652": {"synopsis":"Stores the pitch accumulator's remainder and the new pitch.","comment":"Remainder back"},
        "10653": {"comment":"Store it"},
        "10659": {"comment":"New pitch"},
        "10667": {"comment":"Block pointer kept"},
        "10669": {"comment":"Two amplitudes"},
        "10671": {"synopsis":"Loop: steps one amplitude (left, then right)."},
        "10672": {"comment":"Current amplitude"},
        "10675": {"comment":"Its accumulator"},
        "10681": {"comment":"|Amplitude change|"},
        "10686": {"comment":"Accumulate"},
        "10687": {"comment":"Step +1 or -1"},
        "10690": {"synopsis":"Loop: one amplitude step for each phase duration the accumulator holds; a step out of 0-63\nis undone.","comment":"A whole step?"},
        "10693": {"comment":"No"},
        "10695": {"comment":"Amplitude one step"},
        "10696": {"comment":"Still in 0-63?"},
        "10700": {"comment":"Else undo the step"},
        "10703": {"synopsis":"Stores the amplitude and its accumulator's remainder.","comment":"Remainder back"},
        "10704": {"comment":"New amplitude"},
        "10707": {"comment":"Accumulator"},
        "10714": {"comment":"Next amplitude's bytes"},
        "10716": {"comment":"Both done?"},
        "10719": {"comment":"Block pointer back"},
        "10721": {"comment":"Ticks left in the phase"},
        "10727": {"comment":"One fewer"},
        "10734": {"comment":"Phase over?"},
        "10736": {"comment":"Current phase number"},
        "10739": {"comment":"Load the next phase"},
        "10742": {"synopsis":"Works the channel's pitch and amplitudes into the DAVE register image ($B2E3, written to\nports $A0-$AF by the interrupt):\n1. Pitch high byte = quarter-tone number: its octave (number / 24) and the quarter tone's\n   period from SND_PERIODS, less the low byte's top nibble in sixteenths of the gap to the\n   next entry, halved once for each octave.\n2. Each volume = amplitude (0-63) x the sound's volume (IY+4, IY+5), top byte; the left one\n   goes to $B2EB + channel (port $A8 +), the right one 4 on (port $AC +).\n3. The tone channels get the period - 1 with the style's top nibble in the period's high\n   nibble (ports $A0 + 2 x channel); channel 3, the noise, gets the style byte (port $A6).","comment":"Quarter-tone number"},
        "10745": {"comment":"24 to an octave"},
        "10748": {"comment":"B = 0"},
        "10749": {"synopsis":"Loop: counts the octaves in the quarter-tone number.","comment":"Count the octaves"},
        "10753": {"comment":"Quarter tone in the octave"},
        "10754": {"comment":"Octave + 1 kept"},
        "10755": {"comment":"Word index"},
        "10757": {"comment":"Period table"},
        "10761": {"comment":"This quarter tone's period"},
        "10764": {"comment":"kept"},
        "10766": {"comment":"The next one's"},
        "10769": {"comment":"HL = this period"},
        "10770": {"comment":"Gap to the next"},
        "10772": {"comment":"DE = gap, HL = period"},
        "10773": {"comment":"Fraction: pitch low byte"},
        "10780": {"comment":"Top nibble, 0-15"},
        "10783": {"comment":"Fraction accumulator"},
        "10785": {"synopsis":"Loop: one sixteenth of the gap per step of the fraction nibble, taking 1 from the period for\neach 16 the accumulator passes.","comment":"Next sixteenth"},
        "10787": {"comment":"Fraction done?"},
        "10791": {"comment":"Add the gap"},
        "10792": {"synopsis":"Loop: takes 1 from the period for each 16 in the fraction accumulator.","comment":"A sixteenth's worth"},
        "10796": {"comment":"Period one less"},
        "10799": {"synopsis":"Halves the period once for each octave above the first.","comment":"D = octave + 1"},
        "10800": {"synopsis":"Loop: halves the period.","comment":"Octaves done?"},
        "10803": {"comment":"Halve the period"},
        "10809": {"synopsis":"Works the volumes out and stores the volumes and the tone (or noise) register values.","comment":"Period kept"},
        "10810": {"comment":"Left volume"},
        "10813": {"comment":"times the left amplitude"},
        "10819": {"comment":"kept"},
        "10820": {"comment":"Right volume"},
        "10823": {"comment":"times the right amplitude"},
        "10829": {"comment":"D = left product"},
        "10830": {"comment":"E = right volume"},
        "10831": {"comment":"Channel number"},
        "10835": {"comment":"Volumes into the image"},
        "10838": {"comment":"Back from the right volume"},
        "10842": {"comment":"to the channel's tone pair"},
        "10844": {"comment":"Period"},
        "10845": {"comment":"Register value is period - 1"},
        "10846": {"comment":"Noise channel (3)?"},
        "10848": {"comment":"Style byte"},
        "10851": {"comment":"Noise: style to the noise register"},
        "10853": {"comment":"Style's top nibble"},
        "10855": {"comment":"with the period's high bits"},
        "10856": {"comment":"Period low"},
        "10858": {"synopsis":"Stores the high register byte (the tone's high byte or the noise style)."},
        "10859": {"synopsis":"Counts the sound's duration (IY+8/9) down while it plays (state bit 7). At 0:\n- The beep (envelope 0) ends: state 0.\n- An envelope sound moves to its release: the state is rotated and its bits 6 and 5 flipped\n  (playing becomes envelope running, which lets the next queued sound start), and an\n  envelope not yet in its release phases jumps to the first of them (SND_PHASE with A =\n  IY+$0C).","comment":"Playing?"},
        "10864": {"comment":"Duration"},
        "10870": {"comment":"One tick fewer"},
        "10877": {"comment":"Ended?"},
        "10880": {"comment":"Envelope number"},
        "10883": {"comment":"The beep: state 0"},
        "10885": {"comment":"State"},
        "10888": {"comment":"Bit 7 to 6, 5 to 4, "},
        "10889": {"comment":"Flip bits 6 and 5"},
        "10891": {"synopsis":"Stores the channel's new state."},
        "10894": {"comment":"Nothing left: done"},
        "10895": {"comment":"Phases before the release"},
        "10898": {"comment":"Already past them?"},
        "10902": {"synopsis":"Loads envelope phase A + 1 (A is 0-based) of the sound's envelope into the channel block.\n1. Looks the envelope up in the store at $B2F4: entries of [number + 1][length][phase\n   count][release][6 bytes per phase], ended by 0. Not there: the sound turns silent (state\n   bit 5 cleared, bit 6 set).\n2. Past the envelope's last phase: the same.\n3. Clears IY+$13..$1F, stores the phase count (IY+$0B) and release (IY+$0C), and from the\n   phase's 6 bytes the pitch change (size IY+$1B/$1C, step +-16 at IY+$1F), the amplitude\n   changes (sizes IY+$13, $14, steps +-1 at IY+$19, $1A) and the duration (IY+$0D/$0E and\n   the counter IY+$0F/$10). A duration of 0 becomes $FFFF.\nEntry: IY = the channel block, A = phase number - 1.","comment":"Block pointer kept"},
        "10904": {"comment":"1-based phase"},
        "10905": {"comment":"Current phase"},
        "10908": {"comment":"Envelope store"},
        "10911": {"comment":"D = 0 for the length"},
        "10913": {"synopsis":"Loop: one entry of the envelope store.","comment":"Entry's number"},
        "10914": {"comment":"End of the store?"},
        "10917": {"comment":"This sound's envelope?"},
        "10922": {"comment":"Length byte"},
        "10924": {"comment":"Next entry"},
        "10927": {"synopsis":"The envelope is missing or ended: clears state bit 5 and sets bit 6 (silent until the\nduration ends)."},
        "10929": {"comment":"Envelope over"},
        "10933": {"comment":"Silent"},
        "10938": {"synopsis":"The envelope is found (HL on its entry): loads the phase.","comment":"13 bytes"},
        "10940": {"synopsis":"Loop: clears IY+$13..$1F."},
        "10947": {"comment":"Phase count"},
        "10950": {"comment":"into IY+$0B"},
        "10954": {"comment":"Release"},
        "10956": {"comment":"into IY+$0C"},
        "10959": {"comment":"Phase number"},
        "10962": {"comment":"0-based"},
        "10963": {"comment":"Past the last phase?"},
        "10966": {"comment":"2n"},
        "10968": {"comment":"4n"},
        "10969": {"comment":"6n: six bytes a phase"},
        "10971": {"comment":"The phase"},
        "10973": {"comment":"Pitch change"},
        "10976": {"comment":"Negative?"},
        "10978": {"comment":"Step +16"},
        "10983": {"comment":"HL = 0"},
        "10985": {"comment":"DE = -change"},
        "10988": {"comment":"Step -16"},
        "10991": {"synopsis":"Stores the pitch change's step and size.","comment":"IY+$1F: pitch step"},
        "10994": {"comment":"IY+$1B/$1C: size of the change"},
        "11000": {"comment":"Two amplitude changes"},
        "11002": {"synopsis":"Loop: the left, then the right amplitude change, as a size and a step of +1 or -1."},
        "11003": {"comment":"Change"},
        "11004": {"comment":"Negative?"},
        "11006": {"comment":"Step +1"},
        "11010": {"comment":"Its size"},
        "11012": {"comment":"Step -1"},
        "11014": {"synopsis":"Stores an amplitude change's step and size.","comment":"IY+$19/$1A: step"},
        "11017": {"comment":"IY+$13/$14: size"},
        "11024": {"comment":"Duration's two bytes"},
        "11026": {"synopsis":"Loop: the phase's duration into both its value and its counter."},
        "11028": {"comment":"Duration byte"},
        "11029": {"comment":"IY+$0D/$0E: duration"},
        "11032": {"comment":"IY+$0F/$10: ticks left"},
        "11039": {"comment":"Block pointer back"},
        "11041": {"comment":"Duration 0?"},
        "11043": {"comment":"Then $FFFF"},
        "11051": {"synopsis":"Multiplies two bytes.\nEntry: C, E = the factors; D = 0.\nExit: HL = C x E; B = 0, C = 0.","comment":"HL = 0"},
        "11053": {"comment":"Eight bits of C"},
        "11055": {"synopsis":"Loop: one bit of the multiplier.","comment":"Shift the product"},
        "11056": {"comment":"Next bit of C"},
        "11060": {"comment":"Set: add E"},
        "11061": {"synopsis":"Counts the multiplier's bits."},
        "11064": {"synopsis":"Tone periods for the 24 quarter tones of an octave and the next octave's first (25 words,\n$0FD2 down to $07E9, half of it), read by SND_DAVE in pairs to interpolate between\nneighbours; higher octaves halve them."},
        "11114": {"synopsis":"SOUND's device pseudo-descriptor (ROM form), linked from VIDEO's: XX_NEXT $7054 (KEYBOARD's\nXX_SIZE in page 1), XX_RAM $FFFE (-2), DD_TYPE 0, DD_IRQFLAG $20 (the video interrupt, 50\ntimes a second), DD_FLAGS 0, DD_TAB $6B7C with segment byte $FE, DD_UNIT_COUNT 0, DD_NAME 5\n'SOUND', XX_SIZE 13.","comment":"XX_NEXT: KEYBOARD's descriptor; XX_RAM -2"},
        "11118": {"comment":"DD_TYPE, DD_IRQFLAG (video), DD_FLAGS"},
        "11121": {"comment":"DD_TAB"},
        "11123": {"comment":"Segment byte, unit count"},
        "11125": {"comment":"DD_NAME: 5, 'SOUND'"},
        "11131": {"comment":"XX_SIZE"},
        "11132": {"synopsis":"SOUND's entry-point table (DD_TAB): interrupt SND_INTERRUPT, open and create SND_OPEN, close\nand\ndestroy SND_CLOSE, read character and read block ERR_NOFN (error $E7, .NOFN), write\ncharacter\nSND_WRITE_CHAR, write block $11EA, read and set channel status ERR_NOFN, special function\nSND_SPECIAL, initialise SND_CLOSE, buffer moved SND_BUF_MOVED."},
        "11160": {"synopsis":"SOUND, special function (entry +22): none exists; returns error $EA (.ISPEC).","comment":"Error $EA (.ISPEC)"},
        "11163": {"synopsis":"Points IY and HL at sound channel C's 32-byte block, $B2FB + 32 x C.\nEntry: C = channel (0-3).\nExit: IY = HL = the block; D = 0, E = 32C.","comment":"32 x channel"},
        "11169": {"comment":"Channel blocks"},
        "11173": {"comment":"IY = HL"},
        "11177": {"synopsis":"Runs the routine at IX once for each SOUND channel, 3 down to 0. Before each call C and\n$B2FA hold the channel number and IY = HL = its 32-byte block at $B2FB + 32 x channel (from\nSND_CHAN_BLOCK). The interrupt calls it with SND_NEXT_SOUND and SND_TICK; CTRL Z (written to\nSOUND) with\nSND_FLUSH_CHAN, which empties every queue.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IY, whatever the routine changes.","comment":"Count past channel 3"},
        "11179": {"synopsis":"Loop: one channel per pass, until channel 0 is done.","comment":"Next channel"},
        "11180": {"comment":"Keep the count"},
        "11181": {"comment":"C = the channel"},
        "11182": {"comment":"$B2FA = the channel being worked on"},
        "11185": {"comment":"IY = HL = its block"},
        "11188": {"comment":"Run the routine in IX"},
        "11192": {"comment":"Down to channel 0?"},
        "11195": {"synopsis":"Jumps to IX: SND_EACH_CHAN calls this to call the routine in IX."},
        "11197": {"synopsis":"SOUND, ESC Z n: empties the queue of channel n (0-2 tone, 3 noise). Reached from the escape\ntable at SND_ESC_TABLE once the parameter byte has arrived, with A = n. Finds the channel's\nblock,\nthen falls into SND_FLUSH_CHAN; C is not set on this path, so the volume copies cleared\nthere are the ones C selects as it arrives.","comment":"A = the channel: IY = HL = its block"},
        "11200": {"synopsis":"Empties the queue of channel C: its block's byte count (HL = IY = the block) and state flags\n(IY+7) become 0, $B2F8 (the sync counter: SND_NEXT_SOUND loads it from a sound's style bits\n0-1 and counts it down; a channel with state bit 0 waits while it is not 0) is cleared, and\nthe channel's left and right volume copies ($A8 + C, $AC + C) are zeroed by falling into\nSND_SET_VOL with D = E = 0. Used by CTRL Z through SND_EACH_CHAN, and by ESC S when its flag\nbyte has bit 7 set.","comment":"Queue empty: its byte count 0"},
        "11202": {"comment":"Channel state flags clear"},
        "11205": {"comment":"No sounds waiting to start together"},
        "11208": {"comment":"B = D = E = 0"},
        "11211": {"synopsis":"Sets the copies of channel C's volume registers: left ($B2EB + C, port $A8 + C) to D, right\n($B2EF + C, port $AC + C) to E.\nEntry: B = 0. Also reached from $2A53.","comment":"Left volume copy of channel C ($A8 + C)"},
        "11215": {"comment":"Set it"},
        "11216": {"comment":"On to $AC + C"},
        "11220": {"comment":"Right volume copy"},
        "11222": {"synopsis":"SOUND, interrupt (entry +0): runs on every video interrupt (DD_IRQFLAG $20), 50 times a\nsecond.\n1. Clears the 16 copies of the DAVE sound registers at $B2E3-$B2F2 (ports $A0-$AF).\n2. If a SOUND channel is open ($B2F3 = the segment of its RAM, paged into page 1), runs\n   SND_NEXT_SOUND for each channel, then SND_TICK for each (SND_EACH_CHAN), which rebuild\n   the copies\n   from the queues.\n3. Counts a ping down (SND_INT_PING), then writes all 16 registers out (SND_OUT_REGS).\nSo the sound registers are rewritten on every interrupt, whatever else wrote to them.","comment":"16 register copies"},
        "11224": {"comment":"All 0"},
        "11227": {"comment":"Segment of the SOUND channel's RAM"},
        "11230": {"comment":"Page 1 = that segment"},
        "11232": {"comment":"No channel open?"},
        "11235": {"comment":"First pass per channel"},
        "11239": {"comment":"For channels 3-0"},
        "11242": {"comment":"Second pass per channel"},
        "11246": {"comment":"For channels 3-0"},
        "11249": {"synopsis":"While a ping sounds ($B2F9 not 0), sets the next lower volume (SND_PING_VOL); 1 ends it.","comment":"Ping volume"},
        "11252": {"comment":"Still sounding?"},
        "11253": {"comment":"Yes: one lower"},
        "11256": {"comment":"Write the registers out"},
        "11258": {"synopsis":"SOUND, close and destroy channel, and initialise (entries +6, +8 and +24): clears all $9E\nbytes of the SOUND RAM from $B2E3 to $B380 ($B2F3 = 0: no channel open, no ping, no escape\nin progress), then writes the cleared register copies to the sound chip.\nThe LD DE,$1006 at $2BFC hides a second entry at $2BFD (LD B,$10): clear only the 16\nregister copies and write them out, silencing the chip. The keyboard interrupt calls it when\nHOLD is pressed ($2E4C).\nExit: A = 0.","comment":"All of the SOUND RAM"},
        "11260": {"comment":"Hides LD B,$10 at $2BFD: the 16 copies only"},
        "11263": {"comment":"Clear them"},
        "11266": {"synopsis":"Writes the 16 register copies at $B2E3-$B2F2 to DAVE's ports $A0-$AF.","comment":"Ports from $A0"},
        "11268": {"comment":"Register copies"},
        "11271": {"comment":"16 registers"},
        "11273": {"synopsis":"Loop: one register per pass.","comment":"Next port"},
        "11274": {"comment":"Write one"},
        "11279": {"synopsis":"Zeroes B bytes from $B2E3 up.\nExit: A = 0, B = 0, HL past the last byte.","comment":"Zero B bytes"},
        "11280": {"comment":"From the register copies"},
        "11283": {"synopsis":"Loop: one byte per pass."},
        "11288": {"synopsis":"SOUND, ESC S env p vl vr sty ch d f: queues a sound. Reached from the escape table at\nSND_ESC_TABLE\nafter its 10 parameter bytes have been collected at $B381-$B38A (env, pitch word, left and\nright volume, style, channel, duration word, flags).\n1. Bit 7 of the flags empties the channel's queue first (SND_FLUSH_CHAN).\n2. Each channel queues up to 25 sounds of 10 bytes: the first byte of its block counts the\n   bytes. While the queue is full: error $DF (.SQFUL) if WAIT_SND is not 0, else it waits\n   with interrupts on, until there is room or STOP is pressed (error $E5, .STOP).\n3. Copies the 10 bytes to the channel's queue (256 bytes per channel from the pointer in\n   $B2F6), the envelope number plus 1 (the beep, 255, becomes 0).\nExit: A = 0, or the error.","comment":"Channel of ESC S"},
        "11291": {"comment":"0-3"},
        "11294": {"comment":"IY = HL = its block"},
        "11297": {"comment":"Keep the block"},
        "11298": {"comment":"Flags of ESC S"},
        "11301": {"comment":"Bit 7: cancel the queued sounds?"},
        "11302": {"comment":"Yes: empty the queue"},
        "11306": {"synopsis":"Waits for room in the queue, with interrupts off while it looks.","comment":"No interrupts while looking"},
        "11307": {"comment":"Bytes queued, 10 per sound"},
        "11308": {"comment":"Room for one more?"},
        "11310": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "11312": {"comment":"Full"},
        "11313": {"comment":"WAIT_SND"},
        "11316": {"comment":"Not 0: do not wait"},
        "11317": {"comment":"Error $DF (.SQFUL)"},
        "11320": {"comment":"FLAG_SOFT_IRQ"},
        "11323": {"comment":"STOP pressed?"},
        "11325": {"comment":"Error $E5 (.STOP)"},
        "11327": {"comment":"No: wait for room"},
        "11330": {"synopsis":"Room: the 10 bytes go into the queue; interrupts on again.","comment":"B = the channel"},
        "11331": {"comment":"C = bytes queued before"},
        "11332": {"comment":"The new count"},
        "11333": {"comment":"Queues: 256 bytes per channel"},
        "11337": {"comment":"DE = the free slot"},
        "11338": {"comment":"Envelope number"},
        "11341": {"comment":"Plus 1: the beep, 255, becomes 0"},
        "11342": {"comment":"10 parameter bytes"},
        "11345": {"comment":"Into the queue"},
        "11348": {"comment":"Done"},
        "11350": {"synopsis":"SOUND, ESC E en ep er: first stage of an envelope definition, run when the three header\nbytes are at $B381-$B383. A phase count over 40, or envelope number 255, is error $E1\n(.SENV). Otherwise the envelope number is stored plus 1, $B37B = 6 x phases, and the escape\ncollector is told to take that many more bytes (the phases, 6 bytes each) and then go on at\nSND_ENV_STORE ($B37C).\nExit: A = 0, or the error.","comment":"Next stage after the phase bytes"},
        "11356": {"comment":"Number of phases"},
        "11361": {"comment":"More than 40?"},
        "11363": {"comment":"Error $E1 (.SENV)"},
        "11366": {"comment":"Envelope number"},
        "11367": {"comment":"Stored plus 1"},
        "11368": {"comment":"255 is refused, A still $E1"},
        "11369": {"comment":"Phases x 2"},
        "11372": {"comment":"x 6: bytes of phase data"},
        "11374": {"comment":"$B37B = their count"},
        "11377": {"comment":"Bytes still to collect"},
        "11384": {"synopsis":"SOUND, ESC E, second stage: stores an envelope in the list that starts at the pointer in\n$B2F4 and must end before the queues ($B2F6). Each record is: number + 1, length (6n + 3),\nphase count n, release phase, then 6 bytes per phase; a 0 ends the list.\n1. Walks the list with interrupts off, moving each record down over a record with the same\n   number, so the old definition goes.\n2. Appends the new record from the collected bytes at $B381-; without room the list ends\n   where it would have started, and the result is error $E0 (.SENBF) through the LD A,$E0\n   hidden at $2CB3.\nExit: A = 0, or the error; interrupts on.","comment":"No interrupts while the list moves"},
        "11385": {"comment":"Number of the new envelope, plus 1"},
        "11388": {"comment":"Start of the list"},
        "11391": {"comment":"DE = where records go"},
        "11393": {"comment":"BC = 0"},
        "11396": {"synopsis":"Skips the record at HL (C = its size).","comment":"Over a record"},
        "11397": {"synopsis":"Loop: one record per pass, until the end marker 0.","comment":"End of the list (0)?"},
        "11401": {"comment":"Record length"},
        "11403": {"comment":"Plus the number byte"},
        "11405": {"comment":"Same envelope number?"},
        "11406": {"comment":"Yes: leave it out"},
        "11408": {"comment":"Move the record down"},
        "11410": {"comment":"Next record"},
        "11412": {"synopsis":"End of the list: writes the new record there if it fits.","comment":"Number of the new record"},
        "11413": {"comment":"Bytes of phase data"},
        "11416": {"comment":"Plus number, length, count, release"},
        "11419": {"comment":"A = its length byte"},
        "11420": {"comment":"HL = past the new record"},
        "11422": {"comment":"Start of the queues"},
        "11426": {"comment":"Past it?"},
        "11430": {"comment":"Length byte"},
        "11432": {"comment":"Count, release and phases"},
        "11437": {"comment":"From the collected bytes"},
        "11442": {"comment":"A = 0; hides LD A,$E0 at $2CB3: .SENBF"},
        "11445": {"comment":"HL = where the list ends"},
        "11446": {"comment":"End marker"},
        "11448": {"comment":"Interrupts on again"},
        "11450": {"synopsis":"The key click, called by the keyboard interrupt when CLICK_KEY is 0. Sets tone 0's period to\n$0032, then makes 50 pulses on channel 0's volume: each is 15 delay loops at volume 63 left\nand right, then a silence of (60 - n) / 2 loops that grows as n counts down from 50.\nBusy-waits; leaves channel 0's volume 0 (the next interrupt restores the registers).\nChanges: AF, BC.","comment":"Tone 0 period $0032; 50 pulses"},
        "11453": {"comment":"Low byte"},
        "11456": {"comment":"High byte 0"},
        "11458": {"synopsis":"Loop: one pulse per pass, C = 50 down to 1.","comment":"Loud part: 15 loops"},
        "11460": {"comment":"Volume 63"},
        "11462": {"comment":"Channel 0 left"},
        "11464": {"comment":"Channel 0 right"},
        "11466": {"synopsis":"Delay loop with the volume up.","comment":"Wait"},
        "11468": {"comment":"Quiet part: (60 - C) / 2 loops"},
        "11474": {"comment":"Volume 0"},
        "11479": {"synopsis":"Delay loop with the volume at 0.","comment":"Wait"},
        "11481": {"comment":"All pulses made?"},
        "11485": {"synopsis":"SOUND, CTRL G (code 7, reached from $28E0): a ping on tone channel 2. Waits for any ping\nstill sounding to end (STOP gives error $E5, .STOP), then starts one at volume 50\n(SND_PING_VOL); the interrupt lowers the volume by 1 each tick until it reaches 0.\nExit: A = 0, or the error.","comment":"FLAG_SOFT_IRQ"},
        "11488": {"comment":"STOP pressed?"},
        "11490": {"comment":"Error $E5 (.STOP)"},
        "11493": {"comment":"A ping still sounding?"},
        "11497": {"comment":"Wait for it to end"},
        "11499": {"comment":"Start at volume 50"},
        "11501": {"synopsis":"Sets the ping's volume to A' (the value in A when it is entered). If channel 2 is busy (bit\n7 or 5 of its state byte at $B342, its block's IY+7) the ping stops instead. Otherwise tone\n2's period is set to $0028 and its left and right volume copies to the volume.","comment":"Keep the volume"},
        "11502": {"comment":"Channel 2's state flags"},
        "11505": {"comment":"Channel 2 in use?"},
        "11507": {"comment":"Yes: ping off"},
        "11511": {"comment":"Tone 2 period"},
        "11514": {"comment":"Low byte $28"},
        "11517": {"comment":"High byte 0"},
        "11518": {"comment":"The volume"},
        "11519": {"comment":"Channel 2 left volume"},
        "11522": {"comment":"Channel 2 right volume"},
        "11525": {"synopsis":"Stores the ping volume in $B2F9 (0: no ping).\nExit: A = 0.","comment":"0: no ping"},
        "11530": {"synopsis":"KEYBOARD, close and destroy channel, and initialise (entries +6, +8 and +24): $BEAD = 0, so\nthe interrupt ignores the keyboard and an open is allowed.\nExit: A = 0.","comment":"No KEYBOARD channel"},
        "11534": {"synopsis":"KEYBOARD, buffer moved (entry +26): nothing to do (the channel has no buffer)."},
        "11535": {"synopsis":"KEYBOARD, interrupt (entry +0): scans the keys on every video interrupt while a KEYBOARD\nchannel is open ($BEAD not 0).\n1. Keeps one lock in LOCK_KEY (the lowest of CAPS 1, SHIFT 2, ALT 8) and copies its text, or\n   blanks, to $BEB8 (KBD_LOCK_TEXT).\n2. Reads the 10 key rows (KBD_SCAN). The LOCK key (row 1 bit 1) sets LOCK_KEY from the\n   modifier held with it: CTRL gives CAPS, SHIFT gives SHIFT, ALT gives ALT, none unlocks;\n   $BEAF stops it acting again while it stays down.\n3. $BEAC = the modifier held now (2 SHIFT, 4 CTRL, 8 ALT, KBD_MODIFIERS), then it looks for\n   a newly pressed key (KBD_NEW_KEY). A new character goes to $BEAE with $BEAA = $FF; if\n   KEY_IRQ is 0 it raises software interrupt $21; the first repeat waits DELAY_KEY ticks; it\n   clicks if CLICK_KEY is 0.\n4. With no new key: while HOLD is on it stays here, rescanning and passing the 1 Hz tick on,\n   until HOLD or STOP is pressed (KBD_NO_NEW); otherwise it handles auto-repeat\n   (KBD_REPEAT).\nEntry: IY is set to the row copy at $BD16 by the scan, so the descriptor's IY is not used.","comment":"Channel open?"},
        "11539": {"comment":"No: nothing to scan"},
        "11540": {"comment":"LOCK_KEY"},
        "11543": {"comment":"CAPS, SHIFT and ALT bits only"},
        "11545": {"comment":"Keep the lowest bit set"},
        "11549": {"comment":"Back to LOCK_KEY"},
        "11552": {"comment":"Blanks when none"},
        "11554": {"comment":"Its text to $BEB8"},
        "11557": {"comment":"Read the 10 rows"},
        "11560": {"comment":"LOCK key latch"},
        "11563": {"comment":"LOCK key (row 1 bit 1) down?"},
        "11569": {"comment":"Already acted on?"},
        "11572": {"comment":"Latch it"},
        "11573": {"comment":"CTRL with LOCK: CAPS"},
        "11575": {"comment":"Which modifier is held?"},
        "11578": {"comment":"New LOCK_KEY; 0 unlocks"},
        "11581": {"comment":"A lock set: done this tick"},
        "11582": {"synopsis":"LOCK up, or pressed alone (unlocking, falling through): releases the latch and reads the\nheld modifier.","comment":"Latch off (B = 0 after the scan)"},
        "11583": {"comment":"CTRL held: 4"},
        "11585": {"comment":"Which modifier is held?"},
        "11588": {"comment":"$BEAC = the held modifier"},
        "11591": {"synopsis":"Looks for a newly pressed key without reading the rows again (Z).","comment":"Z: no rescan"},
        "11592": {"synopsis":"Looks for a newly pressed key; NZ reads the rows first (from the HOLD loop).","comment":"Look for a new key"},
        "11595": {"comment":"None (E = $FF)?"},
        "11598": {"comment":"The character"},
        "11599": {"comment":"$BEAE = it"},
        "11602": {"comment":"$BEAA: a character is waiting"},
        "11607": {"comment":"KEY_IRQ"},
        "11610": {"comment":"Not 0: no interrupt"},
        "11613": {"comment":"Software interrupt $21: a key"},
        "11618": {"synopsis":"A character was taken: starts the delay before its first repeat.","comment":"DELAY_KEY"},
        "11621": {"synopsis":"Sets the repeat delay to A, then clicks if CLICK_KEY is 0.","comment":"$BEB3 = ticks to the first repeat"},
        "11624": {"comment":"CLICK_KEY"},
        "11627": {"comment":"0: click"},
        "11632": {"synopsis":"No new key. With HOLD on ($BEAB not 0) it waits here: when the 1 Hz latch is set it resets\nit and calls segment 1's time code through SEG1_CLOCK (service 4, the one-second tick), then\nrescans, until a key ends HOLD.","comment":"HOLD on?"},
        "11634": {"comment":"No: auto-repeat"},
        "11636": {"comment":"1 Hz latch set?"},
        "11642": {"comment":"IRQ_ENABLE_STATE"},
        "11645": {"comment":"Keep the enables"},
        "11646": {"comment":"Reset the 1 Hz latch"},
        "11649": {"comment":"Segment 1's time code, A = 4 there"},
        "11652": {"synopsis":"Rescans the keys (NZ) and loops while HOLD stays on.","comment":"NZ: read the rows again"},
        "11654": {"comment":"Until HOLD ends"},
        "11656": {"synopsis":"Auto-repeat: counts down the first-repeat delay ($BEB3) and the repeat interval ($BEB4);\nwhen one runs out and the key is still held it is decoded again (KBD_REP_AGAIN). A key in\nrow 8 bits 1, 2, 3 or 5 also keeps repeating while another of those is held. When the key is\nup, the old row copy at $BD20 is cleared and the interval stopped.","comment":"Ticks to the first repeat"},
        "11659": {"comment":"Count; run out?"},
        "11662": {"comment":"Repeat interval"},
        "11663": {"comment":"Else count it"},
        "11666": {"comment":"Neither ran out"},
        "11667": {"comment":"The repeating key's bit"},
        "11671": {"comment":"Its row in the old copy"},
        "11675": {"comment":"Row 8?"},
        "11683": {"comment":"Row 8 bits 1, 2, 3 and 5"},
        "11685": {"comment":"Is the key one of them?"},
        "11688": {"comment":"Another of them held?"},
        "11690": {"comment":"Yes: repeat"},
        "11692": {"synopsis":"Is the repeating key still held in the old row copy?","comment":"The key itself still held?"},
        "11694": {"comment":"Yes: repeat"},
        "11696": {"comment":"Forget the old rows"},
        "11701": {"synopsis":"Loop: clears the 10 bytes of the old row copy.","comment":"Clear one"},
        "11705": {"comment":"No repeat interval"},
        "11709": {"synopsis":"Repeats the key: clears its bit in the old row copy so that it looks newly pressed, sets the\ninterval to RATE_KEY and decodes it again.","comment":"Its bit off in the old copy"},
        "11712": {"comment":"RATE_KEY"},
        "11715": {"comment":"$BEB4 = ticks between repeats"},
        "11718": {"comment":"Decode it again"},
        "11721": {"synopsis":"Counts down the byte at HL unless it is 0.\nExit: carry set when it has just reached 0.","comment":"Counter"},
        "11723": {"comment":"0: not counting, no carry"},
        "11724": {"comment":"Count down"},
        "11725": {"comment":"Not yet 0"},
        "11726": {"comment":"Just reached 0"},
        "11728": {"synopsis":"Finds the first newly pressed key, rows 9 down to 0, and decodes it.\n1. NZ on entry reads the rows again (KBD_SCAN). The modifier and LOCK keys are cleared from\n   the new row copy, so they never count as keys.\n2. For each row: the old copy at $BD20-$BD29 keeps only the keys still down; a key down now\n   and not before is new. The lowest new bit is marked held, its old-copy address goes to\n   $BEB5 and its bit to $BEB7.\n3. Its code is the byte at KBD_KEY_CODES + 10 x (7 - bit) + row. D = LOCK_KEY XOR the held\n   modifier, B = the held modifier. Then KBD_NOT_HELD or the HOLD rules decide what it\n   gives.\nExit: E = $FF when there is no new key (or it gives nothing); otherwise C = the character.","comment":"NZ: read the rows first"},
        "11731": {"comment":"Not keys: SHIFT (row 0 bit 7)"},
        "11735": {"comment":"SHIFT (row 8 bit 5)"},
        "11739": {"comment":"CTRL (row 1 bit 7)"},
        "11743": {"comment":"ALT (row 7 bit 7)"},
        "11747": {"comment":"LOCK (row 1 bit 1)"},
        "11751": {"comment":"HOLD flag"},
        "11754": {"comment":"E counts 10 rows"},
        "11758": {"comment":"Old row copy, past row 9"},
        "11761": {"comment":"New row copy, past row 9"},
        "11764": {"synopsis":"Loop: one row per pass, until row 0 is done.","comment":"Previous row"},
        "11767": {"comment":"All rows done?"},
        "11768": {"comment":"Yes: no new key, E = $FF"},
        "11770": {"comment":"Keys down now"},
        "11772": {"comment":"Keys down in both copies"},
        "11775": {"comment":"Old copy: released keys dropped"},
        "11776": {"comment":"Keys newly down"},
        "11777": {"comment":"None in this row"},
        "11779": {"comment":"Keep only the lowest"},
        "11784": {"comment":"Mark it held"},
        "11786": {"comment":"A = its bit"},
        "11787": {"comment":"$BEB5 = its row in the old copy"},
        "11790": {"comment":"$BEB7 = its bit"},
        "11793": {"comment":"Index: 10 x (7 - bit) + row"},
        "11795": {"synopsis":"Loop: forms 10 x (7 - bit) by stepping down 10 per bit.","comment":"10 less per bit"},
        "11797": {"comment":"Found the bit?"},
        "11802": {"comment":"Plus the row"},
        "11803": {"comment":"DE = the index"},
        "11804": {"comment":"Held modifier"},
        "11808": {"comment":"LOCK_KEY"},
        "11811": {"comment":"A lock flips the held modifier"},
        "11813": {"comment":"Key code table"},
        "11817": {"comment":"C = the key's code"},
        "11819": {"comment":"D = the modifiers in effect"},
        "11820": {"comment":"HOLD on?"},
        "11823": {"comment":"No"},
        "11825": {"comment":"STOP ends HOLD"},
        "11829": {"comment":"Other codes do nothing"},
        "11832": {"comment":"HOLD again: off"},
        "11833": {"comment":"No character"},
        "11836": {"synopsis":"HOLD off: code 0 (the HOLD key) turns HOLD on; any other code is translated (KBD_KEY_CODE).","comment":"The HOLD key (code 0)?"},
        "11839": {"synopsis":"Turns HOLD off and translates the code (KBD_XLATE). The 0 key is stored as $7F so that its\nSHIFT form comes from the letter rules: unshifted it becomes $30.\nExit: C = the character.","comment":"HOLD off"},
        "11841": {"comment":"Code to character"},
        "11844": {"comment":"$7F is the 0 key: $30"},
        "11849": {"comment":"C = the character"},
        "11851": {"synopsis":"Turns HOLD on: silences the sound chip, shows the HOLD text, and gives no character.","comment":"HOLD on"},
        "11852": {"comment":"Silence the sound chip"},
        "11855": {"comment":"Show HOLD"},
        "11860": {"synopsis":"No character: E = $FF.","comment":"No key"},
        "11863": {"synopsis":"Translates a key code into a character, using D (LOCK_KEY XOR held modifier: 1 CAPS, 2\nSHIFT, 4 CTRL, 8 ALT) and B (the held modifier).\n- Below $21: as it is (TAB, ESC, CR, space).\n- $21-$3F: SHIFT flips bit 4 (KBD_SHIFT_XOR).\n- $40-$7F: letters and the like (KBD_LETTER).\n- $80-$BF: one of four codes, + 0, 1 SHIFT, 2 CTRL, 3 ALT (KBD_VARIANT).\n- $C0, STOP: code 3 if STOP_IRQ is not 0, else software interrupt $20 and no character.\n- $F0-$F7: function keys (KBD_FKEY).\nExit: A = the character (when it returns).","comment":"Below $21: as it is"},
        "11866": {"comment":"$21-$3F?"},
        "11868": {"comment":"SHIFT flips bit 4"},
        "11872": {"comment":"$40-$7F: letters"},
        "11876": {"comment":"$80-$BF: four codes"},
        "11880": {"comment":"Above $C0: function keys"},
        "11882": {"comment":"STOP: STOP_IRQ"},
        "11886": {"comment":"Not 0: code 3"},
        "11889": {"comment":"Software interrupt $20: STOP"},
        "11893": {"synopsis":"Function key $F0-$F7. With CTRL held the code is returned as it is, with ALT plus 8\n($F8-$FF); otherwise it is key number 0-7, or 8-15 with SHIFT, and its programmed string is\nstarted (KBD_FKEY_NUM).","comment":"CTRL: $F0-$F7 as they are"},
        "11896": {"comment":"$F8-$FF"},
        "11898": {"comment":"ALT: returned"},
        "11901": {"comment":"SHIFT?"},
        "11905": {"comment":"Plain: keys 0-7"},
        "11907": {"synopsis":"Function key n (0-15): if its string at $BD2A + 24n is not empty, $BEB2 = its length and\n$BEB0 its address, for KBD_READ_CHAR to hand out; if it is empty, software interrupt $10 +\nn.","comment":"Key number 0-15"},
        "11911": {"comment":"HL = its string"},
        "11914": {"comment":"Length"},
        "11915": {"comment":"$BEB2 = characters left"},
        "11918": {"comment":"$BEB0 = where they are"},
        "11921": {"comment":"A string programmed?"},
        "11924": {"comment":"None: interrupt $10 + key"},
        "11927": {"synopsis":"Raises software interrupt A (FLAG_SOFT_IRQ), then gives no character.","comment":"FLAG_SOFT_IRQ"},
        "11930": {"synopsis":"No character from this key: no auto-repeat, and the two return addresses (to KBD_NEW_KEY's\ncaller) are dropped so that it goes straight on at KBD_DELAY_CLICK with A = 0.","comment":"No repeat interval"},
        "11934": {"comment":"Drop two return addresses"},
        "11936": {"comment":"No repeat delay; click"},
        "11939": {"synopsis":"Codes $40-$7F: CTRL makes a control code (bits 0-4), ALT the same plus $80.","comment":"Bits kept with CTRL"},
        "11941": {"comment":"CTRL?"},
        "11945": {"comment":"Control code"},
        "11947": {"synopsis":"No CTRL: ALT held or locked?","comment":"ALT?"},
        "11951": {"comment":"Control code"},
        "11952": {"comment":"Plus $80"},
        "11955": {"synopsis":"Neither: CAPS flips the case of a-z, then SHIFT flips it (KBD_SHIFT_XOR).","comment":"C = $20, the case bit"},
        "11956": {"comment":"Below a?"},
        "11960": {"comment":"Above z?"},
        "11964": {"comment":"CAPS?"},
        "11968": {"comment":"Flip the case"},
        "11969": {"synopsis":"SHIFT in D flips the bits in C ($10 for $21-$3F, $20 for letters).","comment":"SHIFT?"},
        "11972": {"comment":"Flip bit 4 or 5"},
        "11974": {"synopsis":"Adds the position of the held modifier's bit: 1 SHIFT, 2 CTRL, 3 ALT, 0 none.","comment":"Held modifier's bit"},
        "11976": {"comment":"Past it: done"},
        "11977": {"comment":"One more"},
        "11980": {"synopsis":"Reads which modifier is held in the row copy (IY): A as passed in for CTRL (row 1 bit 7), 2\nfor SHIFT (row 0 bit 7 or row 8 bit 5), 8 for ALT (row 7 bit 7), 0 (Z) for none. The\ninterrupt passes 4 for the held modifier and 1 (CAPS) for LOCK.","comment":"CTRL (row 1 bit 7)?"},
        "11984": {"comment":"Return A as passed"},
        "11985": {"comment":"SHIFT: 2"},
        "11987": {"comment":"Row 0 bit 7?"},
        "11992": {"comment":"Row 8 bit 5?"},
        "11997": {"comment":"ALT (row 7 bit 7)?"},
        "12001": {"comment":"ALT: 8"},
        "12004": {"comment":"None"},
        "12006": {"synopsis":"Reads the 10 key rows into $BD16-$BD1F, a 1 bit for each key down, selecting row n with port\n$B5's low bits while keeping the upper bits of PORTB5.\nExit: IY = $BD16, B = 0.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL.","comment":"PORTB5"},
        "12009": {"comment":"Keep its upper bits"},
        "12012": {"comment":"New row copy"},
        "12015": {"comment":"IY = it too"},
        "12018": {"comment":"10 rows"},
        "12020": {"synopsis":"Loop: one row per pass.","comment":"Select row C"},
        "12023": {"comment":"Read it"},
        "12025": {"comment":"1 = down"},
        "12027": {"comment":"Next row"},
        "12032": {"synopsis":"Copies the 5-character text for the lowest bit set in A (bit 0 CAPS, 1 SHIFT, 2 HOLD, 3 ALT,\n4 blanks) from KBD_LOCK_TEXTS to $BEB8.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"5 bytes before the first text"},
        "12035": {"comment":"5 bytes per text"},
        "12038": {"synopsis":"Loop: 5 bytes on per bit until the set bit is found.","comment":"Next text"},
        "12039": {"comment":"This bit?"},
        "12042": {"comment":"Status text copy"},
        "12045": {"comment":"5 characters"},
        "12048": {"synopsis":"The texts KBD_LOCK_TEXT copies to $BEB8, 5 characters each, no end mark: CAPS, SHIFT, HOLD,\nALT and five spaces (read at $2F0B + 5 x (bit + 1)). The last two spaces, $2F27-$2F28, are\nalso the first two bytes of KBD_KEY_CODES."},
        "12071": {"synopsis":"The key codes, 80 bytes: the key in row r (0-9), bit b of port $B5 is at KBD_KEY_CODES + 10\nx (7 -\nb) + r (read at $2E25). Below $21 and $21-$7F are characters (the 0 key is $7F, see\nKBD_KEY_CODE), $80-$BF keys with four codes each, $C0 STOP, $F0-$F7 the function keys, $00\nHOLD; $2A marks the modifier and LOCK keys (cleared before the lookup) and the unused\nplaces. Its first two bytes are the end of the blank text in KBD_LOCK_TEXTS."},
        "12151": {"synopsis":"KEYBOARD, open and create channel (entries +2, +4): only one channel; a second is error $E9\n(.2NDCH). Allocates no buffer (EXOS 27 with DE = 0), clears the keyboard RAM $BD16-$BEB7\n(row copies, function key strings, state) and sets $BEAD = $FF.\nExit: A = 0, or the error.","comment":"Already open?"},
        "12155": {"comment":"DE = 0"},
        "12156": {"comment":"Error $E9 (.2NDCH)"},
        "12159": {"comment":"No buffer"},
        "12162": {"comment":"Failed"},
        "12163": {"comment":"Clear the keyboard RAM"},
        "12169": {"comment":"$BD16-$BEB7"},
        "12175": {"comment":"Open: $FF"},
        "12180": {"synopsis":"KEYBOARD, read channel status (entry +18): C = 0 when a character is waiting (a function key\nstring, or a key in $BEAE), 1 when none.\nExit: A = 0.","comment":"Function key characters left?"},
        "12184": {"comment":"C = 0: ready"},
        "12188": {"comment":"A key waiting?"},
        "12194": {"comment":"C = 1: none"},
        "12195": {"synopsis":"Exit: A = 0, status in C."},
        "12197": {"synopsis":"KEYBOARD, read character (entry +10): waits for a character and returns it in B: first the\nrest of a function key's string, else the key the interrupt left in $BEAE. A pending STOP\nsoftware interrupt ends the wait with error $E5 (.STOP). KEYBOARD's read block ($119C) calls\nit for each byte.\nExit: A = 0 and B, or the error.","comment":"FLAG_SOFT_IRQ"},
        "12200": {"comment":"STOP pressed?"},
        "12202": {"comment":"Error $E5 (.STOP)"},
        "12205": {"comment":"Function key string?"},
        "12210": {"comment":"No"},
        "12212": {"comment":"One character less"},
        "12213": {"comment":"String pointer"},
        "12217": {"comment":"B = the next character"},
        "12223": {"synopsis":"No string: is a key waiting? If not, wait (back to KBD_READ_CHAR).","comment":"A key waiting?"},
        "12228": {"comment":"No: wait"},
        "12230": {"comment":"The character"},
        "12233": {"comment":"Into B"},
        "12235": {"comment":"Taken"},
        "12237": {"synopsis":"KEYBOARD, special function (entry +22): B = 8 (@@FKEY) programs a function key\n(KBD_SET_FKEY); B = 9 (@@JOY) reads a joystick into C; anything else is error $EA (.ISPEC).\nFor @@JOY, C = 0 reads the keys of the built-in one (KBD_JOY_KEYS); 1 and 2 read rows 0-4 or\n5-9 of port $B5 through bit 0 of port $B6, giving 5 bits with the first row in bit 4.\nExit: A = 0 and C = the bits (1 = active), or the error.","comment":"Subfunction"},
        "12238": {"comment":"@@FKEY (8)?"},
        "12242": {"comment":"@@JOY (9)?"},
        "12244": {"comment":"Else error $EA (.ISPEC)"},
        "12247": {"comment":"Unit 0: the keys"},
        "12251": {"comment":"5 rows"},
        "12253": {"comment":"Unit 1: rows 0-4"},
        "12255": {"comment":"Unit 2: rows 5-9"},
        "12256": {"synopsis":"Loop: one row per pass, its bit 0 of port $B6 into D."},
        "12257": {"comment":"Next row"},
        "12258": {"comment":"Select the row"},
        "12260": {"comment":"Bit 0 of port $B6"},
        "12263": {"comment":"1 = active"},
        "12264": {"comment":"Into D"},
        "12268": {"comment":"C = the five bits"},
        "12271": {"synopsis":"Unit 0: bit 4 from row 8 bit 6, bits 0-3 from row 7 bits 2, 5, 1 and 3 (in that order), 1 =\npressed.","comment":"Row 8"},
        "12275": {"comment":"Read it"},
        "12277": {"comment":"1 = down"},
        "12278": {"comment":"Bit 6"},
        "12280": {"comment":"To bit 4"},
        "12283": {"comment":"Row 7"},
        "12287": {"comment":"Read it"},
        "12289": {"comment":"1 = down"},
        "12291": {"comment":"Rearrange its bits 1, 2, 3, 5"},
        "12298": {"comment":"Bit 1 from row 7 bit 5"},
        "12303": {"comment":"Bit 3 from row 7 bit 3"},
        "12307": {"comment":"Bits 0-3"},
        "12309": {"comment":"Plus bit 4"},
        "12313": {"synopsis":"@@FKEY: copies the string at the caller's DE (length byte first, up to 23 characters) to the\nslot of function key C (bits 0-3) at $BD2A + 24C; a longer one is error $E2 (.KFSPC).\nMAP_CALLER_DE\npages the caller's segment into page 1 for DE.\nExit: A = 0, or the error.","comment":"Key number"},
        "12314": {"comment":"0-15"},
        "12317": {"comment":"Caller's DE through page 1"},
        "12320": {"comment":"HL = the key's slot"},
        "12323": {"comment":"HL = string, DE = slot"},
        "12324": {"comment":"Length"},
        "12326": {"comment":"Over 23?"},
        "12328": {"comment":"Error $E2 (.KFSPC)"},
        "12331": {"comment":"Plus the length byte"},
        "12334": {"comment":"Copy it"},
        "12337": {"synopsis":"HL = $BD2A + 24 x C: the 24-byte slot of function key C.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL.","comment":"HL = C"},
        "12340": {"comment":"x 8"},
        "12343": {"comment":"Keep 8C"},
        "12345": {"comment":"x 24"},
        "12347": {"comment":"Slots from $BD2A"},
        "12352": {"synopsis":"KEYBOARD's device descriptor in ROM form, linked from SOUND's (XX_NEXT at SND_DESC = $7054):\nXX_NEXT $7083 (EDITOR's XX_SIZE byte with segment 0 in page 1), XX_RAM $FFFE, DD_TYPE 0,\nDD_IRQFLAG $20 (video interrupt), DD_FLAGS 0, DD_TAB $7055 (KBD_TABLE) in this segment, unit\ncount 0, the name \"KEYBOARD\" and XX_SIZE 16."},
        "12373": {"synopsis":"KEYBOARD's entry table, 14 words (run addresses): interrupt, open, create, close, destroy,\nread character, read block, write character, write block, read status, set status, special\nfunction, initialise, buffer moved. Writes and set status go to the shared ERR_NOFN (error\n$E7,\n.NOFN); read block to $119C."},
        "12401": {"synopsis":"EDITOR's device descriptor in ROM form, the last in the chain (XX_NEXT 0): XX_RAM $FFFE,\nDD_TYPE 0, DD_IRQFLAG 0 (no interrupt), DD_FLAGS 0, DD_TAB $7082 (EDT_TABLE), unit count 0,\nthen the name \"EDITOR\", whose last letter and XX_SIZE 14 ($3082-$3083) are also the table's\nfirst word."},
        "12418": {"synopsis":"EDITOR's entry table, 14 words (run addresses). The first word, the interrupt entry, is the\nname's last letter and XX_SIZE ($0E52): never read, as DD_IRQFLAG is 0. Then open, create\n(EDT_OPEN), close, destroy (EDT_CLOSE), read character, read block, write character, write\nblock, read status, set status (ERR_NOFN, error $E7 .NOFN), special function, initialise,\nbuffer moved."},
        "12446": {"synopsis":"EDITOR, close and destroy channel (entries +6, +8): loads the channel's variables\n(EDT_SELECT), then falls into EDT_INIT, so that no channel counts as loaded.","comment":"Load this channel's variables"},
        "12449": {"synopsis":"EDITOR, initialise (entry +24): $B28B = 0, no channel's variables loaded.\nExit: A = 0.","comment":"No channel loaded"},
        "12454": {"synopsis":"EDITOR, buffer moved (entry +26): loads the channel's variables, then moves the five\npointers $B253, $B255, $B257, $B259 and $B25B by BC with ADD_BC_WORD, keeping them page-1\naddresses. Ends at EDT_NO_VIDEO, so it returns A = $D4.","comment":"Load this channel's variables"},
        "12457": {"comment":"Pointers from $B253"},
        "12460": {"comment":"Five of them"},
        "12462": {"synopsis":"Loop: one pointer per pass.","comment":"Z: keep in page 1"},
        "12463": {"comment":"Move it by BC"},
        "12466": {"comment":"All five?"},
        "12469": {"synopsis":"Error $D4 (.EVID): the video page will not do.","comment":"Error $D4 (.EVID)"},
        "12472": {"synopsis":"EDITOR, open and create channel (entries +2, +4).\n1. Asks the video channel in VID_EDIT for its size (@@SIZE): it must answer, be a text page\n   (D, the page's mode, has bit 0 clear), and have at least 3 rows and 4 columns; else error\n   $D4 (.EVID).\n2. Allocates a buffer of (BUF_EDIT AND $3F) + 1 pages of 256 bytes (EXOS 27).\n3. Makes this channel the current one (EDT_SELECT): $B25F = VID_EDIT, $B260 = KEY_EDIT. The\n   text area runs from the buffer's start ($B253) to below the variables and one page-width\n   line under IX ($B255), each end marked by a byte 1; $B265 = rows, $B266 = columns, and\n   $B26D-$B270 1 and columns - 2 (the margins in use and the full-width ones: left 1, right\n   columns - 2).\n4. Starts an empty text (EDT_NEW_TEXT).\nExit: A = 0, or the error.","comment":"Keep the channel number"},
        "12473": {"comment":"VID_EDIT (L), KEY_EDIT (H)"},
        "12476": {"comment":"Video channel"},
        "12477": {"comment":"@@SIZE"},
        "12481": {"comment":"No answer"},
        "12483": {"comment":"Not a text page?"},
        "12487": {"comment":"Rows"},
        "12488": {"comment":"Fewer than 3?"},
        "12492": {"comment":"Columns"},
        "12493": {"comment":"Fewer than 4?"},
        "12497": {"comment":"Keep the size"},
        "12498": {"comment":"BUF_EDIT"},
        "12503": {"comment":"D = pages of 256"},
        "12505": {"comment":"Keep the buffer size"},
        "12506": {"comment":"Allocate the buffer"},
        "12508": {"comment":"BC = buffer size"},
        "12509": {"comment":"D = columns, E = rows"},
        "12510": {"comment":"Failed"},
        "12511": {"comment":"The channel number"},
        "12512": {"comment":"Make it the current one"},
        "12515": {"comment":"$B25F video, $B260 keyboard channel"},
        "12518": {"comment":"IX: the channel RAM"},
        "12523": {"comment":"Below 55 bytes"},
        "12529": {"comment":"and one line of the page's width"},
        "12532": {"comment":"$B255 = end of the text area"},
        "12535": {"comment":"End marker 1"},
        "12538": {"comment":"Buffer start"},
        "12540": {"comment":"$B253 = start of the text area"},
        "12543": {"comment":"Start marker 1"},
        "12544": {"comment":"Rows and columns"},
        "12545": {"comment":"$B265 rows, $B266 columns"},
        "12548": {"comment":"Columns - 2"},
        "12550": {"comment":"and 1"},
        "12552": {"comment":"Margins in use and full-width ones: 1, columns - 2"},
        "12558": {"comment":"Fill the page-width line (EDT_TABS_INIT)"},
        "12561": {"synopsis":"Starts an empty text in the buffer: a line header (the left margin + $80, then $80, then 3)\nand the end mark 2 after it ($B257). $B259 = $B25B = the line's first byte. Clears the free\nspace up to the end marker 1 and keeps its size in $B25D, sets $B269/$B26B and $B273, sends\nESC s and $1A (clear the page) and ESC o to the video channel, and goes on at\nEDT_RULER_TABS. Also\nused by @@CHLD and from $336F.","comment":"First byte of the text"},
        "12565": {"comment":"Left margin"},
        "12568": {"comment":"Also to $B274-$B276"},
        "12571": {"comment":"Header: margin + $80"},
        "12574": {"comment":"$B259 = this line"},
        "12577": {"comment":"$B25B = this line"},
        "12581": {"comment":"Second header byte"},
        "12583": {"comment":"$B272 = $80"},
        "12588": {"comment":"Third byte: 3"},
        "12591": {"comment":"End mark 2"},
        "12594": {"comment":"$B257 = the end mark"},
        "12598": {"comment":"Count free bytes"},
        "12601": {"synopsis":"Loop: clears the free space byte by byte, counting it, up to the end marker 1."},
        "12602": {"comment":"Clear one"},
        "12605": {"comment":"End marker 1 next?"},
        "12609": {"comment":"$B25D = free bytes"},
        "12613": {"comment":"A from EDT_SET_DIRTY"},
        "12619": {"comment":"$B269 and $B26B"},
        "12625": {"comment":"$B273 = 1"},
        "12629": {"comment":"ESC s, then $1A: clear the page"},
        "12636": {"comment":"ESC o"},
        "12638": {"comment":"Also kept in $B27C"},
        "12641": {"comment":"To the video channel"},
        "12644": {"comment":"Goes on at EDT_RULER_TABS"},
        "12647": {"synopsis":"Makes the calling EDITOR channel (A = its number, IX = its RAM) the current one. The current\nchannel's 53 bytes of variables are kept at $B253-$B287 (IY = $B253 from here); when another\nchannel was loaded ($B28B), its variables are first copied back below its IX ($B288) with\nits segment ($B28A) in page 1, then this channel's are copied in from below IX.\nExit: IY = $B253, $B28B/$B288/$B28A = this channel, its number, IX and page-1 segment.\nChanges: AF, IY and the alternate set (BC, DE, HL kept through EXX).","comment":"Keep BC, DE, HL"},
        "12648": {"comment":"Current channel's variables"},
        "12652": {"comment":"B = this channel"},
        "12653": {"comment":"Channel loaded now"},
        "12657": {"comment":"This one?"},
        "12660": {"comment":"Note this one"},
        "12661": {"comment":"None loaded before?"},
        "12662": {"comment":"53 bytes of variables"},
        "12667": {"comment":"Keep page 1"},
        "12670": {"comment":"Old channel's segment"},
        "12672": {"comment":"Into page 1"},
        "12674": {"comment":"Its IX"},
        "12678": {"comment":"Store below it"},
        "12681": {"comment":"Save its variables"},
        "12684": {"comment":"Page 1 back"},
        "12687": {"synopsis":"Copies this channel's variables in from below its IX.","comment":"This channel's IX"},
        "12690": {"comment":"Variables below it"},
        "12691": {"comment":"Into $B253-$B287"},
        "12696": {"synopsis":"Notes the page-1 segment and IX of the loaded channel.","comment":"Page 1 segment"},
        "12698": {"comment":"Of the loaded channel"},
        "12701": {"comment":"And its IX"},
        "12705": {"comment":"Caller's registers back"},
        "12707": {"synopsis":"EDITOR, special function (entry +22), C = a channel: B = 24 (@@MARG) goes to\nEDT_SET_MARGINS; B = 26\n(@@CHSV) writes the text to channel C as a document: a 16-byte header (EDT_DOC_HEADER,\nmodule type 8), then every byte from the end mark round to the end mark; B = 25 (@@CHLD)\nloads one (EDT_LOAD). Anything else is error $EA (.ISPEC).\nExit: A = 0, or an error.","comment":"Channel checks"},
        "12710": {"comment":"Nothing ready to send"},
        "12714": {"comment":"No SEND ALL ended"},
        "12717": {"comment":"Channel to load or save"},
        "12721": {"comment":"@@MARG (24)?"},
        "12727": {"comment":"@@CHLD (25)?"},
        "12731": {"comment":"@@CHSV (26)?"},
        "12733": {"comment":"Else error $EA (.ISPEC)"},
        "12736": {"comment":"To that channel"},
        "12737": {"comment":"Document header"},
        "12740": {"comment":"16 bytes"},
        "12745": {"comment":"Write failed"},
        "12746": {"synopsis":"Goes back round the buffer to the end mark 2.","comment":"One byte back, wrapping round"},
        "12749": {"comment":"End mark 2?"},
        "12754": {"synopsis":"Loop: writes each text byte, jumping over the gap, until the end mark comes round.","comment":"Next byte, over the gap"},
        "12757": {"comment":"B = it"},
        "12758": {"comment":"The target channel"},
        "12763": {"comment":"Write failed"},
        "12764": {"comment":"End mark again?"},
        "12770": {"synopsis":"The 16-byte module header @@CHSV writes before a document (read at $31C1): byte 1 = 8, the\neditor document type; the rest 0."},
        "12786": {"synopsis":"@@CHLD: loads a document from channel $B261 into an empty text, line by line. Each line is a\nmargin byte (bit 7 ignored; clamped to columns - 4), a byte whose bits 0-1 are kept, then 3,\nthen characters from $1F up; 4 or 5 ends the line and 2 the text. Another code is error $D2\n(.EDINV), a full buffer error $D1 (.EDBUF), a read error its own code: the line read so far\nis taken out again (EDT_LOAD_FAIL). Then the page is redrawn from the start (EDT_LOAD_DONE).\nIt reads no module header.\nExit: A = 0, or the error.","comment":"Empty text"},
        "12795": {"comment":"$B25B = HL"},
        "12799": {"synopsis":"A new line: $B259 = the byte before it.","comment":"$B259 = before the line"},
        "12802": {"comment":"Margin byte"},
        "12805": {"comment":"Bit 7 off"},
        "12808": {"comment":"Minus 1"},
        "12809": {"comment":"Columns - 4"},
        "12814": {"comment":"Wider than that?"},
        "12817": {"comment":"No: as read"},
        "12818": {"synopsis":"Stores the line's margin byte, margin + $81.","comment":"Margin + $81"},
        "12821": {"comment":"Second byte"},
        "12824": {"comment":"Bits 0-1"},
        "12826": {"comment":"Plus $80"},
        "12829": {"comment":"Third byte"},
        "12832": {"comment":"Must be 3"},
        "12836": {"synopsis":"Loop: reads the line's characters until a code below $1F.","comment":"Next character"},
        "12839": {"comment":"$1F or above: keep it"},
        "12843": {"comment":"2: end of the text"},
        "12847": {"comment":"4: end of the line"},
        "12851": {"comment":"5: end of the line"},
        "12852": {"comment":"Else error $D2 (.EDINV)"},
        "12854": {"synopsis":"End of a line (4, 5) or of the text (2): counts the line (EDT_ROWS_INC).","comment":"Keep the code"},
        "12855": {"comment":"One more line"},
        "12859": {"comment":"End of the text?"},
        "12860": {"comment":"No: next line"},
        "12862": {"comment":"Result 0"},
        "12863": {"synopsis":"Keeps the result in $B261, then redraws the page from the text's start, row by row, and\nreturns the result.","comment":"$B261 = the result"},
        "12873": {"synopsis":"Loop: lays out lines until the page's rows are filled or the end mark comes."},
        "12883": {"comment":"Rows used"},
        "12886": {"comment":"Page full?"},
        "12891": {"synopsis":"Loop: shows the laid-out rows."},
        "12906": {"comment":"$B257 = the end mark"},
        "12909": {"comment":"The result"},
        "12913": {"synopsis":"Reads the next byte of the document into the gap after HL. The byte there is 0 in free\nspace; the end marker 1 means the buffer is full (EDT_BUF_FULL).\nExit: A = B = the byte; a read error goes to EDT_LOAD_FAIL.","comment":"Next free byte"},
        "12914": {"comment":"End marker 1 there?"},
        "12917": {"comment":"One free byte less"},
        "12920": {"comment":"Channel being loaded"},
        "12925": {"comment":"Read error"},
        "12927": {"comment":"Store the byte"},
        "12930": {"synopsis":"Buffer full: error $D1 (.EDBUF).","comment":"Marker back"},
        "12932": {"comment":"Error $D1 (.EDBUF)"},
        "12934": {"synopsis":"A load failed (A = the error): drops the return address into the loop and hands back the\nbytes of the line being read (free again, cleared to 0). The LD DE,$D23E at $3287 hides LD\nA,$D2 at $3288, the entry for a bad code: error $D2 (.EDINV).","comment":"Drop the return address"},
        "12935": {"comment":"Hides LD A,$D2 at $3288: .EDINV"},
        "12938": {"comment":"Keep the error"},
        "12939": {"synopsis":"Loop: frees bytes back to the line's start ($B259).","comment":"One free byte more"},
        "12942": {"comment":"Free again"},
        "12945": {"comment":"Line start"},
        "12949": {"comment":"Back there?"},
        "12955": {"comment":"Start marker 1 there?"},
        "12957": {"comment":"Nothing loaded: empty text"},
        "12960": {"comment":"End mark 2"},
        "12962": {"comment":"The error"},
        "12963": {"comment":"Redraw and return it"},
        "12965": {"synopsis":"EDITOR, read channel status (entry +18): C = 0 if characters are ready to send ($B282 bits\n0-1) or FLG_EDIT's SEND NOW (bit 7) is set; else $FF if a SEND ALL has just ended ($B284), 1\notherwise.\nExit: A = 0.","comment":"Channel checks"},
        "12968": {"comment":"Characters ready to send?"},
        "12973": {"comment":"C = 0: ready"},
        "12977": {"comment":"FLG_EDIT"},
        "12980": {"comment":"SEND NOW?"},
        "12983": {"comment":"C = 1: not ready"},
        "12984": {"comment":"SEND ALL just ended?"},
        "12989": {"comment":"C = $FF: end of file"},
        "12991": {"synopsis":"Exit: A = 0, status in C."},
        "12993": {"synopsis":"EDITOR, write character (entry +14): takes the character in B (EDT_PUT_CHAR), then\nEDT_CALL_EXIT.","comment":"Channel checks"},
        "12996": {"comment":"Take the character"},
        "13001": {"synopsis":"EDITOR, write block (entry +16): writes each byte through EDT_PUT_CHAR with BLOCK_WRITE;\n$B27A counts\nthat a block is in progress. Then EDT_CALL_EXIT.","comment":"Channel checks"},
        "13004": {"comment":"In a block"},
        "13007": {"comment":"For each byte: EDT_PUT_CHAR"},
        "13010": {"comment":"Write the block"},
        "13013": {"comment":"Block done"},
        "13016": {"synopsis":"Common end of EDITOR's character calls: keeps A, runs $3F73 and EDT_DRAW_ROW with the\ncaller's\nregisters swapped out, then returns error $D4 (.EVID) if a write to the video channel failed\n(bit 0 of $B27B), else the result.","comment":"Results aside"},
        "13017": {"comment":"Keep the status"},
        "13018": {"comment":"Finish off"},
        "13025": {"comment":"Results back"},
        "13026": {"comment":"Video write failed?"},
        "13031": {"comment":"Error $D4 (.EVID)"},
        "13034": {"synopsis":"EDITOR, read character (entry +10): gets a character (EDT_GET_CHAR), then EDT_CALL_EXIT.","comment":"Channel checks"},
        "13037": {"comment":"Get a character"},
        "13042": {"synopsis":"EDITOR, read block (entry +12): reads each byte through EDT_GET_CHAR with BLOCK_READ, then\nEDT_CALL_EXIT.","comment":"Channel checks"},
        "13045": {"comment":"For each byte: EDT_GET_CHAR"},
        "13048": {"comment":"Read the block"},
        "13053": {"synopsis":"Entry check for EDITOR's channel calls: loads the channel's variables (EDT_SELECT). If a\nvideo error is pending ($B27B), it checks that the keyboard channel answers a status read\nand that the video page is still a text page of the same size; if so it clears the error,\nelse it returns from its caller with error $D3 (.EKEY) or $D4 (.EVID). The routine continues\npast $3300.","comment":"Load this channel's variables"},
        "13056": {"comment":"Channel fault flags clear?"},
        "13061": {"comment":"Check the channels again"},
        "13062": {"comment":"Keyboard channel"},
        "13067": {"comment":"Error $D3 (.EKEY) if it fails"},
        "13071": {"comment":"Video channel: ask the page size (@@SIZE)"},
        "13078": {"comment":"Error $D4 (.EVID) if it fails"},
        "13082": {"comment":"Not a text page?"},
        "13086": {"comment":"H = columns, L = rows + ruler row"},
        "13094": {"comment":"Same size as at open?"},
        "13098": {"comment":"Both fine: clear the fault flags"},
        "13104": {"synopsis":"A channel is still faulty: drops the return into the channel routine, so EXOS gets the error\nin A at once."},
        "13106": {"synopsis":"EDITOR, write character, the body (called by the entry at EDT_WRITE_CHAR and, per byte, by\nwrite\nblock): a write cancels a read in progress, then the character is put into the text at the\ncursor.\nEntry: B = the character; IY = $B253, the editor variables of the channel.\nExit: A = status; $B257 = the cursor's buffer address.\n1. $20-$9F are stored at the cursor (EDT_STORE_CHAR), echoed and the cursor moves on.\n2. $A0-$FF act as the same keys typed (EDT_DO_KEY); ^X ($18) acts as Ctrl-F4 ($F3).\n3. $00 goes to the video page as it is; TAB, CR, ^Y, ^Z and ESC have their own actions;\n   other control codes are ignored.\n4. Inside an escape sequence the byte goes to EDT_PUT_ESC.","comment":"A write ends any read in progress"},
        "13110": {"comment":"No pending status"},
        "13113": {"comment":"HL = the cursor in the buffer"},
        "13116": {"comment":"Inside an escape sequence?"},
        "13121": {"comment":"Return through EDT_DONE_OK"},
        "13125": {"comment":"Control code?"},
        "13130": {"comment":"Editing key code $A0-$FF?"},
        "13132": {"synopsis":"Codes from $A0 up (and ^X, made $F3 at $3365) run the key's action, as if typed."},
        "13135": {"comment":"Printable: store it at the cursor"},
        "13138": {"comment":"Echo it on the video page"},
        "13141": {"comment":"Cursor one character on"},
        "13144": {"synopsis":"A control code below $20: picks its action.","comment":"$00?"},
        "13145": {"comment":"Written to the video page as it is"},
        "13148": {"comment":"TAB?"},
        "13153": {"comment":"CR?"},
        "13157": {"comment":"^X acts as Ctrl-F4, set left margin ($F3)"},
        "13159": {"comment":"^X ($18)?"},
        "13163": {"comment":"^Y ($19)?"},
        "13166": {"comment":"^Z ($1A)?"},
        "13167": {"comment":"Clears the whole text"},
        "13170": {"comment":"ESC ($1B)? Others are ignored"},
        "13172": {"comment":"ESC: escape state $80"},
        "13174": {"comment":"$3377 (inside) is xor a: the escape state ends"},
        "13176": {"synopsis":"Stores the escape state ($B262: $80 after ESC, 2 and 1 while the coordinates come, 0 none)\nand returns B as the status.","comment":"Escape state"},
        "13179": {"comment":"Status"},
        "13181": {"synopsis":"^Y, and AUTO ERA before the first typed character: deletes from the cursor to the end of the\nline (Shift-DEL, A = 1); a line that went on in the paragraph now ends it.","comment":"A = 1: Shift-DEL"},
        "13182": {"comment":"Delete to the end of the line"},
        "13185": {"comment":"Line ended by $05 (soft end)?"},
        "13188": {"comment":"Make it $04, a paragraph end"},
        "13190": {"synopsis":"CR: in overwrite mode the cursor goes to the line's end first; then the line is broken at\nthe cursor with a paragraph end ($04).","comment":"Pad the line with spaces up to the cursor"},
        "13193": {"comment":"Insert mode?"},
        "13197": {"comment":"Overwrite: to the end of the line"},
        "13200": {"comment":"Back one character"},
        "13203": {"comment":"Break the line here with a paragraph end"},
        "13208": {"synopsis":"A byte inside an escape sequence. After ESC only '=' (ESC = y x, cursor position) is taken;\nanything else ends it with error $E6 (.ESC).","comment":"Collecting the coordinates?"},
        "13212": {"comment":"ESC '='?"},
        "13214": {"comment":"Error $E6 (.ESC) for anything else"},
        "13218": {"comment":"Status 0"},
        "13219": {"comment":"Two coordinate bytes to come"},
        "13223": {"synopsis":"A coordinate byte of ESC = y x (each $20 + value). After the second one the cursor goes to\nrow y, column x of the page; a 0 keeps that coordinate.\nExit: A = 0, or error $D9 (.VCURS) when a coordinate is outside the page.","comment":"Value of the byte"},
        "13225": {"comment":"E = the byte before, D = this one"},
        "13229": {"comment":"Kept at $B263"},
        "13234": {"comment":"Count the byte; more to come?"},
        "13239": {"comment":"C = cursor row, B = cursor column"},
        "13243": {"comment":"Column 0: keep the column"},
        "13247": {"synopsis":"Checks the row coordinate: 0 keeps the cursor's row.","comment":"Row 0: keep the row"},
        "13251": {"synopsis":"Checks the coordinates against the page size.","comment":"Rows of the page"},
        "13254": {"comment":"Row past the last?"},
        "13257": {"comment":"Columns of the page"},
        "13261": {"synopsis":"Error $D9 (.VCURS) when the row or column is outside the page.","comment":"Error $D9 (.VCURS)"},
        "13264": {"comment":"Set the cursor column"},
        "13267": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor one line up or down until it is on the wanted row."},
        "13270": {"comment":"On the wanted row?"},
        "13277": {"comment":"One line up (carry) or down"},
        "13283": {"synopsis":"Common exit of the editor's write and read paths: status 0 and the cursor's address kept at\n$B257."},
        "13284": {"synopsis":"Keeps the cursor's buffer address at $B257 and returns A.","comment":"Keep the cursor's address"},
        "13288": {"synopsis":"EDITOR, read character, the body (called by the entry at EDT_READ_CHAR and, per byte, by\nread\nblock). While a text is being sent, the next character of it comes back at once\n(EDT_SEND_NEXT). Otherwise a status left from the last read (.EOF after SEND ALL) is given\nonce, or a new read starts: the FLG_EDIT flags are copied, the NO PROMPT position is marked,\nand the edit loop runs until ENTER or ESC (EDT_EDIT_LOOP).\nExit: A = status, B = the character.\n$B282 holds the read's state: FLG_EDIT's bits 2-7, b0 = sending, b1 = LF to send next.","comment":"HL = the cursor in the buffer"},
        "13291": {"comment":"D = the read's state"},
        "13294": {"synopsis":"Continues a send in progress, or starts a new read."},
        "13295": {"comment":"Sending text?"},
        "13300": {"comment":"A status left from the last read?"},
        "13303": {"comment":"Given only once"},
        "13308": {"comment":"FLG_EDIT"},
        "13311": {"comment":"b0: sending once ENTER is pressed; b1: no LF yet"},
        "13315": {"comment":"The read's state"},
        "13319": {"comment":"NO PROMPT?"},
        "13323": {"comment":"Put a $1F mark at the cursor"},
        "13327": {"synopsis":"Walks the buffer from the cursor round to the $1F mark, clearing the prompt-line bits (3, 4)\nof every line's flag byte.","comment":"Walk the whole buffer round to the mark"},
        "13332": {"comment":"A line start ($03)?"},
        "13336": {"comment":"Clear b3-b4 of its flag byte, just before it"},
        "13340": {"synopsis":"Back at the mark? Else on to the next byte."},
        "13344": {"comment":"Take the mark away"},
        "13346": {"comment":"Flags of the cursor's line + b3, b4: the prompt line"},
        "13352": {"comment":"Store them in the line"},
        "13355": {"comment":"Remember the prompt's column"},
        "13361": {"synopsis":"SEND NOW set: sends at once; otherwise enters the edit loop."},
        "13362": {"comment":"SEND NOW: send without editing"},
        "13365": {"synopsis":"The edit loop: every key's action returns here. Keeps the NO PROMPT bit only while the\ncursor stays on the prompt's lines and not left of the prompt, shows the free-byte count,\nblinks the cursor while it waits and reads the next key.\nExit: back to the caller with $E5 (.STOP) when STOP was pressed, $D3 (.EKEY) on a keyboard\nerror, or the first character to send when ENTER or ESC was pressed.","comment":"Keep the cursor's address"},
        "13368": {"comment":"Video channel faulty?"},
        "13372": {"comment":"Error $D4 (.EVID)"},
        "13375": {"comment":"Cursor line marked as a prompt line?"},
        "13382": {"comment":"Not the prompt's first line: keep NO PROMPT"},
        "13386": {"comment":"Left of the prompt?"},
        "13394": {"synopsis":"The cursor has left the prompt: the whole paragraph will be sent.","comment":"Clear NO PROMPT in the read's state"},
        "13398": {"synopsis":"Shows the free-byte count and waits for a key, blinking the cursor.","comment":"Free bytes on the status line when below 100"},
        "13401": {"comment":"Blink pattern"},
        "13403": {"synopsis":"One step of the cursor blink: positions the cursor, turns it on or off by the pattern's top\nbit, then polls the keyboard channel."},
        "13405": {"comment":"Video cursor to the editor's cursor"},
        "13409": {"comment":"Next bit of the pattern: carry = off"},
        "13410": {"comment":"Cursor on or off"},
        "13413": {"comment":"FLAG_SOFT_IRQ: STOP pressed?"},
        "13418": {"comment":"Error $E5 (.STOP)"},
        "13421": {"comment":"Keyboard channel"},
        "13426": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "13428": {"comment":"C = 0: a key is waiting"},
        "13431": {"synopsis":"No key yet: counts the poll; after a run of polls the next blink step comes, with the ruler\nand the cursor line brought up to date."},
        "13432": {"comment":"Count of polls"},
        "13436": {"comment":"Ruler changed?"},
        "13439": {"comment":"Redraw the ruler"},
        "13442": {"comment":"Redraw what is left of the line"},
        "13447": {"synopsis":"A key is waiting: reads it from the keyboard channel.","comment":"Keyboard channel"},
        "13452": {"synopsis":"Status of the keyboard read: STOP goes back to the caller; any other error marks the\nkeyboard faulty and gives $D3 (.EKEY).","comment":"STOP: give $E5 (.STOP)"},
        "13455": {"comment":"Read fine?"},
        "13458": {"comment":"Keyboard faulty"},
        "13462": {"comment":"Error $D3 (.EKEY)"},
        "13465": {"synopsis":"A key read: AUTO ERA is used for the first key only, then the key's action runs and returns\nto the edit loop.","comment":"Clear the word-move state"},
        "13468": {"comment":"AUTO ERA? (Z = no)"},
        "13472": {"comment":"Only for the first key"},
        "13476": {"comment":"Keep the answer"},
        "13477": {"comment":"Actions return to the edit loop"},
        "13481": {"synopsis":"Runs a key: a printable character is stored, a control code or editing key ($A0-$FF) runs\nits action. The actions get A = the key's modifier (0 plain, 1 Shift, 2 Ctrl), B = the\ncursor column, E/D = the left/right margin and HL = the cursor in the buffer.","comment":"The key"},
        "13482": {"comment":"E = left margin, D = right margin"},
        "13486": {"comment":"B = cursor column"},
        "13489": {"comment":"Editing key $A0-$FF?"},
        "13493": {"comment":"Control code?"},
        "13498": {"comment":"AUTO ERA for this first key?"},
        "13499": {"comment":"Then clear to the end of the line first"},
        "13502": {"comment":"Store it at the cursor"},
        "13505": {"comment":"Show it on the video page"},
        "13508": {"comment":"Cursor one character on"},
        "13511": {"synopsis":"A control code from the keyboard: TAB moves to the next tab stop, ENTER sends, ESC goes back\nto the caller as it is; others are ignored.","comment":"TAB?"},
        "13515": {"comment":"Not back to the edit loop"},
        "13516": {"comment":"ENTER?"},
        "13521": {"comment":"ESC?"},
        "13523": {"comment":"D = 0: the read ends"},
        "13524": {"comment":"Give $1B to the caller"},
        "13527": {"comment":"Ignore it"},
        "13530": {"synopsis":"TAB ($09) is run as the editing key $AC.","comment":"TAB runs as key $AC"},
        "13532": {"synopsis":"Finds an editing key's action in EDT_KEY_TABLE. $A0-$BF: one entry per four codes (the low\ntwo bits are the modifier, left in A); $F0-$FF: one entry per code; $C0-$EF are ignored.","comment":"$A0-$BF? (A = $E0-$FF)"},
        "13536": {"comment":"$C0-$EF: no action"},
        "13539": {"comment":"$F0-$FF: A = $A0 + 4 * (code - $F0)"},
        "13543": {"synopsis":"Steps through the table two bytes per 4 added to A, until A passes 0; A is left as the\nmodifier.","comment":"Kept at $B276"},
        "13547": {"comment":"Table base - 2"},
        "13550": {"synopsis":"Steps to the next word until A carries past $FF."},
        "13552": {"comment":"Past zero yet?"},
        "13556": {"comment":"Read the action's address"},
        "13560": {"comment":"Swap it with HL on the stack: go there"},
        "13561": {"synopsis":"Action of the codes with nothing to do ($F7, $FF: Ctrl-F8, Alt-F8): returns."},
        "13562": {"synopsis":"Editing key actions, read by EDT_KEY_SEEK: 24 words. EDT_KEY_TABLE: $BC-$BF right; $34FC:\n$B8-$BB\nleft; $34FE: $B4-$B7 down; $3500: $B0-$B3 up; $3502: $AC-$AF (and TAB) tab; $3504: $A8-$AB\nINS; $3506: $A4-$A7 ERASE; $3508: $A0-$A3 DEL. Then $FF down to $F0 (the function keys with\nCtrl or Alt): $350A $FF none, $350C $FE paragraph colour, $350E $FD paragraph down, $3510\n$FC margins and tabs reset, $3512 $FB right margin, $3514 $FA ruler on/off, $3516 $F9 clear\ntabs, $3518 $F8 justify, $351A $F7 none, $351C $F6 line colour, $351E $F5 paragraph up,\n$3520 $F4 margins released, $3522 $F3 left margin, $3524 $F2 tab stop, $3526 $F1 centre,\n$3528 $F0 reformat."},
        "13610": {"synopsis":"ENTER: turns the cursor off and goes back to where the text to send starts: the paragraph's\nfirst line, the prompt's column on a prompt line (NO PROMPT), or the buffer's first\nparagraph (SEND ALL, with .EOF to follow). Then sending starts (EDT_SEND_NEXT).","comment":"Cursor off"},
        "13613": {"comment":"Start from the cursor's own line"},
        "13614": {"synopsis":"Goes back to the paragraph's first line; with SEND ALL on to the first paragraph of the\ntext.","comment":"Back to the paragraph's start (NZ: prompt line)"},
        "13617": {"comment":"D = the read's state"},
        "13622": {"comment":"SEND ALL?"},
        "13626": {"comment":"After the text: .EOF ($E4)"},
        "13630": {"comment":"Previous line a paragraph end? Go on back"},
        "13634": {"synopsis":"Not on the prompt line: NO PROMPT does not apply.","comment":"No NO PROMPT"},
        "13636": {"synopsis":"Reads the line's header, then with NO PROMPT moves the cursor to the prompt's column.","comment":"Read the line's margin and flags"},
        "13639": {"comment":"NO PROMPT?"},
        "13643": {"comment":"No step on the first pass"},
        "13644": {"synopsis":"Steps over the prompt, up to the remembered column."},
        "13647": {"comment":"End of the line?"},
        "13652": {"comment":"Reached the prompt's column?"},
        "13660": {"synopsis":"At the prompt: no margin spaces to send (count 1)."},
        "13661": {"comment":"Z still set"},
        "13663": {"synopsis":"Sets the count of margin spaces still to send ($B283, one more than the spaces).","comment":"Margin spaces + 1"},
        "13666": {"comment":"Return the character in B (NZ)"},
        "13668": {"synopsis":"Gives the next character of the text being sent: LF after a CR, the margin's spaces (unless\nNO SOFT), then the line's text with soft spaces as spaces (or left out with NO SOFT), then\nCR at the line's end. NO READ makes every character be thrown away instead.","comment":"LF due after a CR?"},
        "13672": {"comment":"LF"},
        "13676": {"comment":"NO SOFT?"},
        "13680": {"comment":"Margin spaces left?"},
        "13683": {"comment":"Send a space"},
        "13687": {"comment":"Keep the count at 1"},
        "13690": {"synopsis":"Sends the character at the cursor and steps over it.","comment":"End of the line?"},
        "13695": {"comment":"The character to send"},
        "13696": {"comment":"Step over it"},
        "13700": {"comment":"A soft space?"},
        "13704": {"comment":"NO SOFT: leave it out"},
        "13708": {"comment":"Else a plain space"},
        "13710": {"synopsis":"Gives B to the caller, or throws it away and goes on when NO READ is set."},
        "13711": {"comment":"NO READ?"},
        "13713": {"synopsis":"Throws the character away and gives the next one.","comment":"Next character instead"},
        "13716": {"comment":"Keep the read's state"},
        "13719": {"comment":"Return B, status 0"},
        "13722": {"synopsis":"At a line's end: $02 (end of text) adds an empty last line unless SEND ALL; $05 (soft end)\nsends CR LF only without NO SOFT; $04 (paragraph end) ends the send unless SEND ALL.","comment":"End of the text?"},
        "13727": {"comment":"SEND ALL?"},
        "13729": {"comment":"No: a new empty line for the cursor"},
        "13735": {"synopsis":"Steps to the next line, then sorts the line end out."},
        "13736": {"comment":"To the next line"},
        "13741": {"comment":"Soft line end?"},
        "13745": {"comment":"NO SOFT: no CR LF, go on"},
        "13751": {"synopsis":"A paragraph end: with SEND ALL the text goes on.","comment":"SEND ALL?"},
        "13755": {"synopsis":"The paragraph's last line: sending stops after its CR LF.","comment":"Sending ends"},
        "13757": {"synopsis":"Sends CR, with LF to follow.","comment":"LF next"},
        "13759": {"comment":"B = $0D, CR"},
        "13762": {"synopsis":"Line start without NO PROMPT: the margin's spaces are counted from the line's start column.","comment":"Column of the line's first character"},
        "13767": {"synopsis":"Joystick right (codes $BC-$BE): plain one column right (to the page's last column), Shift to\nthe line's end, Ctrl to the next word.","comment":"Plain?"},
        "13770": {"comment":"Ctrl?"},
        "13773": {"comment":"Shift: to the line's end"},
        "13776": {"synopsis":"One column left; at column 1 the cursor stays.","comment":"Column - 1"},
        "13780": {"synopsis":"One column right unless at the page's last column.","comment":"Last column of the page?"},
        "13785": {"synopsis":"Column + 1."},
        "13789": {"synopsis":"Ctrl-right: steps over the rest of the word and the gap after it; at a line's end goes to\nthe next line when nothing was passed.","comment":"Cursor to its column in the text"},
        "13792": {"comment":"Nothing passed yet"},
        "13794": {"synopsis":"Steps right until the start of the next word.","comment":"End of the line?"},
        "13800": {"comment":"Start of the next word?"},
        "13804": {"comment":"Step right"},
        "13809": {"synopsis":"At the line's end: to the next line if nothing was passed and it is not the last.","comment":"End of the text?"},
        "13812": {"comment":"Passed nothing: to the next line"},
        "13817": {"synopsis":"Joystick left (codes $B8-$BA): plain one column left, Shift to the line's start, Ctrl to the\nprevious word (on to the line above at a line's start).","comment":"Plain?"},
        "13820": {"comment":"Shift: to the line's first character"},
        "13824": {"comment":"Ctrl: cursor to its column in the text"},
        "13829": {"synopsis":"Steps left until the start of the word.","comment":"Step left"},
        "13833": {"comment":"Line start?"},
        "13838": {"comment":"Start of the word?"},
        "13843": {"synopsis":"Back onto the word's first character."},
        "13846": {"synopsis":"At the line's start: if nothing was passed and a line is above, the cursor goes to its end.","comment":"Passed something?"},
        "13849": {"comment":"First line?"},
        "13854": {"synopsis":"One line up and on to that line's end.","comment":"One line up"},
        "13857": {"comment":"To its end"},
        "13860": {"synopsis":"Joystick down (codes $B4-$B6): plain one line down, Shift a page down (to the page's bottom\nrow, or a page further when already there), Ctrl to the next paragraph's start. The column\nis kept.","comment":"Ctrl?"},
        "13865": {"comment":"One line"},
        "13867": {"comment":"Shift?"},
        "13870": {"comment":"Rows of the page"},
        "13875": {"comment":"Lines to the bottom row"},
        "13878": {"comment":"On the bottom row: a whole page less one"},
        "13881": {"synopsis":"Moves B lines down."},
        "13882": {"comment":"One line down"},
        "13888": {"synopsis":"Puts the cursor back in the column it had."},
        "13889": {"comment":"Same column as before"},
        "13893": {"synopsis":"Ctrl-down: to the end of the paragraph, then to the next line unless it was the last\nparagraph."},
        "13894": {"comment":"To the paragraph's last line"},
        "13897": {"comment":"Then the next line"},
        "13901": {"synopsis":"Joystick up (codes $B0-$B2): plain one line up, Shift a page up (to the top row, or a page\nfurther when already there), Ctrl to the paragraph's start (or the previous one's when\nalready there).","comment":"Ctrl?"},
        "13906": {"comment":"One line"},
        "13908": {"comment":"Shift?"},
        "13911": {"comment":"Cursor on the top row?"},
        "13917": {"comment":"Then a page less one"},
        "13921": {"synopsis":"B = the number of lines to move up."},
        "13922": {"synopsis":"Moves B lines up and keeps the column.","comment":"B lines up"},
        "13927": {"synopsis":"Ctrl-up: to the paragraph's first line; from a line's first character the line above is\ntaken as the start.","comment":"NZ: no padding"},
        "13928": {"comment":"Cursor to its column in the text"},
        "13931": {"comment":"Step left"},
        "13934": {"comment":"Was at the line's first character?"},
        "13937": {"comment":"Then from the line above"},
        "13940": {"comment":"To the paragraph's start"},
        "13943": {"synopsis":"INS (codes $A8-$AA): plain inserts a space, Shift breaks the line at the cursor with a\nparagraph end, Ctrl switches insert and overwrite mode.","comment":"Plain?"},
        "13946": {"synopsis":"Inserts a space at the cursor; the cursor stays on it.","comment":"Redraw from the cursor"},
        "13949": {"comment":"Insert a space"},
        "13954": {"synopsis":"Shift-INS or Ctrl-INS."},
        "13955": {"comment":"Ctrl: insert/overwrite"},
        "13958": {"comment":"Pad the line up to the cursor"},
        "13961": {"comment":"Back one character"},
        "13964": {"comment":"Break the line with a paragraph end"},
        "13969": {"comment":"Cursor back to the first part's end"},
        "13971": {"synopsis":"DEL (codes $A0-$A2): deletes to the right of the cursor. Plain one character (joining the\nnext line at a line's end), Shift to the end of the line, Ctrl the next word (also the line\nbreak).","comment":"E = the modifier"},
        "13972": {"comment":"Redraw from the cursor"},
        "13975": {"synopsis":"Deletes right of the cursor as the modifier in E asks (E = 1: to the line's end).","comment":"Pad the line up to the cursor"},
        "13978": {"synopsis":"Deletes characters until the line's end or the word's end.","comment":"End of the line?"},
        "13983": {"comment":"Ctrl: stop at the next word"},
        "13989": {"comment":"Delete the character at the cursor"},
        "13993": {"comment":"Plain: one only"},
        "13995": {"comment":"Something deleted"},
        "13999": {"synopsis":"At the line's end: nothing is joined past the text's end, by Shift-DEL, or after a Ctrl-DEL\nhas deleted characters; otherwise the line is joined with the next.","comment":"End of the text?"},
        "14002": {"comment":"Shift-DEL with nothing deleted: done"},
        "14004": {"comment":"Something deleted: done"},
        "14006": {"synopsis":"Joins the line with the next by deleting the line break. Returns unless D (popped into A) is\n0, when the joined line ran past the page: then the cursor goes to the line's end."},
        "14007": {"comment":"Delete the break and the next line's header"},
        "14010": {"comment":"A = D, F = E"},
        "14013": {"synopsis":"To the end of the line: from its first character forward to its end, but not past the page's\nlast column.","comment":"To the line's first character"},
        "14016": {"synopsis":"Steps right until the line's end or the page's last column.","comment":"End of the line?"},
        "14020": {"comment":"Page's last column?"},
        "14032": {"synopsis":"ERASE (codes $A4-$A6): deletes to the left of the cursor. Plain one character (joining the\nline above at a line's start), Shift to the start of the line, Ctrl the previous word.","comment":"B = the modifier"},
        "14033": {"comment":"Pad the line up to the cursor"},
        "14036": {"comment":"At the end: one character on"},
        "14040": {"synopsis":"Deletes left of the cursor until the line's start or the word's start.","comment":"Step left"},
        "14043": {"comment":"Line start?"},
        "14048": {"comment":"Redraw from the cursor"},
        "14051": {"comment":"Ctrl: stop at the word's start"},
        "14057": {"comment":"Delete the character"},
        "14060": {"comment":"Plain: one only"},
        "14061": {"comment":"Something deleted"},
        "14066": {"comment":"No step on"},
        "14068": {"synopsis":"At the line's start: on the first line, by Shift-ERASE or after a Ctrl-ERASE has deleted,\nnothing more happens; otherwise the line is joined to the end of the line above.","comment":"First line?"},
        "14072": {"comment":"Shift: stop at the line's start"},
        "14074": {"comment":"Something deleted: stop"},
        "14076": {"comment":"Up to the line above"},
        "14079": {"comment":"Redraw from the cursor"},
        "14082": {"comment":"No step on"},
        "14083": {"comment":"Columns left on the page"},
        "14090": {"synopsis":"Steps to the line's end to join it there; D becomes 0 when the line runs past the page.","comment":"End of the line?"},
        "14093": {"comment":"Yes: join the next line here"},
        "14100": {"comment":"Past the page: D = 0"},
        "14103": {"synopsis":"Alt-F3 ($FA): shows or hides the ruler on the page's top row; the page gives or takes back\none text row."},
        "14104": {"comment":"Ruler rows, 0 or 1"},
        "14108": {"comment":"Switch it"},
        "14111": {"comment":"Text rows of the page"},
        "14114": {"comment":"Hidden now?"},
        "14116": {"comment":"Shown: one text row less"},
        "14118": {"comment":"Cursor row - 1"},
        "14124": {"comment":"Was on the top row: stay"},
        "14128": {"synopsis":"Draws the ruler."},
        "14129": {"synopsis":"Shows the ruler line on the page."},
        "14132": {"synopsis":"The ruler is hidden: one text row more, and the page is redrawn.","comment":"One text row more"},
        "14134": {"comment":"Redraw the page"},
        "14137": {"synopsis":"Ctrl-F3 ($F2): sets a tab stop at the cursor's column, or clears the one there. Only between\nthe margins, where the ruler has '-' or a stop.","comment":"Ruler character at the column"},
        "14140": {"comment":"C = '|' (a stop), B = '-'"},
        "14144": {"comment":"No stop, between the margins?"},
        "14148": {"comment":"Then a stop ('|' with b7)"},
        "14150": {"synopsis":"Stores the new ruler character and redraws the ruler."},
        "14151": {"comment":"Into the ruler"},
        "14154": {"synopsis":"Alt-F5 ($FC): margins and tab stops back to their defaults. The two next instructions hide\nthe entries of Ctrl-F4 ($F3, $374F: ld e,b, left margin = cursor column) and Alt-F4 ($FB,\n$3751: ld d,b, right margin = cursor column); all go on to EDT_MARG_CHECK.","comment":"Left = right: forces the defaults"},
        "14155": {"comment":"Tab stops every 8 columns"},
        "14158": {"comment":"$374F (inside): ld e,b, Ctrl-F4's entry"},
        "14160": {"comment":"$3751 (inside): ld d,b, Alt-F4's entry"},
        "14164": {"synopsis":"EDITOR, special function 24 (@@MARG): sets the margins.\nEntry: D = right margin, E = left margin; $FF keeps that margin, 0 takes the cursor's column.\nThe specification gives the two values the other way round ($FF the cursor, 0 unchanged, DE\n= 0 to read the margins); the code does what is written here.\nExit: A = 0; D, E = the margins now. A left margin not below the right one, or a right\nmargin past the default, gives the defaults (1 and the page's width - 2).","comment":"B = cursor column"},
        "14167": {"comment":"L = left, H = right margin now"},
        "14170": {"comment":"Right $FF: keep it"},
        "14174": {"comment":"Right 0: the cursor's column"},
        "14177": {"synopsis":"Takes H as the right margin."},
        "14178": {"synopsis":"The left margin: $FF keeps it, 0 takes the cursor's column.","comment":"Left $FF: keep it"},
        "14182": {"comment":"Left 0: the cursor's column"},
        "14185": {"synopsis":"Takes L as the left margin."},
        "14186": {"synopsis":"Checks the margins and stores them, or the defaults.","comment":"Left below right?"},
        "14188": {"comment":"Default right margin"},
        "14193": {"comment":"Right margin past the default?"},
        "14196": {"synopsis":"Defaults: left margin 1, right margin the default.","comment":"Default right"},
        "14197": {"comment":"Left margin 1"},
        "14199": {"synopsis":"Stores the margins and asks for the ruler to be redrawn.","comment":"The margins"},
        "14203": {"comment":"Ruler to redraw"},
        "14208": {"synopsis":"TAB, every step: stops on a tab stop or the left margin's 'L', otherwise steps again.","comment":"Ruler character at the cursor's column"},
        "14214": {"comment":"A tab stop?"},
        "14217": {"comment":"The left margin?"},
        "14220": {"synopsis":"TAB (code $09 and keys $AC-$AE): moves to the next tab stop. In insert mode spaces are\ninserted; past the right margin the cursor goes to the next line (overwrite) or a new line\nis opened with a soft line end (insert, or on the last line).","comment":"Each step returns to EDT_TAB_AGAIN"},
        "14224": {"comment":"Past the right margin?"},
        "14231": {"comment":"Insert mode? (Z = yes)"},
        "14237": {"comment":"Insert: a space"},
        "14240": {"comment":"One column right"},
        "14243": {"synopsis":"Past the right margin: overwrite mode goes to the next line's start; on the last line or in\ninsert mode a new line follows."},
        "14245": {"comment":"To the line's end"},
        "14249": {"comment":"Last line?"},
        "14251": {"comment":"No: the next line"},
        "14255": {"synopsis":"Breaks the line with a soft line end ($05) and the cursor goes on the new line.","comment":"Insert: pad up to the cursor"},
        "14258": {"comment":"Back one character"},
        "14261": {"comment":"Break the line with a soft end"},
        "14266": {"synopsis":"Ctrl-F7 ($F6): the cursor line's colour (b0-b1 of its flag byte) goes to the next of four;\nwhen the video page will not take it, the one after.","comment":"Flags of the cursor's line"},
        "14269": {"synopsis":"Next colour (b0-b1 counting, b2 dropped)."},
        "14273": {"comment":"Set it as the video ink"},
        "14278": {"comment":"Refused? Try the next"},
        "14280": {"synopsis":"Stores B as the cursor line's flag byte (second header byte, and $B272) and redraws the\nline."},
        "14281": {"comment":"The line's first header byte"},
        "14284": {"comment":"Its flag byte"},
        "14288": {"comment":"Also the cursor line's flags"},
        "14292": {"comment":"Redraw the line"},
        "14295": {"synopsis":"Ctrl-F1 ($F0): reformats the paragraph (mode 2); falls into EDT_JUSTIFY.","comment":"Mode 2: reformat"},
        "14296": {"synopsis":"Alt-F1 ($F8) with mode 1, or reformat: from the paragraph's start every character is put\nthrough the word wrap again, soft spaces are taken out and lines with a soft end are joined;\nthe cursor ends on the next paragraph.","comment":"Mode 1: justify"},
        "14297": {"comment":"Kept at $B287"},
        "14300": {"comment":"To the paragraph's start"},
        "14303": {"comment":"Its first header byte"},
        "14307": {"comment":"Margin byte $81"},
        "14310": {"comment":"Read the header again"},
        "14313": {"comment":"Redraw the line"},
        "14316": {"synopsis":"Walks the paragraph's characters.","comment":"End of the line?"},
        "14321": {"comment":"A soft space?"},
        "14325": {"comment":"Take it out"},
        "14330": {"synopsis":"Wraps at the right margin if the character is past it, and steps on.","comment":"Wrap if past the margin"},
        "14333": {"comment":"Step right"},
        "14338": {"synopsis":"At a line's end: a soft end joins the next line and goes on; any other end goes to the next\nline and stops.","comment":"Soft end?"},
        "14340": {"comment":"No: next line, done"},
        "14343": {"comment":"Keep the redraw column"},
        "14347": {"comment":"Clear the redraw request"},
        "14350": {"comment":"Join the next line"},
        "14359": {"synopsis":"Ctrl-F2 ($F1): centres the cursor line between the margins: leading and trailing spaces go,\nthen half the room left is put before the text; the cursor ends at the line's start.","comment":"No NO PROMPT any more"},
        "14363": {"comment":"Keep the margins"},
        "14364": {"comment":"Line's margin byte: the left margin"},
        "14372": {"comment":"To the line's first character"},
        "14375": {"synopsis":"Takes out the leading spaces.","comment":"A space (soft or not)?"},
        "14382": {"comment":"Take it out"},
        "14387": {"synopsis":"Width between the margins, then goes to the line's end.","comment":"C = left, B = right margin"},
        "14391": {"comment":"B = width between them"},
        "14392": {"comment":"To the line's end"},
        "14395": {"synopsis":"Takes out the trailing spaces.","comment":"Step left"},
        "14398": {"comment":"A space (soft or not)?"},
        "14405": {"comment":"Take it out"},
        "14410": {"synopsis":"Steps back to the line's start, counting the text off the width.","comment":"Line start?"},
        "14415": {"comment":"Step left"},
        "14420": {"synopsis":"Half of the room left goes before the text.","comment":"Half of it"},
        "14423": {"synopsis":"Inserts the spaces before the text.","comment":"All in?"},
        "14426": {"comment":"Room for one more byte"},
        "14429": {"comment":"A space"},
        "14433": {"synopsis":"Cursor to the line's start; the line is redrawn."},
        "14439": {"synopsis":"Alt-F7 ($FE): the paragraph's lines all take the next colour (as Ctrl-F7 gives its first\nline).","comment":"To the paragraph's start"},
        "14442": {"comment":"Next colour for the first line"},
        "14445": {"comment":"NZ: stay on the first line"},
        "14446": {"synopsis":"Gives each further line of the paragraph the same flags."},
        "14447": {"comment":"Next line"},
        "14451": {"comment":"Same flags"},
        "14454": {"comment":"To the line's end"},
        "14458": {"comment":"Soft end: the paragraph goes on"},
        "14462": {"synopsis":"To the first line of the cursor's paragraph and its header.","comment":"Back to the paragraph's first line"},
        "14468": {"synopsis":"Ctrl-F6 ($F5): moves the paragraph starting at the cursor line one line up. The line above\nis copied after the paragraph's end and then deleted.","comment":"First line? Nothing to do"},
        "14472": {"comment":"Up to the line above"},
        "14475": {"comment":"Room for a copy of it, DE' = its size"},
        "14478": {"comment":"HL' = its first header byte"},
        "14484": {"comment":"To the paragraph's end (D counts lines)"},
        "14488": {"comment":"It now ends with a paragraph end"},
        "14491": {"comment":"Copy the line in after it"},
        "14495": {"comment":"Not the text's end?"},
        "14497": {"comment":"Keep the end of the text"},
        "14498": {"synopsis":"Back up to the line copied, deletes it and redraws.","comment":"Line count + 1"},
        "14502": {"comment":"Back up the paragraph's lines"},
        "14505": {"comment":"Delete the old line"},
        "14511": {"comment":"To the line's first character"},
        "14517": {"comment":"Redraw from that row"},
        "14520": {"synopsis":"Alt-F6 ($FD): moves the paragraph starting at the cursor line one line down. The line below\nit is copied before the paragraph and then deleted.","comment":"D counts the paragraph's lines"},
        "14522": {"comment":"To the paragraph's end"},
        "14526": {"comment":"Last paragraph? Nothing to do"},
        "14528": {"comment":"To the line below it"},
        "14531": {"comment":"Room for a copy of it, DE' = its size"},
        "14535": {"comment":"Was it the text's last line?"},
        "14540": {"comment":"It now ends with a paragraph end"},
        "14542": {"synopsis":"Goes back up to the paragraph's first line and copies the line in before it."},
        "14546": {"comment":"Back to before the line start"},
        "14553": {"comment":"HL' = after the cursor"},
        "14563": {"comment":"Up the paragraph's lines"},
        "14572": {"comment":"Copy the line in"},
        "14579": {"comment":"Up to it"},
        "14584": {"synopsis":"Down again, past the paragraph, to the old copy."},
        "14585": {"comment":"One line down"},
        "14591": {"comment":"Delete the old line"},
        "14594": {"comment":"Was the text's end?"},
        "14597": {"comment":"Keep the end of the text"},
        "14598": {"synopsis":"Back up to the paragraph and redraws."},
        "14605": {"synopsis":"Ends the move: back to the line start and up the paragraph's lines.","comment":"To the line's first character"},
        "14611": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor B lines up."},
        "14612": {"comment":"One line up"},
        "14619": {"synopsis":"Measures the cursor line and makes sure there is room for a copy of it: as many bytes are\nclaimed (an old line is deleted if the buffer is full) and freed again.\nExit: DE' = the line's size, header and end included; the cursor at the line's end.","comment":"Header and end bytes"},
        "14622": {"comment":"No step on the first pass"},
        "14623": {"synopsis":"Steps to the line's end, counting."},
        "14627": {"comment":"End of the line?"},
        "14633": {"comment":"End byte after the cursor"},
        "14636": {"synopsis":"Claims one $1F filler byte per byte of the line.","comment":"Room for one more byte"},
        "14639": {"comment":"Filler"},
        "14646": {"synopsis":"Frees the filler bytes again.","comment":"Free it, step back"},
        "14650": {"comment":"More filler?"},
        "14654": {"comment":"End byte back"},
        "14660": {"synopsis":"Copies DE' bytes from HL' (the alternate set, wrapping round the buffer) into the text at\nthe cursor.","comment":"Room for one more byte"},
        "14664": {"comment":"Byte of the source"},
        "14665": {"comment":"Next source byte"},
        "14668": {"comment":"Count it"},
        "14673": {"comment":"Into the text"},
        "14677": {"synopsis":"Deletes the cursor line: its text (as Shift-DEL) and the four bytes of its break.","comment":"To the line's end"},
        "14682": {"comment":"End byte and next header"},
        "14684": {"synopsis":"Frees one byte, stepping back."},
        "14690": {"synopsis":"Word test for the word moves and deletes: a word is a run of one kind of character (letters,\ndigits, ' and .; or the rest) and the run of the other kind after it.\nEntry: HL = the character; $B285 = the state, 0 at the first character.\nExit: NZ at the start of the next word, Z inside it.","comment":"Kind of the character"},
        "14694": {"comment":"First character?"},
        "14701": {"comment":"$83: started on a separator"},
        "14705": {"comment":"$81: started on a word character"},
        "14707": {"synopsis":"Stores the state for the first character."},
        "14710": {"synopsis":"Still inside the word: Z."},
        "14712": {"synopsis":"Compares the character's kind with the run's.","comment":"Started on a separator?"},
        "14717": {"synopsis":"In the first run carry means same kind, in the second a different kind.","comment":"Still in the first run?"},
        "14722": {"synopsis":"No change: inside the word; a change moves on to the next run."},
        "14724": {"comment":"Next run"},
        "14728": {"comment":"NZ when the second run has ended"},
        "14731": {"synopsis":"Kind of the character in A: carry clear for a letter, a digit, ' or '.', carry set for\nanything else.","comment":"Apostrophe"},
        "14734": {"comment":"Full stop"},
        "14737": {"comment":"Below '0'"},
        "14740": {"comment":"Digit?"},
        "14744": {"comment":"Below 'A'"},
        "14747": {"comment":"Capital?"},
        "14751": {"comment":"Below 'a'"},
        "14754": {"comment":"Small letter? Else above 'z'"},
        "14758": {"synopsis":"Stores the character B at the cursor: overwrites the one there, or inserts it (insert mode,\nor at the line's end); the line is padded with spaces up to the cursor first. Then the word\nwrap is checked (EDT_WRAP_CHECK).","comment":"Pad the line up to the cursor"},
        "14761": {"comment":"End of the line?"},
        "14766": {"comment":"Insert mode?"},
        "14772": {"comment":"Redraw from the cursor"},
        "14775": {"synopsis":"Inserts B before the cursor's character.","comment":"Pad the line up to the cursor"},
        "14778": {"comment":"Step left"},
        "14781": {"comment":"Room for one more byte"},
        "14784": {"synopsis":"Puts B at the cursor and clears the justify mode.","comment":"The character"},
        "14785": {"comment":"Justify mode off"},
        "14789": {"synopsis":"Word wrap: a character left of the left margin moves the line's margin; one past the right\nmargin makes the word it is in go to a new line (from EDT_WORD_BACK on).\nEntry: HL = the cursor."},
        "14790": {"comment":"C = left, B = right margin"},
        "14793": {"comment":"Left of the left margin?"},
        "14801": {"comment":"Line's margin byte moves left"},
        "14808": {"comment":"Line position = the margin"},
        "14812": {"comment":"Redraw the line"},
        "14815": {"synopsis":"Past the right margin? Then the word wraps.","comment":"C = left, B = right margin"},
        "14818": {"comment":"Past it?"},
        "14825": {"comment":"E counts the steps back"},
        "14828": {"synopsis":"Steps back to the right margin.","comment":"At the margin?"},
        "14832": {"comment":"Step left"},
        "14837": {"synopsis":"On a space (or soft space) at the margin no word is cut.","comment":"A space?"},
        "14842": {"comment":"A soft space?"},
        "14846": {"synopsis":"On a space: breaks the line there when the cursor moved back, else nothing to do.","comment":"Stepped back?"},
        "14851": {"synopsis":"Loop: moves the cursor left over the word that crosses the right margin (E and B count the\nsteps) until EDT_IS_SEP reports a character that is not part of a word.","comment":"One step left"},
        "14856": {"comment":"The character now under the cursor"},
        "14857": {"comment":"Letter, digit, ' or .?"},
        "14860": {"comment":"Still in the word: go on"},
        "14862": {"comment":"Back at the row's text start ($03)?"},
        "14866": {"synopsis":"Loop: the word fills the whole row and cannot move down; steps right again (B counts down)\nso that the break goes in at the margin.","comment":"Back at the margin?"},
        "14869": {"comment":"One step right"},
        "14875": {"synopsis":"A word boundary is found: justifies the row first (EDT_PAD_ROW) when bit 0 of $B287 asks for\nit.","comment":"Justify the row?"},
        "14882": {"synopsis":"Breaks the row at the cursor: EDT_NEW_ROW_E inserts end byte 5 (the row continues below) and\na new\nrow header; E (from $B287) goes along."},
        "14883": {"comment":"End byte 5: a wrapped row"},
        "14885": {"comment":"E = $B287 for EDT_NEW_ROW_E"},
        "14888": {"comment":"Open the next row here"},
        "14892": {"synopsis":"Loop: moves the cursor right again by the steps E counted, then goes back to EDT_WRAP_RIGHT\nto check\nthe new row against the margin.","comment":"All steps undone?"},
        "14893": {"comment":"Yes: check the new row too"},
        "14895": {"comment":"One step right"},
        "14900": {"synopsis":"Justifies the cursor's row by inserting padding spaces ($A0, a space with bit 7 set) after\nits words.\n1. Counts in D the steps back to the row's text start ($03).\n2. Walks the row forward word by word; after each word's following space inserts one $A0 and\n   counts B down.\n3. B at 0: steps back right to where it started and returns. Reaching the cursor's place\n   with B left over starts another pass from the row's start, unless the pass inserted\n   nothing.\nEntry: B = the number of padding spaces wanted; A = the character under the cursor (a space\nadds one).\nExit: the cursor where it was; BC, DE preserved."},
        "14902": {"comment":"E = $A0, the padding space"},
        "14904": {"comment":"Space or padding under the cursor?"},
        "14909": {"comment":"Then one more"},
        "14910": {"synopsis":"One pass over the row: saves the count, then goes back to the row's text start.","comment":"B kept to see if a pass inserts any"},
        "14911": {"comment":"D counts the steps back"},
        "14913": {"synopsis":"Loop: steps left, counting in D, until the $03 that starts the row's text."},
        "14918": {"comment":"The row's text start?"},
        "14922": {"synopsis":"Loop: steps right over spaces and padding."},
        "14927": {"synopsis":"Loop: steps right over a word up to the space after it."},
        "14932": {"comment":"One padding space less: done?"},
        "14935": {"comment":"Take a byte of the gap"},
        "14938": {"comment":"It holds $A0"},
        "14939": {"comment":"On to the next word"},
        "14941": {"synopsis":"Reached the cursor's place: drops EDT_JUST_STEP's return address, takes the B saved at\nEDT_JUST_PASS and\nstarts another pass unless nothing was inserted.","comment":"Drop the return into the pass"},
        "14942": {"comment":"A = B at the pass's start"},
        "14943": {"comment":"Nothing inserted this pass?"},
        "14946": {"comment":"Else go round again"},
        "14948": {"synopsis":"Loop: steps right D times, back to where the cursor started."},
        "14955": {"synopsis":"Restores DE and BC and returns."},
        "14958": {"synopsis":"One step of a pass: moves right and counts D down; at 0 (back at the cursor's place) it\njumps to EDT_JUST_ROW_END. Otherwise Z if the character now under the cursor is a space or\npadding."},
        "14961": {"comment":"Back at the cursor's place?"},
        "14965": {"comment":"Space and $A0 both give $A0"},
        "14967": {"comment":"Z: a space or padding"},
        "14969": {"synopsis":"Adds an empty row at the end of the text: steps left (so the end of text, $02, goes after\nthe cursor) and opens a row ending in 4, as Enter does.","comment":"Step left: $02 goes after the gap"},
        "14972": {"comment":"End byte 4: a hard line end"},
        "14978": {"synopsis":"Breaks the row at the cursor and opens a new one.\n1. Marks the row for redrawing from the buffer column + 1, inserts four bytes and makes them\n   the end byte (A) and the new row's header: the left margin + $80, the row's attribute\n   ($B272 without bit 4) and $03.\n2. In overwrite mode, with E = 0, when the old row went on in a wrapped row (the next end\n   byte is not 2 and not A - 1), the old break and the next row's header are deleted, so the\n   rest flows into that row and no screen row is opened.\n3. Otherwise counts one row more and scrolls the window's rows below the cursor down to open\n   a screen row; moves the cursor down to the new row and marks it for redrawing.\nEntry: A = the end byte: 4 (Enter) or 5 (a wrapped row); EDT_NEW_ROW_E takes E, nonzero to\nalways\nopen a screen row.","comment":"E = 0: may reuse the next row"},
        "14980": {"synopsis":"Entry with E given by the caller.","comment":"D = the end byte"},
        "14981": {"comment":"Redraw from the buffer column + 1"},
        "14988": {"synopsis":"Inserts the four bytes of a row break (D each), then fills them in.","comment":"Four bytes: end byte + 3-byte header"},
        "14990": {"synopsis":"Loop: takes a byte of the gap and stores D in it, four times."},
        "14997": {"comment":"Step left once: the last one after the gap"},
        "15000": {"comment":"C = the left margin"},
        "15003": {"comment":"Header byte 1: $80 + start column"},
        "15006": {"comment":"The cursor's columns = the margin"},
        "15010": {"comment":"Header byte 2"},
        "15013": {"comment":"The row's attribute"},
        "15016": {"comment":"Without bit 4"},
        "15019": {"comment":"Header byte 3"},
        "15022": {"comment":"$03: the row's text starts after it"},
        "15024": {"comment":"Right to the end of the new row's text"},
        "15027": {"comment":"Insert mode or E nonzero?"},
        "15031": {"comment":"Then open a screen row"},
        "15033": {"comment":"The end byte found"},
        "15034": {"comment":"End of the text?"},
        "15038": {"comment":"End byte = D - 1 (4 after a 5)?"},
        "15042": {"comment":"Delete the old end byte"},
        "15045": {"comment":"Buffer column - 1 - start column byte"},
        "15050": {"comment":"Normally negative: count 1"},
        "15053": {"synopsis":"Sets B, the count for the deleting loop at EDT_NR_SCAN."},
        "15055": {"comment":"Delete the next row's column byte"},
        "15058": {"comment":"And its attribute byte"},
        "15061": {"synopsis":"Loop: deletes the byte under the cursor (the $03 first), up to B bytes, stopping at a marker\nbyte."},
        "15065": {"comment":"A marker (below $1F)?"},
        "15071": {"synopsis":"Done deleting: goes on at EDT_NR_FINISH."},
        "15073": {"synopsis":"Opens a screen row below the cursor: one row more in the text, and the window's rows from\nthe cursor row + 1 to the last scroll down when that row is above the last.","comment":"One row more in the text"},
        "15076": {"synopsis":"Opens a screen row below the cursor (A = 1: the cursor row + 1): scrolls the window's rows\nfrom there down when it is above the last row, then moves to the next row."},
        "15078": {"synopsis":"Entry with A = the offset from the cursor row of the first screen row to scroll down.","comment":"B = the window's rows"},
        "15081": {"comment":"+ the cursor row"},
        "15086": {"comment":"Above the last row: ESC D, rows C-B"},
        "15089": {"synopsis":"Steps back over the new row's start, then moves down to the next row (EDT_ROW_DOWN_B with B\n= H,\nwhich never matches a marker) and marks it for redrawing from column 1.","comment":"Back over the row's $03"},
        "15092": {"comment":"One byte more without moving the columns"},
        "15095": {"comment":"B = H: skips EDT_ROW_DOWN_B's end-of-text test"},
        "15099": {"synopsis":"Marks the current row for redrawing from column 1 (EDT_DIRTY_FROM)."},
        "15104": {"synopsis":"Returns the margins in use: from $B26F/$B270, or from $B26D/$B26E (the full width set when\nthe channel opens) while $B271 is nonzero.\nExit: C = the left margin, B = the right margin."},
        "15108": {"comment":"Margins released?"},
        "15113": {"comment":"Then the full-width ones"},
        "15118": {"synopsis":"Brings the buffer position (HL, column $B275) to the cursor column ($B274).\nMoves right over the row's text, or left. Where the cursor is past the row's end, spaces are\nadded; where it is left of the row's start ($03), spaces are inserted and the row's start\ncolumn (its header byte, at $B259) goes down by one each.\nEntry EDT_SYNC_COL_A: with NZ in F' it adds nothing: the cursor column snaps to the buffer\nposition\ninstead.","comment":"Z in F': spaces may be added"},
        "15119": {"synopsis":"Entry with F' set by the caller: NZ adds no spaces."},
        "15120": {"synopsis":"Loop: compares the buffer column with the cursor column and steps one way.","comment":"Buffer column - cursor column"},
        "15126": {"comment":"Equal: done"},
        "15127": {"comment":"Buffer column right of the cursor"},
        "15129": {"comment":"The byte under HL"},
        "15130": {"comment":"A marker: the row's end?"},
        "15134": {"comment":"Padding allowed?"},
        "15138": {"comment":"Step back over the end byte"},
        "15141": {"comment":"Take a byte of the gap"},
        "15144": {"comment":"A space to pad the row"},
        "15146": {"synopsis":"Steps the buffer position right one byte and counts the buffer column up."},
        "15154": {"synopsis":"Steps the buffer position left one byte; at the row's text start ($03) inserts a space and\nmoves the row's start column left instead."},
        "15157": {"comment":"The row's text start?"},
        "15162": {"comment":"Padding allowed?"},
        "15166": {"comment":"Take a byte of the gap"},
        "15169": {"comment":"A space before the text"},
        "15172": {"comment":"The row's header byte 1"},
        "15175": {"comment":"Start column one less"},
        "15177": {"synopsis":"Counts the buffer column down and goes round again."},
        "15182": {"synopsis":"No padding: steps right again, back past the $03."},
        "15185": {"synopsis":"No padding: sets the cursor column to the buffer column."},
        "15191": {"synopsis":"Restores DE and BC after the buffer was made room in and tries the insertion again."},
        "15193": {"synopsis":"Takes one byte of the gap for an insertion: counts the free bytes down and steps HL onto the\ngap's first byte (Z, A = 0).\nWhen there is no gap (the buffer is full) it makes room by throwing text away, then tries\nagain:\n1. Steps forward to the end of the text ($02); the empty gap is moved there.\n2. If the window does not start at row 1 of the text, the first row of the text is deleted\n   (one row less before the cursor).\n3. Otherwise the last row of the text is deleted (scrolling the window when it shows it);\n   with a single row left, the last character before the $02.\n4. Sets the free count to the bytes freed, steps the cursor back to where it was and goes to\n   EDT_INS_RETRY.\nEntry: HL = the cursor.\nExit: HL on the new byte (still 0).","comment":"One free byte less"},
        "15196": {"comment":"Step onto the next byte"},
        "15200": {"comment":"Part of the gap? Done"},
        "15202": {"comment":"No gap: back to the cursor's byte"},
        "15207": {"comment":"The cursor, to come back to"},
        "15208": {"synopsis":"Loop: steps forward to the end of the text ($02)."},
        "15212": {"comment":"The end of the text?"},
        "15216": {"comment":"Keep its place"},
        "15217": {"comment":"The current row number"},
        "15220": {"comment":"- the cursor's screen row"},
        "15224": {"comment":"0: the window starts at row 1?"},
        "15226": {"comment":"No: delete the text's first row"},
        "15228": {"comment":"Rows in the text - cursor row"},
        "15233": {"comment":"A = the window's rows"},
        "15236": {"comment":"Rows below the cursor: delete the last"},
        "15238": {"comment":"Cursor on row 1?"},
        "15241": {"comment":"One row only: HL = the $02"},
        "15242": {"synopsis":"Loop: one row in the text and the cursor on it: makes the gap start here and steps back over\nthe marker bytes to the last character, which is deleted (one byte freed).","comment":"The gap ends here"},
        "15249": {"comment":"A marker?"},
        "15253": {"comment":"Delete the character"},
        "15257": {"comment":"One byte freed"},
        "15262": {"synopsis":"The text's first row is on the window's top row: scrolls the window's rows up (ESC U), moves\nthe cursor row up, and deletes the first row."},
        "15265": {"comment":"From row 1"},
        "15267": {"comment":"To row A"},
        "15271": {"comment":"The cursor's screen row one up"},
        "15274": {"synopsis":"Deletes the first row of the text: the bytes after the $02 up to and including its end byte\nare cleared (DE counts them) and the gap ends after them.","comment":"One row less before the cursor"},
        "15277": {"comment":"HL = the $02"},
        "15278": {"comment":"DE counts the bytes freed"},
        "15282": {"synopsis":"Loop: clears the next byte; goes on over the $03 and over characters and header bytes, stops\nafter the row's end byte."},
        "15287": {"comment":"Cleared"},
        "15289": {"comment":"The text start marker?"},
        "15293": {"comment":"A character or header byte?"},
        "15297": {"comment":"The new first row starts here"},
        "15300": {"comment":"The gap ends before it"},
        "15306": {"synopsis":"Deletes the last row of the text: scrolls the window up when it shows the end, then clears\nthe bytes back from the $02 over the row's text, its $03 and three more (header and the end\nbyte before it).","comment":"HL = the rows in the text again"},
        "15307": {"comment":"C = the window's rows"},
        "15309": {"comment":"Rows in the text <= the window's?"},
        "15314": {"comment":"Then scroll rows A-A up"},
        "15317": {"comment":"HL = the $02"},
        "15318": {"comment":"The gap ends there"},
        "15321": {"comment":"DE counts the bytes freed"},
        "15324": {"comment":"B = 4 header bytes, C = 0 to clear"},
        "15327": {"synopsis":"Loop: steps back and clears bytes up to the row's $03."},
        "15337": {"synopsis":"Loop: clears four more bytes back."},
        "15343": {"synopsis":"One row less in the text; the bytes cleared become the free count.","comment":"One row less in the text"},
        "15346": {"synopsis":"Sets the free count to DE and steps the cursor back to where it was.","comment":"Free bytes = those cleared"},
        "15350": {"comment":"DE = the cursor's old place"},
        "15351": {"synopsis":"Loop: steps the gap left until HL is back at the cursor's old place, then retries the\ninsertion.","comment":"Back at the old place?"},
        "15355": {"comment":"Yes: try again"},
        "15363": {"synopsis":"Goes up to the first row of the cursor's paragraph: redraws what is pending, goes back over\nthe row's start, reads a byte of the row's start into B and steps forward again; B = 5 (a\nrow that continues another) goes up a row (EDT_ROW_PREV) and round again. With bit 3 of\n$B282 set\nit stops early at a row whose attribute ($B272) has bit 4.\nExit: Z, unless stopped early (NZ).","comment":"Carry: skip the first move up"},
        "15368": {"synopsis":"Loop: up a row when NC, then checks the row reached."},
        "15371": {"comment":"Draw what is pending"},
        "15374": {"comment":"Back over the row's $03"},
        "15380": {"comment":"B = the byte there"},
        "15384": {"comment":"Stop on a marked row?"},
        "15390": {"comment":"Bit 4 of the row's attribute?"},
        "15395": {"synopsis":"Checks the byte read: 5 goes up again, anything else returns Z."},
        "15396": {"comment":"A wrapped row?"},
        "15400": {"comment":"Z: at the paragraph's first row"},
        "15402": {"synopsis":"Loop: counts in D the rows to the end of the cursor's paragraph: moves down a row (when Z)\nand to its end byte until that is not 5.\nExit: Z if the paragraph ends the text (end byte 2)."},
        "15403": {"comment":"Down a row"},
        "15406": {"comment":"To the row's end byte"},
        "15410": {"comment":"One row more"},
        "15412": {"comment":"Wrapped: the paragraph goes on"},
        "15416": {"comment":"Z: the end of the text"},
        "15419": {"synopsis":"Moves to the next row (NC, EDT_ROW_DOWN) or the previous one (carry, EDT_ROW_UP)."},
        "15421": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor up a row: redraws what is pending, goes back over the row's start; on row 1\nof the text it only re-reads the row's header (EDT_ROW_HEADER).","comment":"Draw what is pending"},
        "15424": {"synopsis":"Goes back over the row's start and checks for row 1 of the text."},
        "15427": {"comment":"Row 1 of the text?"},
        "15432": {"synopsis":"Goes back over the previous row's start and makes it current: one row number less, the\ncursor's screen row one up. On the window's top row the window's rows scroll down (ESC D)\nand the row is marked for redrawing."},
        "15435": {"comment":"Row number one less"},
        "15438": {"comment":"B = the window's rows"},
        "15441": {"comment":"Cursor screen row one up"},
        "15444": {"comment":"Still inside the window?"},
        "15446": {"comment":"Top row: redraw from column 1"},
        "15449": {"comment":"Scroll rows 1-B down"},
        "15456": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor down a row (B = 2: the end-of-text test is active).\nRedraws what is pending and moves to the row's end byte. At the end of the text ($02) an\nempty row is added first when the cursor is not on the window's last row. Otherwise the next\nrow becomes current: one row number more, and the cursor's screen row one down, or on the\nlast row the window's rows scroll up (ESC U) and the new row is marked for redrawing.","comment":"B = 2, the end of the text"},
        "15458": {"synopsis":"Entry with B = the byte that counts as the end of the text."},
        "15459": {"comment":"Draw what is pending"},
        "15463": {"comment":"To the row's end byte"},
        "15467": {"comment":"The end of the text?"},
        "15470": {"comment":"Cursor on the window's last row?"},
        "15476": {"comment":"No: add an empty row"},
        "15479": {"synopsis":"Goes back over the row's start (EDT_TO_ROW_START) and makes that row current again\n(EDT_ROW_ENTER).","comment":"Back over the row's start"},
        "15484": {"synopsis":"Steps into the next row: one row number more; on the window's last row the rows scroll up\ninstead of the cursor moving down.","comment":"Row number one more"},
        "15487": {"comment":"Step onto the next row's header"},
        "15490": {"comment":"The window's rows"},
        "15496": {"comment":"Cursor on the last row?"},
        "15499": {"comment":"A = 1"},
        "15501": {"comment":"Redraw from column 1"},
        "15504": {"comment":"Scroll rows 1-B up"},
        "15509": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor's screen row one down."},
        "15512": {"synopsis":"Makes the row whose header HL is on the current one ($B259), then reads its header.","comment":"The current row's header"},
        "15515": {"synopsis":"Reads the current row's header at HL: the start column (bit 7 off) becomes the cursor's\ncolumns, the attribute byte goes to $B272, and the cursor steps onto the row's first text\nbyte."},
        "15516": {"comment":"Start column without bit 7"},
        "15518": {"comment":"Both cursor columns = it"},
        "15521": {"synopsis":"Steps onto the header's attribute byte, keeps it in $B272 and steps past the $03."},
        "15524": {"comment":"The row's attribute byte"},
        "15528": {"synopsis":"Moves the gap right two bytes (the columns unchanged)."},
        "15533": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor right until the byte under it is a marker (below $1F): the row's end byte.\nEach byte read goes to $B276, so the video cursor is placed again.\nExit: A = the end byte, carry set."},
        "15534": {"comment":"Nonzero: the cursor must be placed again"},
        "15537": {"comment":"A marker?"},
        "15540": {"synopsis":"Steps right once, then on to the next marker (EDT_TO_ROW_END)."},
        "15545": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor left until it has stepped back over a $03 (the start of a row's text). Each\nbyte read goes to $B276."},
        "15549": {"comment":"The row's text start?"},
        "15551": {"synopsis":"Steps left once; with NZ in F (the caller's) it goes on as EDT_TO_ROW_START."},
        "15558": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor left one byte: both columns one less, then the gap moves left\n(EDT_GAP_LEFT).","comment":"Buffer column one less"},
        "15561": {"comment":"Cursor column one less"},
        "15564": {"synopsis":"Moves the gap left one byte: the byte at HL goes in front of the text after the gap ($B25B)\nand HL steps back.\nChanges: C.","comment":"The byte to move"},
        "15565": {"comment":"Its place joins the gap"},
        "15571": {"comment":"The first byte after the gap"},
        "15577": {"comment":"Now one place earlier"},
        "15578": {"comment":"The gap ends one byte earlier"},
        "15583": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor right one byte: both columns one more, then the gap moves right\n(EDT_GAP_RIGHT).","comment":"Buffer column one more"},
        "15586": {"comment":"Cursor column one more"},
        "15589": {"synopsis":"Moves the gap right one byte: the first byte after the gap ($B25B) moves to just after HL,\nand HL steps onto it.\nChanges: C."},
        "15590": {"comment":"The first byte after the gap"},
        "15594": {"comment":"Its place joins the gap"},
        "15599": {"comment":"The gap ends one byte later"},
        "15603": {"comment":"The gap's first byte"},
        "15606": {"comment":"Gets the byte moved"},
        "15608": {"synopsis":"Joins the cursor's row with the next one: deletes the four bytes of the break\n(EDT_CUT_BREAK), then\nscrolls the window's rows below the cursor up and draws the row that comes in at the bottom\n(EDT_SCROLL_UP_AT)."},
        "15611": {"synopsis":"Scrolls the window's rows below the cursor row up by one and draws the row that comes in at\nthe bottom (EDT_SCROLL_UP_AT).","comment":"From the cursor row + 1"},
        "15618": {"synopsis":"Deletes four bytes at the cursor (an end byte and the next row's header) and counts one row\nless in the text.","comment":"End byte + 3 header bytes"},
        "15620": {"synopsis":"Loop: deletes the byte under the cursor, four times."},
        "15625": {"comment":"One row less in the text"},
        "15628": {"synopsis":"Deletes the character under the cursor. Deleting a space next to a padding space ($A0) turns\nthat padding into a plain space, so the gap between the words stays."},
        "15629": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "15633": {"comment":"Look at the byte before it"},
        "15637": {"comment":"Padding?"},
        "15641": {"comment":"Make it a plain space"},
        "15643": {"comment":"Back onto the space"},
        "15648": {"synopsis":"Looks at the byte after the space: padding becomes a plain space."},
        "15651": {"comment":"Padding?"},
        "15656": {"comment":"Make it a plain space"},
        "15658": {"synopsis":"Steps back onto the space and deletes it."},
        "15661": {"synopsis":"Deletes the byte under the cursor: it joins the gap and the next byte moves onto HL."},
        "15666": {"synopsis":"Clears the byte at HL (one free byte more) and steps HL back (EDT_PREV_BYTE).","comment":"One free byte more"},
        "15669": {"comment":"It joins the gap"},
        "15671": {"synopsis":"Steps HL back one byte in the circular text buffer: from the start sentinel (a 1 at $B253's\naddress) it goes on at the end, before the sentinel at $B255's address.\nExit: A = the byte - 1 (Z at the sentinel, before the jump)."},
        "15673": {"comment":"The sentinel (1)?"},
        "15675": {"comment":"Go round to the end"},
        "15680": {"synopsis":"Steps HL forward one byte in the circular text buffer: from the end sentinel (a 1 at $B255's\naddress) it goes on after the start one ($B253's address)."},
        "15682": {"comment":"The sentinel (1)?"},
        "15684": {"comment":"Go round to the start"},
        "15689": {"synopsis":"Steps HL to the next byte of the text, jumping over the gap (to $B25B) when it reaches it.\nExit: A = the byte."},
        "15693": {"comment":"In the gap (0)?"},
        "15695": {"comment":"Then the first byte after the gap"},
        "15700": {"synopsis":"Counts the current row number ($B26B) up."},
        "15707": {"synopsis":"Counts the current row number ($B26B) down."},
        "15712": {"synopsis":"Stores BC as the current row number."},
        "15717": {"synopsis":"Counts the rows in the text ($B269) up."},
        "15724": {"synopsis":"Counts the rows in the text ($B269) down."},
        "15729": {"synopsis":"Stores BC as the rows in the text."},
        "15734": {"synopsis":"Counts the free bytes of the buffer ($B25D, the gap's size) up. Preserves HL."},
        "15741": {"synopsis":"Counts the free bytes of the buffer ($B25D) down. Preserves HL."},
        "15746": {"synopsis":"Stores HL as the free count."},
        "15751": {"synopsis":"Z if the current row is row 1 of the text.\nExit: DE = the row number - 1."},
        "15759": {"synopsis":"Points DE at column B's byte of the ruler (from $B255's address + 1, one byte per column).\nExit: DE = its address; A = the byte with bit 7 (the tab stop mark) off; C = the column, B =\n0; HL preserved."},
        "15760": {"comment":"The ruler's base"},
        "15766": {"comment":"+ the column"},
        "15767": {"comment":"HL back, the address to DE"},
        "15770": {"comment":"Without the tab stop mark"},
        "15773": {"synopsis":"Sets the cursor column ($B274) and the buffer column ($B275) to A, and $B276 nonzero (the\nvideo cursor must be placed again)."},
        "15776": {"synopsis":"Sets the cursor column and the buffer column to A only."},
        "15783": {"synopsis":"Sets up the ruler, one byte per window column after $B255's address: $7F (no tab stop), and\n$FC (bit 7, a tab stop) in columns 1, 9, 17 and so on. Preserves HL.","comment":"B = the window's columns"},
        "15786": {"comment":"A counts the columns from 0"},
        "15791": {"synopsis":"Loop: one ruler byte per column."},
        "15792": {"comment":"No tab stop"},
        "15794": {"comment":"Every eighth column"},
        "15798": {"comment":"A tab stop"},
        "15800": {"synopsis":"Next column."},
        "15805": {"synopsis":"Editor key handler (the word at $3516 of the key table at EDT_KEY_TABLE): clears every tab\nstop\nbetween the margins by building the ruler with E = '-' (no bit 7), and shows it."},
        "15806": {"comment":"'-' with no tab mark"},
        "15810": {"synopsis":"Editor key handler (the word at $3520 of the key table at EDT_KEY_TABLE): switches $B271\nbetween 0\nand '*': while it is '*', EDT_GET_MARGINS gives the full-width margins kept at $B26D. Falls\ninto EDT_RULER_TABS\nto show the ruler."},
        "15813": {"comment":"0 <-> '*'"},
        "15818": {"synopsis":"Builds the ruler text with the tab stops shown ($FC) and shows it when the window has a\nruler row."},
        "15819": {"comment":"E = $FC: tab stops are kept"},
        "15821": {"synopsis":"Rewrites the ruler bytes as the ruler's text, keeping bit 7 (a tab stop) where E has bit 7:\nspaces left of the left margin, 'L' at it, '-' (or $FC at a tab stop) between, 'R' at the\nright margin, spaces to the end (a 0 byte), and '*' in the last column while the margins are\nreleased ($B271). Then draws it (EDT_RULER_TOP).\nEntry: E = the inside character to keep ($FC keeps tab stops, '-' clears them); the main\nregisters swapped out (EXX)."},
        "15824": {"comment":"C = left, B = right margin"},
        "15828": {"synopsis":"Loop: spaces up to the left margin."},
        "15832": {"comment":"B counts on to the right margin"},
        "15836": {"comment":"'L' at the left margin"},
        "15841": {"synopsis":"Loop: between the margins: a byte equal to E stays, others become '-' (a tab stop shown as\n$FC)."},
        "15843": {"comment":"Already E?"},
        "15846": {"comment":"'-'"},
        "15851": {"synopsis":"Next column between the margins."},
        "15853": {"comment":"'R' at the right margin"},
        "15859": {"synopsis":"Loop: spaces from the right margin to the ruler's end (a 0 byte)."},
        "15863": {"comment":"The end of the ruler (0)?"},
        "15867": {"comment":"$B267 = 0"},
        "15870": {"comment":"Margins released?"},
        "15875": {"comment":"'*' in the last column"},
        "15877": {"synopsis":"Swaps the registers back and goes on to draw the ruler."},
        "15878": {"synopsis":"Draws the ruler on the window's top row when the window has a ruler row ($B268 nonzero):\ncursor off, home ($1E), then the ruler's bytes, one per column, in paper colour 1.\nExit: A = 0, Z (also when there is no ruler row).","comment":"A ruler row?"},
        "15884": {"comment":"The cursor must be placed again"},
        "15887": {"comment":"Cursor off"},
        "15890": {"comment":"$1E: home"},
        "15895": {"comment":"C = the window's columns"},
        "15898": {"comment":"DE = the ruler's first byte"},
        "15903": {"comment":"In paper colour 1"},
        "15911": {"synopsis":"Stores a space as this column's ruler byte (with bit 7, $A0, at a tab stop when E has bit\n7)."},
        "15913": {"synopsis":"Stores A as the ruler byte at HL; at a tab stop (bit 7 set) with E having bit 7 the byte\nkeeps bit 7 set, and '-' becomes $FC.","comment":"A tab stop here?"},
        "15917": {"comment":"Tab stops shown?"},
        "15921": {"comment":"Bit 7 on"},
        "15923": {"comment":"'-' marked?"},
        "15927": {"comment":"Then the tab stop sign"},
        "15929": {"synopsis":"Stores the byte."},
        "15931": {"synopsis":"Scrolls the window's rows from row C to the last up by one (ESC U) and draws the row of the\ntext that comes in on the last row.\nEntry: C = the first window row to move.\nExit: A = 0; HL preserved.","comment":"The window's rows"},
        "15935": {"comment":"Row C below the window?"},
        "15938": {"comment":"Scroll rows C-B up"},
        "15941": {"comment":"Draw what is pending"},
        "15944": {"comment":"A = the window's last row"},
        "15946": {"comment":"Rows from the cursor row to it"},
        "15951": {"synopsis":"Loop: steps HL back to the cursor row's $03."},
        "15959": {"synopsis":"Counts B rows down: at 0 the row is found."},
        "15964": {"synopsis":"Loop: steps forward through the text to the next $03; the end of the text ($02) means no row\ncomes in."},
        "15967": {"comment":"The end of the text?"},
        "15972": {"comment":"The next row's text start?"},
        "15978": {"synopsis":"The row is found: E = its attribute byte, HL on its column byte; draws it from column 1\n(EDT_DRAW_ROW_AT)."},
        "15981": {"comment":"E = the attribute byte"},
        "15985": {"comment":"From column 1"},
        "15989": {"synopsis":"Draws the part of the current row that is marked for redrawing ($B278 nonzero: its\ncomplement is the first column; $B279 the end) and clears the mark.\n1. Sets the paper colour from the attribute, turns the cursor off and places it at the first\n   column on the cursor's screen row.\n2. Spaces up to the row's start column, then finds the text byte for the column (skipping\n   the header) and writes runs of characters as blocks, following the text over the gap and\n   round the buffer's end.\n3. At the row's end byte clears the rest of the screen row ($19); a row longer than the\n   window gets '>' in paper colour 1 in the last column.\nPreserves HL. EDT_DRAW_ROW_AT draws a given row: HL on its column byte, C = the screen row,\nA = the\nfirst column, E = the attribute.","comment":"Anything to redraw?"},
        "15995": {"comment":"The current row's header"},
        "15998": {"comment":"C = the cursor's screen row"},
        "16001": {"comment":"E = the row's attribute"},
        "16004": {"comment":"The first column"},
        "16005": {"synopsis":"Draws a row from column A."},
        "16006": {"comment":"The cursor must be placed again"},
        "16012": {"comment":"Paper colour of the row"},
        "16016": {"comment":"Cursor off"},
        "16020": {"comment":"Cursor to row C, column B"},
        "16023": {"comment":"A = the first column"},
        "16027": {"comment":"- the row's start column"},
        "16029": {"comment":"At or right of the row's start"},
        "16031": {"synopsis":"Loop: writes spaces up to the row's start column."},
        "16032": {"comment":"A space"},
        "16042": {"synopsis":"Adds 3 to the count: the header bytes come before the text."},
        "16045": {"synopsis":"Loop: steps through the text to the column's byte."},
        "16050": {"comment":"B = the column"},
        "16051": {"synopsis":"Starts a run of characters at HL (DE = its start)."},
        "16053": {"comment":"C counts the run"},
        "16055": {"synopsis":"Loop: counts characters up to a marker, the window's last column or the end of the marked\npart."},
        "16058": {"comment":"A marker?"},
        "16062": {"comment":"The window's last column?"},
        "16071": {"comment":"The end of the marked part?"},
        "16076": {"synopsis":"Writes the run as a block, then looks at why it stopped: the gap (0) goes on after it, the\nend sentinel (1) goes on at the buffer's start, a row end clears the rest of the screen row."},
        "16078": {"comment":"Write the run"},
        "16083": {"comment":"Stopped by a column, not a marker"},
        "16085": {"comment":"The gap?"},
        "16088": {"comment":"Go on after it"},
        "16093": {"synopsis":"Not the gap: the end sentinel (1) goes on at the buffer's start.","comment":"The buffer's end sentinel?"},
        "16097": {"comment":"Go on at the buffer's start"},
        "16103": {"synopsis":"The row's end: clears the rest of the screen row ($19) when the run ended before the\nwindow's last column."},
        "16108": {"comment":"$19: clear to the end of the row"},
        "16113": {"comment":"H, never 0: to the exit"},
        "16114": {"synopsis":"The run stopped at a column: if the write went well, the window's last column gets '>' in\npaper colour 1 (the row goes on beyond the window)."},
        "16118": {"comment":"The window's last column"},
        "16121": {"comment":"Cursor there"},
        "16124": {"comment":"Paper colour 1"},
        "16126": {"comment":"'>'; EDT_VID_CHAR_COL sets the paper, writes it"},
        "16131": {"synopsis":"Restores HL and clears the redraw mark (EDT_SET_DIRTY with A = 0)."},
        "16135": {"synopsis":"Marks the current row for redrawing from the cursor column to the end, unless a mark from\nfurther left exists.","comment":"The cursor column"},
        "16138": {"synopsis":"Marks the current row for redrawing from column A to the end ($B278 = the complement of A,\n$B279 = $FF), unless a mark from further left exists.","comment":"Kept as its complement"},
        "16139": {"comment":"A mark further left already?"},
        "16143": {"synopsis":"Stores A as the redraw mark ($B278; 0 = none) with the end $FF ($B279)."},
        "16146": {"comment":"To the row's end"},
        "16151": {"synopsis":"Shows a typed character: if the cursor column is inside a pending redraw (marked from it or\nfurther left), the mark's end is moved past it. Otherwise, while a block is written ($B27A\nnonzero) the cursor column is marked; else the character is written at once (EDT_ECHO_NOW).\nEntry: B = the character.","comment":"D = the cursor column + 1"},
        "16156": {"comment":"Marked from this column or left?"},
        "16161": {"comment":"Writing a block?"},
        "16164": {"comment":"No: write the character now"},
        "16168": {"comment":"Mark from the cursor column"},
        "16174": {"comment":"With its end after it"},
        "16176": {"synopsis":"Inside a pending redraw: moves its end to D unless it is already past."},
        "16181": {"synopsis":"Stores D as the end of the redraw."},
        "16185": {"synopsis":"Places the video cursor at the editor's cursor (ESC =, the screen row $B273 and column\n$B274) when $B276 says it is out of place, and clears $B276. Preserves BC."},
        "16186": {"comment":"Out of place?"},
        "16194": {"comment":"C = the row, B = the column"},
        "16203": {"synopsis":"Sends ESC U (scroll up) for the window's rows C to B. The LD DE at $3F4D hides a second\nentry at $3F4E, LD A,'D': ESC D (scroll down) for the same rows. Both add the ruler's rows\n($B268) to B and C.\nEntry: C = the first row, B = the last row.","comment":"'U'; $3F4E (inside) is LD A,'D'"},
        "16205": {"comment":"Hides LD A,'D' at $3F4E: the scroll-down entry"},
        "16209": {"comment":"+ the ruler's rows"},
        "16216": {"synopsis":"Sends ESC = (place the cursor): C = the window row (the ruler's rows are added), B = the\ncolumn.","comment":"'='"},
        "16219": {"synopsis":"Adds the ruler's rows to C, then stores C + $20 and B + $20 as the two parameters and sends\nthe 4-byte sequence."},
        "16226": {"comment":"Parameters are sent + $20"},
        "16234": {"comment":"ESC, code and two parameters"},
        "16238": {"synopsis":"Turns the video cursor off (carry) or on (NC). The LD DE at $3F72 hides the entry $3F73, LD\nA,'o': cursor off, used by many callers. Nothing is sent when the code equals the last one\nsent ($B277).","comment":"Carry: off"},
        "16240": {"comment":"'O': cursor on"},
        "16242": {"comment":"$3F73 (inside) is LD A,'o'"},
        "16245": {"comment":"Sent already?"},
        "16249": {"synopsis":"Sends ESC with the code in A (2 bytes) and keeps the code in $B277."},
        "16256": {"synopsis":"Switches between insert and overwrite mode ($B286: nonzero in insert mode) and sets the\ncursor's character to match (ESC . with $1E in insert mode, $0E in overwrite mode)."},
        "16259": {"comment":"Insert <-> overwrite"},
        "16264": {"comment":"$0E: overwrite cursor"},
        "16268": {"comment":"$1E: insert cursor"},
        "16270": {"synopsis":"Sends ESC . with A: sets the cursor's character.","comment":"'.'"},
        "16272": {"synopsis":"Sends the 3-byte sequence ESC, B, A.\nEntry: B = the code, A = the parameter.","comment":"The parameter"},
        "16275": {"comment":"Three bytes"},
        "16278": {"synopsis":"Sends C bytes of the sequence at $B27D: ESC, then the code (A), then the parameters already\nstored at $B27F on.","comment":"The code after ESC"},
        "16283": {"comment":"ESC"},
        "16288": {"comment":"Not reached: no jump or table leads here"},
        "16291": {"synopsis":"Sets the paper colour to A (EDT_SET_PAPER), then writes C bytes from DE to the video channel\n(EDT_VID_BLOCK)."},
        "16294": {"synopsis":"Writes C bytes from DE to the editor's video channel ($B25F) with EXOS 8 (write block); C =\n0 writes nothing. A failed write sets bit 0 of $B27B.\nExit: A = the status (0, Z on success)."},
        "16296": {"comment":"C = 0: nothing to write"},
        "16298": {"comment":"The video channel"},
        "16303": {"synopsis":"Returns on success; else marks the video error (bit 0 of $B27B), which the channel's read\nand write calls report as error $D4 (.EVID)."},
        "16304": {"comment":"A video write failed"},
        "16309": {"synopsis":"Writes character B at the editor's cursor: places the video cursor, sets the row's paper\ncolour, writes it."},
        "16312": {"comment":"The row's paper colour"},
        "16315": {"synopsis":"Sets the paper colour to A, then writes character B (EDT_VID_CHAR)."},
        "16318": {"synopsis":"Writes character B to the editor's video channel ($B25F) with EXOS 7 (write character); a\nfailure sets bit 0 of $B27B.","comment":"The video channel"},
        "16325": {"synopsis":"Sets the paper colour to bits 0-1 of A, unless it is the one set last ($B27C): sends ESC P\nwith twice the colour and, if that worked, keeps the colour in $B27C.\nExit: A = the colour; BC, DE preserved.","comment":"Bits 0-1: the colour"},
        "16327": {"comment":"Set already?"},
        "16334": {"comment":"Paper = 2 x the colour"},
        "16335": {"comment":"'P'"},
        "16341": {"comment":"B = the colour"},
        "16344": {"comment":"The write failed?"},
        "16345": {"comment":"The colour now set"},
        "16349": {"synopsis":"Shows the editor buffer's free bytes ($B25D) on the status line as two characters at $BEDE\n(the status line starts at $BEB8, set at $12B5): two digits below 100, a leading zero as a\nspace; two spaces from 100 up."},
        "16350": {"comment":"The free bytes"},
        "16354": {"comment":"100 or more?"},
        "16358": {"comment":"Two spaces"},
        "16363": {"comment":"Below 100: the low byte"},
        "16366": {"synopsis":"Loop: one ten more in the tens digit (from space to '1', then up).","comment":"Space becomes '0'"},
        "16368": {"comment":"One ten more"},
        "16369": {"synopsis":"Loop: takes 10 off until it goes below 0; the remainder gives the units digit."},
        "16373": {"comment":"Back to 0-9, + '0'"},
        "16376": {"synopsis":"Stores the two characters in the status line.","comment":"Tens, then units"},
        "16381": {"synopsis":"Three bytes after the segment's last routine that no code reaches and no code reads after\nthe boot. The boot's check adds the 32K ROM's words ($0084-$0097) and wants 0; with these\nbytes the sum is 0."}
      }
    }
  },
